l=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except V5 Humanity means that you can have the Conviction of, &quot;Suffer not a Baby To Live.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the Chronicle Tenet of, &quot;Kill anyone who disrespects Kayne.&quot;<br /> <br /> Humanity isn't humane anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-27-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:11:04-07:00","id":1449833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449830#post1449830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Touchstones, oh and appearing human...</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I presume the Touchstone for baby murdering would be your Baby Eating Ghoul who helps you dispose of evidence. I mean, we're going full Baali here hypothetically.<br /> <br /> 2.I kind of like that you can be utterly HORRIFICALLY monstrous and look human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449831#post1449831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and then you've gotta stalk a swan who embodies those convictions, which is absurd. It's incredibly clunky, since it is clearly designed with relatively humane versions of humanity(I'm so sick of that word I'm ready to vomit just typing it) in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, V5 seems the most committed to making it clear that there's no such thing as a good vampire. Almost to the point of being problematic.<br /> <br /> And I tell all my players, &quot;Your characters have murdered at least one innocent person unless they were Embraced that night and you will kill someone in-game that way.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:26:22-07:00","id":1449839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449833#post1449833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, V5 seems the most committed to making it clear that there's no such thing as a good vampire. Almost to the point of being problematic.<br /> <br /> And I tell all my players, &quot;Your characters have murdered at least one innocent person unless they were Embraced that night and you will kill someone in-game that way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing &quot;bad&quot; isn't the same as playing &quot;spiritual in an alien manner&quot;. Playing &quot;bad&quot; still takes...I'm not typing that word out again I'm too sick of the sight of it...playing &quot;bad&quot; still takes the supremacy of THAT word as a given.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:29:16-07:00","id":1449841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449827#post1449827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> except, ya know, touchstones</div> </div> </div> </div>I remind you, Satanic fascist Evil Overlord Dracula had Renfield.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449839#post1449839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Playing &quot;bad&quot; isn't the same as playing &quot;spiritual in an alien manner&quot;. Playing &quot;bad&quot; still takes...I'm not typing that word out again I'm too sick of the sight of it...playing &quot;bad&quot; still takes the supremacy of THAT word as a given.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the &quot;alieness&quot; of Sabbat beliefs has often been greatly exaggerated. Plenty of the Paths are just RL religious and philosophical beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:37:25-07:00","id":1449843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449833#post1449833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. I presume the Touchstone for baby murdering would be your Baby Eating Ghoul who helps you dispose of evidence. I mean, we're going full Baali here hypothetically.<br /> <br /> 2.I kind of like that you can be utterly HORRIFICALLY monstrous and look human.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, V5 seems the most committed to making it clear that there's no such thing as a good vampire. Almost to the point of being problematic.<br /> <br /> And I tell all my players, &quot;Your characters have murdered at least one innocent person unless they were Embraced that night and you will kill someone in-game that way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) still places the source of your morality outside you. <br /> <br /> 2) I don't,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:46:16-07:00","id":1449846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449822#post1449822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it?<br /> <br /> I mean, that's the nature of supplements. They expand the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expand, not re-write the base nature of the world and replace it with a completely different world where everything is different. (Unless, of course, you're Star Trek and you're writing a Mirror Universe book). <br /> <br /> <b>Base Game:</b> &quot;Game is about The Office&quot;<br /> <b>That One Sourcebook:</b> &quot;All around The Office, countless Witchers rule the land...&quot;<br /> <br /> If you only read the base game, the world is largely dominated by Camarilla and contrasted by Anarchs. <br /> If, according to the sourcebook (not an expansion - a sourcebook), entire cities are dominated by blood cults instead of this world order, then yes - things are radically different.<br /> <br /> As for Humanity, arguing that Humanity can be a nonhuman sort of Humanity is kind of weird and feels like being served a salad and told to pretend that it's ice-cream. <br /> <br /> As I have informed my babysitter when I was a child - I know when what I'm eating isn't ice-cream.<br /> <br /> PS<br /> <br /> Why does everytime someone brings up Paths or non-Humanity, people go straight for the baby cannibalism? <br /> A lion has no Humanity - and yet, even though its eating habits are quite non-discriminatory, &quot;baby-eater&quot; probably wasn't the first thing that sprung to your mind when you thought &quot;lion&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:54:10-07:00","id":1449849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449846#post1449846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why does everytime someone brings up Paths or non-Humanity, people go straight for the baby cannibalism?<br /> A lion has no Humanity - and yet, even though its eating habits are quite non-discriminatory, &quot;baby-eater&quot; probably wasn't the first thing that sprung to your mind when you thought &quot;lion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because everything is framed from the human perspective. So talking to him about Paths is like trying to talk about atheism to someone who divides the world into Christianity and Satanism, and so any anti-Christian belief just MUST be inline with Satanism.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T12:00:45-07:00","id":1449851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449841#post1449841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remind you, Satanic fascist Evil Overlord Dracula had Renfield.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dracula doesn't give a shit about Renfield. Renfield is the archetypal VtM ghoul: a corrupt servant there to be a pawn.<br /> <br /> Nobody in the original novel serves as a Touchstone for Dracula. He doesn't give a shit about humans besides as food, pawns, or threats. Not even Mina. Later reworkings of Dracula turn Mina into a Touchstone, but they also turn her into the basis for Bella Swan in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T12:36:44-07:00","id":1449856,"title":"","content":"<i>None of my player hve the above verions of what you describe. Nor any players in teh two campaigns I play in.. and we are all players who have played for at least vampire for 20 years (apart from 1 who is new to the game in V5)</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":25995,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","user":"Ethryo","date":". 05-27-2021, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T12:50:38-07:00","id":1449859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449856#post1449856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of my player hve the above verions of what you describe. Nor any players in teh two campaigns I play in.. and we are all players who have played for at least vampire for 20 years (apart from 1 who is new to the game in V5)</div> </div> </div> </div>Good for you. I don't think that's how it's meant to be run. However, there's a lot of people who think they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T12:54:27-07:00","id":1449861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449859#post1449859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good for you. I don't think that's how it's meant to be run. However, there's a lot of people who think they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because that's how the core book portrays it, gaslighting, physical, emotional abuse, murdered for changing or for being to risky, to the extent that 'any storyteller worth their salt ' will use them that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T13:18:22-07:00","id":1449865,"title":"","content":"<b>Regarding the book not allowing you to play Sabbat</b>: There might not be character creation rules how to make a Sabbat Vampire tep by step. But as Justin and Martyna has said with little effort it will be poible to play Sabbat, although the storyline that the designers has made will advise you not to play Sabbat as V5's core is the strugle gainst the beast within and for that the Sabbat is no part of what they had as a thought.<br /> <br /> Just like that in FFG Star wars and WEG Star Wars there are no rules to play the Empire. You are supposed to play the Good /neutral side.<br /> <br /> <b>Regarding the Cover Art</b>: Lookig at both lips, the image is distorted and can be the artist's thought of the Lasombra picture. Or maybe just Art to make her threatening, alien and to look cool.<br /> <br /> <b>Regarding the &quot;Everytime someone takes up PoE people goes straight to baby canabalism&quot;</b>: The book is not even out and there has been so many (or maybe the same voices on Discord, Twitter, Facebook etc who tries to promote the &quot;Long rod to hell&quot;, or what it is called. I mean, wait till August look at the book and then say what you think. Dont be pessimistic but give the book a chance to actually give a new perspective of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Regarding all changes in V5: </b>V1-V2 was rather much set into stone. VR changed it all with changing clans. Ravnos when from thieving gypsy (sorry for the word) tricksters, to a semi-cult of fleshed out fighters who fought a secret war against the Cathayan undead with a rich culture and exciting stories only to kill off almost all of them. Assamites became the Banu haquim whowere no longer jut bloodthirsty killers, but an enriched cultural clan who ot their own problem with an internal schism,<br /> <br /> V5 has changed things, yes... they have altered our perspective on almost all of the lore. I understand that not all like it, but it seems so black and white for a few here that tries to read every word in the books just to tur and twist them so that they do not like what they see, only to complain about it here.<br /> <br /> Peronally, I dont now if I love everything about v5, but I have played it since Alpha and we have played both Dark Ages and Modern and I am currently playing a 1990-2018 campaign set i Gary/Chicago and it works splendid. I have borrowed from revised to portray Sabbat and other antagonists and my players love it. I am hopeful for what the Sabbat book will bring. Am I sad about no definitive rules for Sabbat players, well yes. But I believe tat the lore is more important and the PoE and both will be in the book.<br /> <br /> Maybe they will add some Sabbat Player rules when they see what people want, maybe not, maybe it will be in an update of the Companion. Regardles, But one thing I think i now and that i the more complait without substance or just showing hatred and promoting a cut/paste PDF from vampire revised as &quot;I will use this instead and tries to promote it on the Twitch where they tell u about the Sabbat Book is maybenot the way to make frends and make them listen.<br /> <br /> I had a talk with Justin when I contacted him, And I told him my concerns and asked question about those things and he took time to answer them so I could see it from is POV and we chatted a little about it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T13:22:38-07:00","id":1449866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449859#post1449859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good for you. I don't think that's how it's meant to be run. However, there's a lot of people who think they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean we have a Ventrue (former Maffia Bodyguard) who feed only on nerds and his touchstone is a young RPG playing nerd who tries to go through highschool without getting bullied.<br /> Another one is a Tremere who still cares for her old Grandmother who lives in a retirement home and a Gangrel who has his girlfriend as his Touchstone. One is playing a gay who has his non-accepting father who hates gay and has turned away from his son as his touchstone or the Lasombra who has a 4 year old girl whom they used to (and still) babysit for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T13:54:51-07:00","id":1449870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449861#post1449861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because that's how the core book portrays it, gaslighting, physical, emotional abuse, murdered for changing or for being to risky, to the extent that 'any storyteller worth their salt ' will use them that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's like the book immediately assumed, &quot;Person you genuinely love&quot; would make your vampires less scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T15:40:12-07:00","id":1449879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449678#post1449678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they haven't lost them already, they won't be losing any new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 hasn't seen a dime from me because I was waiting to see what happened with this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T15:40:43-07:00","id":1449880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449865#post1449865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Regarding the book not allowing you to play Sabbat</b>: There might not be character creation rules how to make a Sabbat Vampire tep by step. But as Justin and Martyna has said with little effort it will be poible to play Sabbat, although the storyline that the designers has made will advise you not to play Sabbat as V5's core is the strugle gainst the beast within and for that the Sabbat is no part of what they had as a thought.<br /> <br /> Just like that in FFG Star wars and WEG Star Wars there are no rules to play the Empire. You are supposed to play the Good /neutral side.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has to be the most bizarre statement I have ever read of anyone who claims to have read a Vampire: The Masquerade book at any point.<br /> <br /> Are you claiming that you &quot;you are supposed to play the Good/Neutral side&quot; in all RPGs and games or just in Vampire?<br /> <br /> That is an extremely mind-boggling statement to make, and not only for Vampire where the game is supposed to be about shades of grey and <i>there are no more heroes</i> as part of the base characteristics of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It's extremely bizarre, what you just said.<br /> It completely ignores all previous editions, as the Sabbat being playable isn't some &quot;un-canon&quot; new notion \u2013 they've been playable since 1992.<br /> The very first guide to the Sabbat released back then was the <b>Players'</b> Handbook to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> As for Good vs Evil, originally Vampire was designed as a shades-of-grey game and the original 1<sup>st</sup> edition contained an essay where the Dotmeister talked about how the game was meant as an exploration of evil, with players playing as the monster.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla and the Anarchs are not &quot;the Good vampires&quot;, they are still fucking <i>vampires</i> and their entire society is a den of snakes.<br /> Intrigue and betrayals are core parts of vampire society and player characters (even fluffy bunny Anarchs) can absolutely be nasty, violent or treacherous individuals.<br /> <br /> In the Revised Edition's Guide to the Sabbat there is an entire chapter devoted to discussing the Sabbat's supposed &quot;evil&quot; and the appeal to players.<br /> There were entire essays across many Vampire: The Masquerade books devoted to quashing any notion of &quot;Camarilla = good, Sabbat = evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> Comparing Vampire with Star Wars is\u2026 Extremely wrong. In Vampire, you play monsters, not superheroes (or psionic space paladins).<br /> A closer comparison would be if Exalted suddenly turned around and removed Dragon-Blooded and Abyssals as playable characters, making them NPC antagonists only. <br /> <br /> Also, this entire statement is just confounding and smacks of 80s D&amp;D attitudes.<br /> <br /> You know what? I don't mind if you maintain that &quot;Sabbat = Evil&quot;.<br /> As consumers, we gamers have repeatedly demonstrated that people fucking <i>love</i> playing evil characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, let's step away from RPGs for just a second.<br /> <i>Dead by Daylight</i> is a very successful video game. It's not the biggest one out there, but it has many times the numbers of all Vampire video games and every Shadowrun video game combined and ever since its release DBD has only seen growth.<br /> It's a multiplayer survival-horror game where four survivors try to evade a monstrous killer tasked with preventing their escape.<br /> <br /> Here's the kicker: you can play <i>as the killer</i>.<br /> <br /> In fact, all the killers in the game are player-controlled. That was the selling point of the game: as a survivor you're not just trying to dupe some shoddy AI (&quot;NPC antagonist&quot;) \u2013 you're facing off against a human player behind the controls.<br /> That premise appealed to <i>a lot</i> of people and while there are many more survivor players than there are killers, there are nevertheless many killers and many people who <i>only</i> play killer.<br /> <br /> To date, DBD has done better than every single one of its competitors.<br /> <br /> As for the struggle against the Beast being central to the game \u2013 that theme was still central for the Sabbat in previous editions and I don't understand how suddenly Sabbat characters would have &quot;no place for that&quot;.<br /> In Revised Edition and V20, most Sabbat characters still maintained Humanity (albeit in low scores). Paths of Enlightenment were ways for vampires to contend with the Beast \u2013 but contend with the Beast is something that every vampire, Sabbat or otherwise, has to do on a nightly basis.<br /> <br /> I am not convinced by your logic, not at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T15:53:29-07:00","id":1449881,"title":"","content":"I still cannot believe that the developing team as so little ambition that they cannot for the life of them make a Sabbat handbook. The date is quite early for V5 release rates so I'd wager that it's mostly a Lore dump book like the Camarilla/Anarch ones.<br /> <br /> New rules will have to wait another release. Perhaps when the player handbook is actually released? The one that was supposed to offer variants rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T16:01:03-07:00","id":1449884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449879#post1449879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 hasn't seen a dime from me because I was waiting to see what happened with this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry it wasn't what you wanted. Sincerely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-27-2021, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T16:17:20-07:00","id":1449885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449884#post1449884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point, I think that kind of proves people have already made up their mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>You gotta lend me those rose-tinted glasses that give you this <i>supreme optimism</i> towards this book.<br /> <br /> They <b>stated</b>, very clearly, that the book will not let you create Sabbat characters and they will not be playable. Your insisting that there's still anything for us to see in that book, that we'll get tools to make characters anyhow and play Sabbat games anyway, is... Really standing in the face of evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> They said they won't give us any support, that the Sabbat is from now on meant only as antagonists and that if we want to play them in V5 we have to do so by <i>making up our own rules </i>and essentially going against everything they've said so far about the game's direction, the Sabbat's place in their world and their future plans.<br /> <br /> What more is there for us to see in this book? <br /> I'll be blunt: <i><b>I don't give a shit about a lore book for a faction with zero relevance to the game and one that will contain zero support for playable characters</b></i>. <br /> This is them telling us that we're not welcome in their new franchise, that if we want to play V5 we have to play Anarchs like they want us to. <br /> <br /> I'm glad that's fine for you - it's not for me.<br /> I'm a Sabbat player and I shouldn't be told that my sect of choice is only available if I bend over backwards, break some rules, houserule like crazy, homebrew and drag older edition material into the new one by myself. <br /> <br /> Let me be clear: if I'm &quot;free to just homebrew&quot;, what the fuck do I need the devs for? I can just homebrew myself an entire game from the ground up.<br /> I can write my own vampire game, using my own rules and my own lore and my own world. If homebrew is so great, why should I purchase the products being offered? I don't need to read someone else's guide for Chicago - I'll just make my own one.<br /> <br /> This is what I don't understand about this attitude - you do realize that if I can do THAT, I just don't <i>need</i> to buy into the product line at all?<br /> <br /> Here we are, literally <i>begging</i> the devs that we are willing consumers - willfully gullible saps who repeatedly and faithfully purchased the brand's products for just about 30 years now, and would be <i>delighted</i> to give them our money, and they respond with &quot;no thanks, just homebrew your own stuff if you want to play&quot;. <br /> <br /> ...................Uhmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm mmmmmmmmm............<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T16:23:48-07:00","id":1449887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449880#post1449880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Revised Edition and V20, most Sabbat characters still maintained Humanity (albeit in low scores).</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what Justin Achilli said in the interview earlier, that isn't so in this book. Whether or not the Sabbat struggle between the Beast and a superego of any kind and whether or not they have a &quot;humanity&quot; rating, they have no conflict with humanity because they're entirely dehumanised.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm curious to see if their commitment to the path and Sabbat ideals has deepened or diversified during their fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T16:37:07-07:00","id":1449888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449880#post1449880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paths of Enlightenment were ways for vampires to contend with the Beast \u2013 but contend with the Beast is something that every vampire, Sabbat or otherwise, has to do on a nightly basis.<br /> <br /> I am not convinced by your logic, not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, because &quot;The Beast&quot; is misnamed. That thing inside a vampire would happily jump face-first into a wood-chipper to sate its hunger or rage. That's nothing like, say, a wolf, which avoids suicidal situations and is loyal to its mate, cubs, and pack. Most Sabbat paths are trying to emulate that sort of tribalism in some form.<br /> <br /> Feral Heart is the most obvious, but Honorable Accord is also basically about being loyal to your own and indifferent to everyone else, just with different details. Even Power and the Inner Voice is often about increasing the strength of the tribe via competition, respect for successful leaders, and only replacing those leaders when you are a genuinely superior choice. The Sabbat are tribalists, and have encouraged Paths or variations on Paths that that support fighting the badly misnamed &quot;Beast&quot; with tribalism.<br /> <br /> You don't resist &quot;the Beast&quot; because you are human, you resist the &quot;Beast&quot; because not resisting it hurts your tribe. Not resisting the &quot;Beast&quot; causes behavior that would make the Feral Hearter hurt her pack. Not resisting the &quot;Beast&quot; causes behavior that would make the Honorable Accorder break his oaths of loyalty to the Archbishop. Not resisting the &quot;Beast&quot; causes behavior that would make the Power and the Inner Voiceer be unworthy of being called a wise leader destined to rise in the Sabbat. The Sabbat resist the &quot;Beast&quot; via variations on tribalism rather than humanity.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the &quot;Beast's&quot; behavior is so unbeastlike that I prefer to call it the Inner Demon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T16:53:41-07:00","id":1449890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449881#post1449881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still cannot believe that the developing team as so little ambition that they cannot for the life of them make a Sabbat handbook. The date is quite early for V5 release rates so I'd wager that it's mostly a Lore dump book like the Camarilla/Anarch ones.<br /> <br /> New rules will have to wait another release. Perhaps when the player handbook is actually released? The one that was supposed to offer variants rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are focusing more on what happened and how to use them in stories rather than the full detailing of fluff like those books had. It is not that they don't have the ambition to do it. The sabbat are explicitly against their artistic vision for the edition as playable entities so. No sabbat players book should be expected ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T17:19:22-07:00","id":1449892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449890#post1449890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are focusing more on what happened and how to use them in stories rather than the full detailing of fluff like those books had. It is not that they don't have the ambition to do it. The sabbat are explicitly against their artistic vision for the edition as playable entities so. No sabbat players book should be expected ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it wouldn't really be compatible with the focus of V5 and their goals for play. &quot;Playable Sabbat&quot; was a bit of a controversy back in early VtM, after all, and there's always been tension between the Paths of Enlightenment and the personal horror of the original game. They can sometimes act as an escape hatch from the core character story arc in a way that watered down the gothic tragedy of very early VtM. <br /> <br /> Of course, VtM expanded its scope as the WoD bloated out and arguably it's too late to &quot;go back to basics&quot; when people have grown accustomed to certain options being present. But VtM 20th is like, right there, if you want a big open vampire buffet. V5 wants to be more of a fancy restaurant meal with a selective menu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T17:28:25-07:00","id":1449893,"title":"","content":"It's more like you are sitting in a restaurant where you have been a patron for the last 20 years and then one morning the manager show you the door saying that he doesn't want you as a patron anymore, and invites you to get your food somewhere else.<br /> <br /> That said the real problem is not the manager. The problem is that some of the new patrons are annoyed because after I have eaten there I wrote a bad review on Tripadvisor and I said to my friends to avoid the restaurant, because it's not what it used to be. And instead of simply admitting that yeah, there are some problems since a lot of old patrons are disappointed and a big chunk of them has been ejected out of the restaurant without apparent reason, they push you, by saying that either you can't understand fine cousine, or by saying that you cannot still comply because yeah maybe the food is shit, sure, but the merchandising of the restaurant is going so great! So everybody win!<br /> Except for the old patrons obviously...ah...those poor sods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-27-2021, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T17:44:17-07:00","id":1449895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449893#post1449893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more like you are sitting in a restaurant where you have been a patron for the last 20 years and then one morning the manager show you the door saying that he doesn't want you as client, and please go get your food somewhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Justin Achilli isn't trying to bum you out, personally. As far as I know, at least. <br /> <br /> V5 isn't entitled to your purchase. But you're not entitled to a particular creative choice from them, either. There are benefits and drawbacks to any addition to the playable cast of a game that so significantly departs from the intended playstyle. They landed one way, you'd rather they went the other way, it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T18:23:48-07:00","id":1449898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449885#post1449885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You gotta lend me those rose-tinted glasses that give you this <i>supreme optimism</i> towards this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the simple fact is that making NPCs is the same rules as making PCs.<br /> <br /> But you're having a weird interpretation of my reaction because I'm saddened and upset by this revelation. I also think it's a bad business decision.<br /> <br /> My reaction as a huge V5 fan is this is a mistake and disappointment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T18:54:03-07:00","id":1449901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449890#post1449890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are focusing more on what happened and how to use them in stories rather than the full detailing of fluff like those books had. It is not that they don't have the ambition to do it. The sabbat are explicitly against their artistic vision for the edition as playable entities so. No sabbat players book should be expected ever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what I don't understand. From a business view, it makes no sense whatsoever.<br /> <br /> The restaurants metaphor is sound. It's like if mcdonald's discontinued chicken burgers. And instead of reinstating them even if only just some of them because of popular demand, you just tell your customers to go to KFC. How does that make any sense???<br /> <br /> Even CTPhilipps comes up with better PR than White Wolf by spinning it like this is the Sabbat book everyone waited all along. I still think that people at WW will clarify in the coming days that the real Sabbat book will come up later and this is just a quick cash out for an edition that hasn't seen much content delivered.<br /> I am no V5 lover, but there's no way the devs are that stupid, no?<br /> <br /> At least this is the least moronic outcome of this mess that I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-27-2021, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:00:05-07:00","id":1449902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449901#post1449901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is what I don't understand. From a business view, it makes no sense whatsoever.<br /> <br /> The restaurants metaphor is sound. It's like if mcdonald's discontinued chicken burgers. And instead of reinstating them because of popular demand, you just tell your customers to go to KFC. How does that make any sense???<br /> <br /> Even CTPhilipps comes up with better PR than White Wolf by spinning it like this is the Sabbat book everyone waited all along. I still think that people at WW will clarify that the real Sabbat book will come up later and this is just a quick cash out for an edition that hasn't seen much content delivered.<br /> <br /> At least this is the least moronic outcome of this mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm highly doubtful. If you go by this forum, well V5 is a trash fire that's waiting to crumble at any moment. It's assuming there is popular demand that outweighs the pull of keeping the game with a tighter focus on a theme (Maintaining your humanity) and that this in no way helps maintain the branding that they are going for. It does, and while there is a portion of the fan base that is upset about it, it is just that. A portion of the fan base, and of that portion, there are those that would never buy or purchase the newest edition even if they gave into those complaints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:18:12-07:00","id":1449903,"title":"","content":"I sometimes have the reputation on these forums as the V5 cheerleader. I may be overestimating my importance but I do feel that I sometimes am the guy taking the vanguard of defending it while singing its praises.<br /> <br /> Reviving Chicago does a lot for my good will as does the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> Still, I am a long-time Sabbat player and while I tend to play the Sabbat as a dysfunctional mess that is always on the verge of imploding, I do that with a kind of RED DEAD REDEMPTION 2 sort of feeling that while they're murderers, outlaws, lunatics, and psychopaths--they're also a weird sort of family that has their own internal logic.<br /> <br /> I love the occult, demonic, alien Call of Cthulhu Cult thing combined with the fact that they're also the most EXTREME version of the Anarchs. So devoted to the cause of freedom that they have arguably lost all real freedom. They're a tremendously fun bunch of vampires and they also don't get the central premise of V:TM lost in the process.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are playing the <u>Bad Guy</u>.&quot;<br /> <br /> V:TM has its share of Louis, Nick Knight, and Angel types. However, you're usually playing Lestat, The Lost Boys (David), or Dracula rather than the good guys. You are drinkers of blood and mobsters who seek power over mortals as well as USUALLY have the dubious honor of being less evil than the guy against you--for now.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are IMPORTANT to Vampire: The Masquerade because they represent &quot;but for the grace of Caine go I&quot; and in Camarilla and Anarch games were needed as a necessary third party to get them to work together under extreme circumstances. However, there's no reason not to let people play them.<br /> <br /> You're <u>already</u> a serial killer and gangster. One of the silliest ever things to happen in gaming was when TSR folded like a deck of cards to BADD and tried to remove references to demons and devils in their game (Baatezu! Ta'anari!). You know, despite the fact that they were still embodiments of evil living in the afterlives of gods. For Mystra's sake. I'm really hoping this is not something motivated by controversy and I have too much respect for White Wolf's creators to think it is.<br /> <br /> So I don't get it.<br /> <br /> I <u><b>love </b></u>V5 but the absence of the Sword of Caine has been a conspicuous from the main book onward. The Gehenna Crusade is something I wanted information on and updates for the Paths of Enlightenment. I'm hoping that this book will contain everything you need to make Sabbat PCs as well as NPCs but I still can't help but be confused by the decision to not provide a book with the assumption of Sabbat PCs. The barn door has been open for 25 years. Both the Camarilla and Anarchs in V5 have been portrayed as complete scumbags.<br /> <br /> <i>Why</i> no Sabbat PCs?<br /> <br /> I'd like to know.<br /> <br /> Humor Mode: I should note my current character is a Malkavian Anarch that's a member of the Church of Caine. One of my players pointed out, &quot;Why not just play a Sabbat member?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-27-2021, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:25:14-07:00","id":1449904,"title":"","content":"Personally as someone who started in V5, and has started recently playing older editions, I do have to say I am disappointed in how the book is turning out. While with a little work it might be possible to make Sabbat PCs, the confusion created by several sources making it clear Sabbat in V5 are meant to be exclusively antagonistic is sad to say the least. They're inhuman yes, and should be antagonists for many games. However, not making it a clear option to play as a Sabbat seems like a backrooms decision from the branding department or something. I'll still likely play V5, but I'll likely not get Sabbat, or I'll buy it when it is on sale or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449888#post1449888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, the &quot;Beast's&quot; behavior is so unbeastlike that I prefer to call it the Inner Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in Werewolf lore the &quot;Beast&quot; as the vampires call it IS the &quot;Beast of War&quot;, which is a force of senseless rage and aggression that also gives the Werewolves their rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Grammer, that's it really. 05-27-2021, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:27:46-07:00","id":1449905,"title":"","content":"It also feels like a repeat of Requiem, which wasn't that popular. Requiem also dumped all Paths, focused on the gradual loss of humanity, and it was really rather forgettable. Lots of people want to play cool vampires, not Wraith with a vampire skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:37:35-07:00","id":1449907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449865#post1449865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like that in FFG Star wars and WEG Star Wars there are no rules to play the Empire. You are supposed to play the Good /neutral side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on there, while true for FFG it is not for WEG. WEG did not have splats, it was a pure skill based system so there was not a mechanical connection between character and factions, the gameplay support for factions came with information of their structure and what they did at large and various sub structure and the Empire certainly had that in the Imperial Sourcebook as did other &quot;bad guys&quot; with books like Privates and Privateers, GG: Bounty Hunter, GG: Criminal Organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","name":"Palp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:38:33-07:00","id":1449908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449905#post1449905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It also feels like a repeat of Requiem, which wasn't that popular. Requiem also dumped all Paths, focused on the gradual loss of humanity, and it was really rather forgettable. Lots of people want to play cool vampires, not Wraith with a vampire skin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And here we have the prime example of why they said they dropped the Sabbat as playable. The complete and utter abandonment of humanity in pursuit of doing what you want. Why do I say this? Because if your goal is to play a vampire who wants to use their powers and kill people? You still can with the current system but it's counterweighted by the humanity system. You can have an absolute serial killer but they have some way of saying &quot;I am not a beast.&quot; and the sabbat in their current interpretation do not do that. They say &quot;I am a beast&quot; and that's the end of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:42:50-07:00","id":1449909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449905#post1449905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It also feels like a repeat of Requiem, which wasn't that popular. Requiem also dumped all Paths, focused on the gradual loss of humanity, and it was really rather forgettable. Lots of people want to play cool vampires, not Wraith with a vampire skin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is incorrect. If we are looking at a faction supplement for more monstrous vampires who do not need to worry much about humanity you have Belials Brood and their Chorozon ritual system. There was also various other systems that bypassed or mitigated humanity loss IIRC. Especially in Dance Macabre where there are entire alternative systems to Humanity and is where I think what became Touchstones originated in Vampire, but worked a bit differently there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":724,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","user":"Palp","date":". 05-27-2021, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","name":"Palp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T19:45:11-07:00","id":1449910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449908#post1449908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And here we have the prime example of why they said they dropped the Sabbat as playable. The complete and utter abandonment of humanity in pursuit of doing what you want. Why do I say this? Because if your goal is to play a vampire who wants to use their powers and kill people? You still can with the current system but it's counterweighted by the humanity system. You can have an absolute serial killer but they have some way of saying &quot;I am not a beast.&quot; and the sabbat in their current interpretation do not do that. They say &quot;I am a beast&quot; and that's the end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>......What???? You don't understand Paths at all if you think this. For example, in a game I'm currently in, I'm playing a Feral Hearter, and I use the entire Feral Heart description in roleplaying my character, not just the violent parts, While I have only the usual three official Convictions, I roleplay my character as if it had avoiding all ten sins as convictions, plus the Ethics descriptions. It provides a rich experience that's not just about going psycho nuts.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_the_Feral_Heart\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pa...he_Feral_Heart</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-27-2021, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T20:14:45-07:00","id":1449911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449905#post1449905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It also feels like a repeat of Requiem, which wasn't that popular. Requiem also dumped all Paths, focused on the gradual loss of humanity, and it was really rather forgettable. Lots of people want to play cool vampires, not Wraith with a vampire skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity also means something different in Requiem. In Requiem, it was more important you don't use inhuman powers than not eat babies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T20:43:58-07:00","id":1449915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449905#post1449905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It also feels like a repeat of Requiem, which wasn't that popular. Requiem also dumped all Paths, focused on the gradual loss of humanity, and it was really rather forgettable. Lots of people want to play cool vampires, not Wraith with a vampire skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire: The Requiem 2e and the rest of the Chronicles of Darkness are great games. <br /> There's no Sabbat in VtR, but between the Circle of the Crone, Ordo Dracul (Metmorphosists/Necronomists), the Lancea et Sanctum (Path of Caine/Cainite Heresy + Path of Night) and other features, there's enough <i>of</i> the Sabbat in that game - who needs Belial's Brood? VtR vampires (and in fact, all CofD supernaturals) are much more monstrous than VtM vampires just at base, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Like CTPhipps mentioned, Humanity in VtR isn't the same as it is in VtM - much like how CofD moved away from NWoD's original Morality trait and replaced it with Integrity. <br /> Humanity in VtR is a more Lovecraftian trait - a high Humanity vampire isn't necessarily a good person. It still measures how monstrous you are, but high ratings are no longer associate with words like &quot;saintly&quot; or &quot;kind&quot;.<br /> Simply put, Humanity in VtR measures your ability to relate to, and understand, humans. It's your ability to understand how humans think and act, to discern their emotional cues and your ability to engage in human social mores over mere survival. <br /> <br /> So, in VtR, a vampire with Humanity 10 is simply a vampire who is an expert in how humans think, feel and act and is confident in dealing with them - but the book clearly states that this is a similar expertise to that of <i>a method actor</i>, rather than the Bodhisatva of previous editions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T20:54:58-07:00","id":1449916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Palp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449909#post1449909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is incorrect. If we are looking at a faction supplement for more monstrous vampires who do not need to worry much about humanity you have Belials Brood and their Chorozon ritual system. There was also various other systems that bypassed or mitigated humanity loss IIRC. Especially in Dance Macabre where there are entire alternative systems to Humanity and is where I think what became Touchstones originated in Vampire, but worked a bit differently there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Belials Brood where still on Humanity tho, they were still just humans with fangs. They weren't transhuman flesh crafters more akin to SCPs Sarkicist Klavigars and Karcists than to the Son of Sam, or mystics starring over the Far Horizon and ripping power and knowledge from that void while becoming something as bizarre as a Mi-Go, who cares about this repeated baby eating slander it isn't and never was about being something so pettily, mundanely human as that, and never has been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-28-2021, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:00:13-07:00","id":1449922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449916#post1449916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Belials Brood where still on Humanity tho, they were still just humans with fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically yes, but not to keeping it, they where devoted to loosing it in a rather interesting way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","name":"Palp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:09:50-07:00","id":1449927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449915#post1449915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire: The Requiem 2e and the rest of the Chronicles of Darkness are great games.<br /> There's no Sabbat in VtR, but between the Circle of the Crone, Ordo Dracul (Metmorphosists/Necronomists), the Lancea et Sanctum (Path of Caine/Cainite Heresy + Path of Night) and other features, there's enough <i>of</i> the Sabbat in that game - who needs Belial's Brood? VtR vampires (and in fact, all CofD supernaturals) are much more monstrous than VtM vampires just at base, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Like CTPhipps mentioned, Humanity in VtR isn't the same as it is in VtM - much like how CofD moved away from NWoD's original Morality trait and replaced it with Integrity.<br /> Humanity in VtR is a more Lovecraftian trait - a high Humanity vampire isn't necessarily a good person. It still measures how monstrous you are, but high ratings are no longer associate with words like &quot;saintly&quot; or &quot;kind&quot;.<br /> Simply put, Humanity in VtR measures your ability to relate to, and understand, humans. It's your ability to understand how humans think and act, to discern their emotional cues and your ability to engage in human social mores over mere survival.<br /> <br /> So, in VtR, a vampire with Humanity 10 is simply a vampire who is an expert in how humans think, feel and act and is confident in dealing with them - but the book clearly states that this is a similar expertise to that of <i>a method actor</i>, rather than the Bodhisatva of previous editions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>None of those are Path followers. They're just assholes. You are still not getting that I enjoy playing these Paths fully, and not as an excuse to twirl my mustache.<br /> <br /> Read this: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_the_Feral_Heart\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pa...he_Feral_Heart</a><br /> <br /> Does it sound like just an excuse to mustache twirl?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:09:56-07:00","id":1449928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Palp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449922#post1449922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Technically yes, but not to keeping it, they where devoted to loosing it in a rather interesting way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the boring baby eaters when what I was after was the Flesh That Hates, or a Karcist of the Path of Metamorphosis, (Would be stunned if the writers of the Sarkic Cults SCPs weren't Tzimisce players, because they nail what is interesting about them, and some of it looks like doing Viscittitude as an alien disease in an actually interesting way...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-28-2021, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:12:55-07:00","id":1449929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449928#post1449928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the boring baby eaters when what I was after was the Flesh That Hates, or a Karcist of the Path of Metamorphosis, (Would be stunned if the writers of the Sarkic Cults SCPs weren't Tzimisce players, because they nail what is interesting about them)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that calling them baby eaters are a simplification and rather depends on the subfaction they follow. And I did not mean to say that they where the Sabbat, they are not. Merely that they are an alternative to playing a vampire that follows the path of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","name":"Palp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:19:02-07:00","id":1449931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449908#post1449908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And here we have the prime example of why they said they dropped the Sabbat as playable. The complete and utter abandonment of humanity in pursuit of doing what you want. Why do I say this? Because if your goal is to play a vampire who wants to use their powers and kill people? You still can with the current system but it's counterweighted by the humanity system. You can have an absolute serial killer but they have some way of saying &quot;I am not a beast.&quot; and the sabbat in their current interpretation do not do that. They say &quot;I am a beast&quot; and that's the end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. A Sabbat on the Path of Honorable Accord would say, &quot;I am not a beast, I am an honorable knight sworn to the Sword of Cain. I kill when my liege orders me to or when I must do so to protect my comrades.&quot; Likewise a Sabbat on any Path would say, &quot;I am not a beast, I am X&quot; because in all ways Paths of Enlightements are methods one follows to specifically stave off the Beast. Any vampire who says, &quot;I am a beast and will act like a beast&quot; will very quickly spiral down to being a wright, regardless of whether they're following a Path or following Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:28:26-07:00","id":1449935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449908#post1449908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And here we have the prime example of why they said they dropped the Sabbat as playable. The complete and utter abandonment of humanity in pursuit of doing what you want. Why do I say this? Because if your goal is to play a vampire who wants to use their powers and kill people? You still can with the current system but it's counterweighted by the humanity system. You can have an absolute serial killer but they have some way of saying &quot;I am not a beast.&quot; and the sabbat in their current interpretation do not do that. They say &quot;I am a beast&quot; and that's the end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way to miss what made paths interesting. Inhumane doesn't mean mindless beast,it is about staving off the beast while not pretending to be human, doing by sheer will and spiritual enlightenment what anarchs do through delusional denials of their nature, and trying, however imperfectly to put yourself in that head space, the motives, desires and actions of a transcendent, and honestly pretty alien mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:46:23-07:00","id":1449939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449927#post1449927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of those are Path followers. They're just assholes. You are still not getting that I enjoy playing these Paths fully, and not as an excuse to twirl my mustache.<br /> <br /> Read this: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_the_Feral_Heart\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pa...he_Feral_Heart</a><br /> <br /> Does it sound like just an excuse to mustache twirl?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, twirling your mustache can be quite fun!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T22:03:44-07:00","id":1449942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449939#post1449939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, twirling your mustache can be quite fun!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and is what the Cam is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T01:29:56-07:00","id":1449955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449880#post1449880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has to be the most bizarre statement I have ever read of anyone who claims to have read a Vampire: The Masquerade book at any point.<br /> <br /> Are you claiming that you &quot;you are supposed to play the Good/Neutral side&quot; in all RPGs and games or just in Vampire?<br /> <br /> That is an extremely mind-boggling statement to make, and not only for Vampire where the game is supposed to be about shades of grey and <i>there are no more heroes</i> as part of the base characteristics of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It's extremely bizarre, what you just said.<br /> It completely ignores all previous editions, as the Sabbat being playable isn't some &quot;un-canon&quot; new notion \u2013 they've been playable since 1992.<br /> The very first guide to the Sabbat released back then was the <b>Players'</b> Handbook to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> As for Good vs Evil, originally Vampire was designed as a shades-of-grey game and the original 1<sup>st</sup> edition contained an essay where the Dotmeister talked about how the game was meant as an exploration of evil, with players playing as the monster.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla and the Anarchs are not &quot;the Good vampires&quot;, they are still fucking <i>vampires</i> and their entire society is a den of snakes.<br /> Intrigue and betrayals are core parts of vampire society and player characters (even fluffy bunny Anarchs) can absolutely be nasty, violent or treacherous individuals.<br /> <br /> In the Revised Edition's Guide to the Sabbat there is an entire chapter devoted to discussing the Sabbat's supposed &quot;evil&quot; and the appeal to players.<br /> There were entire essays across many Vampire: The Masquerade books devoted to quashing any notion of &quot;Camarilla = good, Sabbat = evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> Comparing Vampire with Star Wars is\u2026 Extremely wrong. In Vampire, you play monsters, not superheroes (or psionic space paladins).<br /> A closer comparison would be if Exalted suddenly turned around and removed Dragon-Blooded and Abyssals as playable characters, making them NPC antagonists only.<br /> <br /> Also, this entire statement is just confounding and smacks of 80s D&amp;D attitudes.<br /> <br /> You know what? I don't mind if you maintain that &quot;Sabbat = Evil&quot;.<br /> As consumers, we gamers have repeatedly demonstrated that people fucking <i>love</i> playing evil characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, let's step away from RPGs for just a second.<br /> <i>Dead by Daylight</i> is a very successful video game. It's not the biggest one out there, but it has many times the numbers of all Vampire video games and every Shadowrun video game combined and ever since its release DBD has only seen growth.<br /> It's a multiplayer survival-horror game where four survivors try to evade a monstrous killer tasked with preventing their escape.<br /> <br /> Here's the kicker: you can play <i>as the killer</i>.<br /> <br /> In fact, all the killers in the game are player-controlled. That was the selling point of the game: as a survivor you're not just trying to dupe some shoddy AI (&quot;NPC antagonist&quot;) \u2013 you're facing off against a human player behind the controls.<br /> That premise appealed to <i>a lot</i> of people and while there are many more survivor players than there are killers, there are nevertheless many killers and many people who <i>only</i> play killer.<br /> <br /> To date, DBD has done better than every single one of its competitors.<br /> <br /> As for the struggle against the Beast being central to the game \u2013 that theme was still central for the Sabbat in previous editions and I don't understand how suddenly Sabbat characters would have &quot;no place for that&quot;.<br /> In Revised Edition and V20, most Sabbat characters still maintained Humanity (albeit in low scores). Paths of Enlightenment were ways for vampires to contend with the Beast \u2013 but contend with the Beast is something that every vampire, Sabbat or otherwise, has to do on a nightly basis.<br /> <br /> I am not convinced by your logic, not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how I understood Justin's comments in teh Twitch stream.<br /> <br /> They do not want to have caracter creation rules for Sabbat vampires as they want to focus on the struggle against the beast and the personal horror which comes with that. The Sabbat vampires do not have a struggle against the beast they relish in it and lets it roam and they willingly roam with it, whereas a non-camarilla struggles against it and tries to control it.<br /> <br /> I am well aware that there is no good/evil side and that it is all shades of gray in vampire. My reference to the Star wars games was that both these companies made so much effort for you to play rebels, and neutrals and did all they could to deny their fans to play an Empire-sided campaign - Just as Paradox tries to limit us from playing Sabbat in thi book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T02:02:24-07:00","id":1449957,"title":"","content":"honestly i don't think the issue is that sabbath aren't &quot;playable&quot; so much as it is that the current humanity system is way to restrictive (and kinda shit) and ppl were banking on the devs to use paths to expand the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T03:28:07-07:00","id":1449960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449683#post1449683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, how many of you play material in a &amp;quot;Rules as Written&amp;quot; kind of way? Speaking myself I always alter everything in an RPG book to suit myself. My standard is a book should be mostly useful and require little hand waving on my part - but I go in assuming I will change things to suit me. All that to say while I am (somewhat) disappointed by a lack of direct PC options in the book, I can handle it and make it work for me. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer games to be RAW, for the simple reason that tweaking one small thing can cause problems elsewhere that then also need to be patched.<br /> <br /> Warhammer 4e is a good example of this. Lots of people immediately started house-ruling it, and then created a domino effect where they had to implement more and more house-rules. We certainly noticed that. Once we went back to RAW, it flowed much better.<br /> <br /> That said, if you know the game inside and out, house-ruling is much easier. I am very familiar with V20 now, so that's easy enough to hack. Hacking something like V5 would be harder as there are more interdependent mechanisms, so changing one affects several others (e.g., consider the way BP, Generation, Hunger, Compulsions and Frenzy are all interwoven).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T04:05:07-07:00","id":1449962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449955#post1449955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do not want to have caracter creation rules for Sabbat vampires as they want to focus on the struggle against the beast and the personal horror which comes with that. The Sabbat vampires do not have a struggle against the beast they relish in it and lets it roam and they willingly roam with it, whereas a non-camarilla struggles against it and tries to control it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems really strange. In previous editions, the Sabbat still struggled again the Beast. Paths of Enlightenment were just a tool they used. If they let the Beast roam free though, they'd eventually fall into wassail, and that would be it for them no different than a vampire on Humanity. If the 5th edition Sabbat are all basically wright's or on the verge of wassail, that's a significant change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T04:33:10-07:00","id":1449964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449962#post1449962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems really strange. In previous editions, the Sabbat still struggled again the Beast. Paths of Enlightenment were just a tool they used. If they let the Beast roam free though, they'd eventually fall into wassail, and that would be it for them no different than a vampire on Humanity. If the 5th edition Sabbat are all basically wright's or on the verge of wassail, that's a significant change.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are slash and burning the previous lore and setting to make room for their vision, past lore, settings etc aren't a working guide to what is happening now, from what was being said yesterday the Sabbat are predatory drones now, communicating in clicks, hisses and gestures, in mono Path packs, more than in words. We probably should have seen this coming, with the utter devastation of the Camarilla to make room for the Anarchs, and the transformation of the Tzim into Dracula wannabes, when before he had always been hated by that clan, as well as what happened to the Giovanni and Settites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-28-2021, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T06:38:16-07:00","id":1449972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449931#post1449931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really. A Sabbat on the Path of Honorable Accord would say, &quot;I am not a beast, I am an honorable knight sworn to the Sword of Cain. I kill when my liege orders me to or when I must do so to protect my comrades.&quot; Likewise a Sabbat on any Path would say, &quot;I am not a beast, I am X&quot; because in all ways Paths of Enlightements are methods one follows to specifically stave off the Beast. Any vampire who says, &quot;I am a beast and will act like a beast&quot; will very quickly spiral down to being a wright, regardless of whether they're following a Path or following Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Feral Hearter might say &quot;I am a beast and will act like a beast&quot;, but only because they think of the force usually called &quot;the beast&quot; as something infernal like &quot;the inner demon&quot; or &quot;the inner maniac&quot;. Semantics aside, the spirit of your point still stands: Sabbat have no more desire to become wights than anyone else. They just aren't interested in staving it off by holding on to their former species. They seek a third option.<br /> <br /> Really, the way Achilli and Outstar talk about &quot;The Beast&quot; now implies they consider it to mean anything conventional morality would consider &quot;evil&quot;. While technically the Tenet system could be used for anything, the examples examples in the book are all mild examples of genre variations on conventional morality. In their minds, you can be the protagonist in a Hallmark Romance novel, or the protagonist in something like &quot;Sin City&quot;, but that's the range limit, and anything past that is giving in to the beast. As different as a Hallmark Romance novel and &quot;Sin City&quot; are, that range is really very conventionally human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-28-2021, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T07:13:47-07:00","id":1449973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449964#post1449964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">from what was being said yesterday the Sabbat are predatory drones now, communicating in clicks, hisses and gestures, in mono Path packs, more than in words.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here is where I punch out on adapting V5 metaplot to my V20 campaigns.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s nothing interesting to explore with this change. It\u2019s replacing an entire faction with wights. If you want packs of wights running around in your campaign just put a pack of wights into your campaign. There\u2019s no need to destroy an entire faction with interesting philosophies and counterpoints to Camarilla just to have more Wights in V5.<br /> <br /> Also, so much for the \u201cyou build NPCs just like PCs so clearly the rules will be easy to adapt\u201d nonsense. These rules aren\u2019t gonna be NPC creation rules, they\u2019re going to be monster manual entries.<br /> <br /> What a fustercluck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T07:14:01-07:00","id":1449974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449902#post1449902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm highly doubtful. If you go by this forum, well V5 is a trash fire that's waiting to crumble at any moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. The people producing the books base a lot of their work on a different set of numbers and results than the opinions expressed here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T07:42:16-07:00","id":1449975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449974#post1449974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. The people producing the books base a lot of their work on a different set of numbers and results than the opinions expressed here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given that they had to change development team 3 times in 4 years I'd say those numbers are not that different from the opinions expressed here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T07:58:23-07:00","id":1449976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449903#post1449903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the occult, demonic, alien Call of Cthulhu Cult thing combined with the fact that they're also the most EXTREME version of the Anarchs. So devoted to the cause of freedom that they have arguably lost all real freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I feel is often lost in the discussions of the Sabbat - even in Achilli's talk with Outstar. That is, PC members of the Sabbat are still under the control of elders who don't give a damn about them, and those elders are controlled by Ancients who do not care about them in turn. In following Paths thoroughly, members give up even what agency the members of the Camarilla possess. So yes, in many ways members of the Sabbat are less free than are members of the Camarilla. Add to this situation that vampires that no longer use language to communicate but do so though body language and clicking sounds have devolved from the human. That is how herd and pack animals communicate, not how sentient creatures communicate. The Sabbat are devolved and unfree creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T07:59:12-07:00","id":1449977,"title":"","content":"I feel as a thallain swimming in evil glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T08:24:28-07:00","id":1449983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449976#post1449976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something I feel is often lost in the discussions of the Sabbat - even in Achilli's talk with Outstar. That is, PC members of the Sabbat are still under the control of elders who don't give a damn about them, and those elders are controlled by Ancients who do not care about them in turn. In following Paths thoroughly, members give up even what agency the members of the Camarilla possess. So yes, in many ways members of the Sabbat are less free than are members of the Camarilla. Add to this situation that vampires that no longer use language to communicate but do so though body language and clicking sounds have devolved from the human. That is how herd and pack animals communicate, not how sentient creatures communicate. The Sabbat are devolved and unfree creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are several hunter/gatherer tribes in the real world who would take offense at the idea that a clicking language is subhuman. And body language is important in all communication. The loss of body language and tone in online discussion is part of the reason there are so often misunderstandings and trollings. In any case this special language stuff is a new thing that wasn't part of Paths for 30 years.<br /> <br /> Whether following a Path makes you less free than someone on &quot;humanity&quot; is a complicated question. I do find myself often referring back to the Feral Heart sheet when roleplaying my main character, and devoting myself to making my character a Path Paragon does limit my choices significantly. But I don't see how it is anymore limiting than attempting to achieve Humanity 10 would be.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T08:43:12-07:00","id":1449986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449975#post1449975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given that they had to change development team 3 times in 4 years I'd say those numbers are not that different from the opinions expressed here.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Allow me to state that opinion is not true and against the policies of Onyx Path Publishing's forums. That you are posting here in. This is greatly against the forum rules and take an infraction.<br /> <br /> Do not speak for the developers, especially to trash 