attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T09:28:10-07:00","id":1449993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449990#post1449990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outstar's interview regarding the Sabbat w/ Justin Achilli.<br /> <br /> It's an hour long so I'll tell you more when I watch the whole thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/v_JiRakxa5M\" data-code=\"v_JiRakxa5M\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/v_JiRakxa5M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sabbat section starts at 22minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T09:48:00-07:00","id":1449996,"title":"","content":"TL;dr version<br /> <br /> * Talk a lot about how Humanity is the pillar of V5, and V5 being a 'return to basics' for Vampire.<br /> * Talk a lot about what the development thought process was and why doing this as an antagonist book.<br /> * Book is written from the standpoint of using the Sabbat as SPC antagonists and talk about why<br /> * Book can be used for PCs if you want and all rules are there, but isn't written as a PC book<br /> -- Quote from the stream: Justin Achilli: \u201cI\u2019m sure there are players who are going to play Sabbat once they got the rule book. I have no doubt about it. Everything is there if you absolutely want to do it!\u201d<br /> * Talk about some Discipline powers, like one that lets you yank your vitae out of a ghoul from anywhere in the world, and one that leaves shovelheads as sleeping time bombs in a domain. Heavy talk about how the things that are done are Stain worthy, BUUUUUUT... <br /> * Talk about whole packs being on Paths, and concepts of Paths. Mechanics seem to just be 'the SPCs can ignore humanity and Stains entirely.'<br /> * Talk about Antitribu and 'things that distance you from your Antediluvian'.<br /> * Justin wants to have a preview document with art, a path example and some antitribu thoughts at the Elysium thing in June. No confirmation though as nothing is specifically nailed down for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 05-28-2021, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T09:55:30-07:00","id":1449998,"title":"","content":"I do really know what's going on and who's pushing for what. I mean, Can you imagine the meeting they had where they decided against playable sabbat? Is this a lead developer or a producer laying down the law, is it a team effort? What makes people decide on a move that's so obviously not what the fans want? Are we genuinely worried about a moral panic or something, or is it really a case of someone with a very specific vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T09:59:48-07:00","id":1450000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449996#post1449996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;dr version<br /> <br /> * Book can be used for PCs if you want and all rules are there, but isn't written as a PC book</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Ok then. <br /> Crisis averted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T10:06:33-07:00","id":1450001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449902#post1449902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm highly doubtful. If you go by this forum, well V5 is a trash fire that's waiting to crumble at any moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully the team at Paradox <i><b>probably</b></i> goes by sales numbers that they have visibility to, rather than a single forum that has a history of hostility to the new edition!<br /> <br /> The internet fandom does not define literally everyone who plays WoD, let alone one forum (which has had a lot of people who like V5 just stop because of the constant vitriol that comes out of this place, anyway) in that internet fandom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449998#post1449998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do really know what's going on and who's pushing for what. I mean, Can you imagine the meeting they had where they decided against playable sabbat? Is this a lead developer or a producer laying down the law, is it a team effort? What makes people decide on a move that's so obviously not what the fans want? Are we genuinely worried about a moral panic or something, or is it really a case of someone with a very specific vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, like all the other things in V5, it's not being solely marketed at old players. Which, if they're making good money from things being back in stores for everyone to purchase, that's going to hold up their business decisions. Also, the way some things were talked about in the stream too, like the mention of 'how this would be seen in games and TV shows' from Outstar is probably also a good indicator of a portion of Paradox's aims, from a business standpoint. They do have people working on a TV show right now, after all. Remember, they're not just 'writing an RPG'. They're also laying the backbone for something Paradox expects to make a lot more money on, and so things need to be written with a facing towards that as well.<br /> <br /> Does it really matter anyway at this point? It's been out and out stated that you can use the book to play PC Sabbat by Justin, all the rules and history will be there, it's just not going to tell you that stuff from a PC perspective. Which, based on a lot of comments throughout, the 'teaching you how to play a Sabbat' part of 'PC facing' really won't matter?<br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see if Paths are anything but a named handwave though, based on the description and outstars continued comments though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 05-28-2021, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T10:39:21-07:00","id":1450008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450001#post1450001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see if Paths are anything but a named handwave though, based on the description and outstars continued comments though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I get is that it won't be so much a handwave as a monster manual label for pack types. Want to tell a there-but-for-the-grace-of-god story about the players becoming too Ayn Randian business/politics ruthless? Plug in a Power/Inner Voice Pack antagonists. Want to tell a story about the players becoming too feral? Plug in a Feral Heart pack antagonists. Want to tell a story about the players becoming too ruthless in their enforcement of Camarilla rules? Plug in a Honorable Accord pack antagonists.<br /> <br /> That's why they keep talking about Paths in the context of entire Packs following them. In a Sabbat player game, different players will be on different paths and part of the fun is the internal conflict between pack members.<br /> <br /> In a Cammy game, the Sabbat are there to be the clearly themed There-But-For-The-Grace-Of-God-Go-I role. So mono-path packs <b>caricaturing</b> your Ventrue's obsession with power and order, or your Gangrel's animalistic behavior.<br /> <br /> Your players are debating whether to kill that Duskborn because he is violating the masquerade by keeping a family who know his secret? Throw an Honorable Accord pack who kill their own families to protect Sabbat Secrets at them.<br /> <br /> They are there for the ST to wag his finger at the Cammy players and say, &quot;if you keep going down this path, you'll end up like those guys. Don't end up like those guys. Keep your humanity. Forgive that minor masquerade breech from a Duskborn keeping his family. Interact with humans instead of prowling the forest in search of prey. Don't be like those guys!:<br /> <br /> So, yeah, mono-path-packs designed to be plugged into finger-wagging lessons from the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-28-2021, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T10:44:11-07:00","id":1450010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449996#post1449996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;dr version<br /> * Talk about whole packs being on Paths, and concepts of Paths. Mechanics seem to just be 'the SPCs can ignore humanity and Stains entirely.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's boring as hell. Stains are ironically the part of V5's Humanity I love the most, other then the ability to make just about any conviction you desire. The slow spiral one goes that as they slowly realize they aren't human anymore is a great part of vampire. It also doesn't seem lore consistent, as followers of a Path could still fall to their beast if they didn't follow their path tenets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T10:49:07-07:00","id":1450012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450010#post1450010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's boring as hell. Stains are ironically the part of V5's Humanity I love the most, other then the ability to make just about any conviction you desire. The slow spiral one goes that as they slowly realize they aren't human anymore is a great part of vampire. It also doesn't seem lore consistent, as followers of a Path could still fall to their beast if they didn't follow their path tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They were flatly up front in saying 'this is a mechanic developed to facilitate SPCs.' But as Stains don't super matter for SPCs anyway by RAW, it feels weirdly tacked on and handwavey. They were very clear in stating that it's basically 'so the Sabbat can do bad things, but if normal PCs do these, they'll gain Stains' with how they described some of the Discipline powers.<br /> <br /> We'll see how it shakes out when we get the book, but it sounds like that's one mechanic that may not be great for PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:33:52-07:00","id":1450030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450001#post1450001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The internet fandom does not define literally everyone who plays WoD, let alone one forum (which has had a lot of people who like V5 just stop because of the constant vitriol that comes out of this place, anyway) in that internet fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it cuts both ways. I had to delete the official WoD Discord because the people there were downright antagonistic to a few people who came asking questions about V5 Sabbat, and it felt like a pile-on.<br /> <br /> It's so hard to gauge these things by what's happening online alone. That's why I think things like ICv2 and the DTRPG rankings are at least somewhat useful for these conversations, because any website will tend to attract its own particular audience and not others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:46:54-07:00","id":1450032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1449996#post1449996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;dr version<br /> * Book can be used for PCs if you want and all rules are there, but isn't written as a PC book<br /> -- Quote from the stream: Justin Achilli: \u201cI\u2019m sure there are players who are going to play Sabbat once they got the rule book. I have no doubt about it. Everything is there if you absolutely want to do it!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Called it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-28-2021, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:29:47-07:00","id":1450036,"title":"","content":"I didn't get chance to watch the interview yet, but I wouldn't break out the champagne just yet, CTPhipps. <br /> <br /> We still don't have the full picture of what the V5 Sabbat are going to be like, but it looks like they were truly devolved into pure monsters. People have been using the term &quot;monster manual&quot; to describe what we're likely to get with this book, and it sounds about right.<br /> <br /> With the Sabbat turned more and more into <i>creatures</i> that no longer even share a language with other vampires, we can expect them to be not only completely alien and monstrous beyond any previous depiction - we can expect that all they're capable of is to provide punching bags for Camarilla and Anarch characters to fight against, with zero other options (you can't <i>talk </i>to them). <br /> <br /> We're going to have about as much ability to creat and play Sabbat characters in V5 as we have the ability to create and play the Owls in Vampire: The Requiem 2e. <br /> The only difference between them is that Strix can actually fucking <i>talk</i> to other beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:44:51-07:00","id":1450041,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the whole clicking thing will be restricted to Feral Heart packs. After all, Power/Inner Voice vampires can't caricature your political ruthlessness if they can't talk, and Honorable Accord packs can't caricature your utter lack of mercy when upholding the masquerade if they can't talk either. However, Feral Heart packs can certainly caricature how predatory your Gangrel has become in his desire to live a hermit's life of simple hunting without speaking a word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:48:07-07:00","id":1450042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450036#post1450036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't get chance to watch the interview yet, but I wouldn't break out the champagne just yet, CTPhipps.<br /> <br /> We still don't have the full picture of what the V5 Sabbat are going to be like, but it looks like they were truly devolved into pure monsters. People have been using the term &quot;monster manual&quot; to describe what we're likely to get with this book, and it sounds about right.<br /> <br /> With the Sabbat turned more and more into <i>creatures</i> that no longer even share a language with other vampires, we can expect them to be not only completely alien and monstrous beyond any previous depiction - we can expect that all they're capable of is to provide punching bags for Camarilla and Anarch characters to fight against, with zero other options (you can't <i>talk </i>to them).<br /> <br /> We're going to have about as much ability to creat and play Sabbat characters in V5 as we have the ability to create and play the Owls in Vampire: The Requiem 2e.<br /> The only difference between them is that Strix can actually fucking <i>talk</i> to other beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That probably only applies to packs that follow very bestial paths. Achilli also proposed that a pack of Albigensians could operate in a Camarilla/Anarch domain by starting hedonistic cults that attract local kindred and deploying a load of ghouls. The Path of Death and the Soul was also mentioned, and they're nothing if not scholars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:05:01-07:00","id":1450047,"title":"","content":"Going by the part of his speech focusing on &quot;antitrbu&quot; makes me think he'll be going the caricature route. Where a Camarilla character seeks justice that may be infected with cruelty and mercilousness, the honorable accord vampire will be utterly cruel and merciless in pursuit of honor. Where the Camarilla Gangrel might seek to become a hermit hunting peacefully, the feral heart vampire will live so much like a beast that it forgets how to even speak in human language. Etc, etc. Caricatures of Camarilla PCs rather than characters unto themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:06:30-07:00","id":1450049,"title":"","content":"Well I guess now that V5 is officially the &quot;one true way &quot; to play the game and a real break from the previous editions of Vampire.<br /> <br /> No other editions purposefully excluded the Sabbat in that fashion, so I hope we can lay to rest the idea that V5 is for all VTM fan. It's not and never claimed to be. On the contrary devs have constantly pushed the idea that it's not the same game.<br /> <br /> If anything we the fans are to blame of believing otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:12:19-07:00","id":1450051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450049#post1450049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I guess now that V5 is officially the one true way to play game and a real break from the previous editions of Vampire.<br /> <br /> No other editions purposefully excluded the Sabbat in that fashion, so I hope we can lay to rest the idea that V5 is for all VTM fan. It's one and never claimed to be. On the contrary devs have constantly pushed the idea that it's not the same game.<br /> <br /> If anything we the fans are to blame of believing otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you're aware, the Sabbat didn't become playable - or even described in detail - until the 2nd edition of VtM, specifically the Player's Guide to the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> Maybe this is just a sign of how old and decrepit I have become, but I remember quite a lot of argument over whether the Player's Guide to the Sabbat was a good addition to the game. A lot of V5 aims to recapture the spirit of VtM 1st edition. The game changed in subtle and not-so-subtle ways over time as it was expanded and modified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:16:02-07:00","id":1450052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450049#post1450049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I guess now that V5 is officially the &amp;quot;one true way &amp;quot; to play the game and a real break from the previous editions of Vampire.<br /> <br /> No other editions purposefully excluded the Sabbat in that fashion, so I hope we can lay to rest the idea that V5 is for all VTM fan. It's not and never claimed to be. On the contrary devs have constantly pushed the idea that it's not the same game.<br /> <br /> If anything we the fans are to blame of believing otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. It's their game and their goals, and we can follow or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:16:48-07:00","id":1450053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450051#post1450051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so you're aware, the Sabbat didn't become playable - or even described in detail - until the 2nd edition of VtM, specifically the Player's Guide to the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a wait of about a year. 1st Ed was 1991, 2nd Ed and PGttS were both 1992. V5 is already three years old.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:21:57-07:00","id":1450056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450049#post1450049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I guess now that V5 is officially the &quot;one true way &quot; to play the game and a real break from the previous editions of Vampire.<br /> <br /> No other editions purposefully excluded the Sabbat in that fashion, so I hope we can lay to rest the idea that V5 is for all VTM fan. It's not and never claimed to be. On the contrary devs have constantly pushed the idea that it's not the same game.<br /> <br /> If anything we the fans are to blame of believing otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>No other Editions but 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> So its not a surprise.<br /> <br /> But I am glad Justin clarified the book will allow you to make PCs. I knew they'd do a cop out like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:22:40-07:00","id":1450057,"title":"","content":"While the player's guide came out in 1992 at the time of second edition, we should remember that First edition lasted only from 1991 to mid 1992. Second edition, revised and V20 lasted from 1992 to 2018. So until the arrival of V5, Sabbat was a playable faction for 26 years out of 27.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:23:18-07:00","id":1450058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450047#post1450047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the part of his speech focusing on &quot;antitrbu&quot; makes me think he'll be going the caricature route. Where a Camarilla character seeks justice that may be infected with cruelty and mercilousness, the honorable accord vampire will be utterly cruel and merciless in pursuit of honor. Where the Camarilla Gangrel might seek to become a hermit hunting peacefully, the feral heart vampire will live so much like a beast that it forgets how to even speak in human language. Etc, etc. Caricatures of Camarilla PCs rather than characters unto themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope not. Honestly, the &quot;clicking thing&quot; sounds more like how a WIGHT would ask. Sabbat have no use for Wights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:25:55-07:00","id":1450060,"title":"","content":"Yes. Well. At the start of the V5 vs. V20 thread I summed up my impression of V5 with:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443657#post1443657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short version is, V5 wants you to play a very specific sort of game and is not an asset if you want any other sort of game.<br /> <br /> [....]<br /> It feels like it could have been a softback alternate setting for the people who want those games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading this thread, my days of thinking V5 wants you to play a very narrow and specific type of game is certainly coming to a middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:29:56-07:00","id":1450061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450051#post1450051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so you're aware, the Sabbat didn't become playable - or even described in detail - until the 2nd edition of VtM, specifically the Player's Guide to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is just a sign of how old and decrepit I have become, but I remember quite a lot of argument over whether the Player's Guide to the Sabbat was a good addition to the game. A lot of V5 aims to recapture the spirit of VtM 1st edition. The game changed in subtle and not-so-subtle ways over time as it was expanded and modified.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes it's what we call a retcon. At best. Not that this change anything to what I said about one true wayism. We got you loud and clear. V2 onwards was a mistake. A mistake that V5 strives to correct. Okay. 25 years of Vampire down the drain.<br /> <br /> People like to compare V5 to DND4 but frankly it's far more divisive than 4e ever was. Imagine if wizards deleted the Sorcerer or Bard class because &quot;it was not in the first edition.&quot; Or &quot;it was a mistake.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-28-2021, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:46:25-07:00","id":1450063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450061#post1450061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes it's what we call a retcon. At best. Not that this change anything to what I said about one true wayism. We got you loud and clear. V2 onwards was a mistake. A mistake that V5 strives to correct. Okay. 25 years of Vampire down the drain.<br /> <br /> People like to compare V5 to DND4 but frankly it's far more divisive than 4e ever was. Imagine if wizards deleted the Sorcerer or Bard class because &quot;it was not in the first edition.&quot; Or &quot;it was a mistake.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh?<br /> <br /> My point is just that the creative vision is rooted in a dispute over this particular setting element that goes way, way back. Part of the reason Vampire: The Requiem even came into existence was creative dissatisfaction with some of the path-dependency built up in Masquerade over time; the setting kind of became stagnant, difficult to shake up, revise.<br /> <br /> Anyone remember the VtR book VII? It had three complete takes on what VII could be in your game. Part of the reason they did that was the toolkit approach the nWoD was taking at the time, but another reason was to preserve VII as a mysterious antagonist force - because back when the Sabbat was described in-full, that sense of mystery was lost, so they were attempting to split the difference and not make the same &quot;mistake.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want my personal opinion on what &quot;way&quot; they should have gone, I think attempting to put the Sabbat back in the mystery box is...well, I wouldn't call it a mistake, per se, since it's their vision to implement, so much as a lost opportunity. As pointed out, the vast majority of VtM's lifespan, the Sabbat has been the detailed organization we know and love. I would prefer V5 add a new antagonist group, one that they deliberately keep vague and/or toolkit in design approach, thereby creating a mysterious &quot;off the map&quot; antagonist.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, on the other hand, I'd like to see go through the Gehenna War and the V5 metaplot changes and all that fun stuff. Evolve it over time. Take some of the dated and juvenile elements that survived to VtM revised and dial them back, work the Paths to be more playable and interesting, and so on. One of the things I like about V5 is the Camarilla's regression into neo-feudalism as a defense mechanism against the Second Inquisition, it would be interesting to see how the Sabbat evolved to survive it as well in a playable sense.<br /> <br /> They've been on the map so long I think it'll be difficult to slap a &quot;Here be Dragons&quot; sign on the Sabbat and have it stick for old-timers, and newcomers won't notice either way.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But then again, I'd take a hatchet to every single WoD game, mechanics and setting, so I'm probably not the right person to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 05-28-2021, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:54:48-07:00","id":1450065,"title":"","content":"I don't see where you disagree with me.<br /> <br /> A lot of people actually think that the Sorcerer and Bard class and any Spontaneous Casters were a mistake. And were partly responsible for the abundance of magic present in modern D&amp;D. Especially compared to earlier editions. I did not make that comparison on the fly.<br /> <br /> The devs vision is thus comparable to Wizards deleting those classes to come back to a &quot;low fantasy&quot; feel like the good old days. There's nothing wrong with people prefering that kind of games but let's not pretend this is what D&amp;D is right now.<br /> <br /> V5 likewise divorced with previous editions of VTM. Comparable to Requiem indeed. This is why I do not like the comparison with DND4. V5 is another attempt at Requiem. It's rather clear by now. Keeping the setting but the driving concepts are the same: Scratch 25 years of Vampire to remake the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:57:54-07:00","id":1450066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450065#post1450065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see where you disagree with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not, I just thought it was useful context. People have been arguing about VtM since it came out; one of the reasons White Wolf was so successful was it made genuinely controversial (at the time) creative decisions. Of course it all seems quaint now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:59:29-07:00","id":1450067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450051#post1450051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so you're aware, the Sabbat didn't become playable - or even described in detail - until the 2nd edition of VtM, specifically the Player's Guide to the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>First edition released July 1991, PGtS released February 1993. That's 17 months, a year and a half, not a big leap, especially as with the first edition things were still getting worked out: the Cam was a global monopoly and the next biggest thing was the inconnu. Has V5 mentioned the Inconnu? V5 released in August 2018 and the book is scheduled for august 2021. That's three years, more than twice the time. When vampire was new and people weren't entirely sure what they were doing, now they should know better, yet they seem to be doing worse.<br /> <br /> Really don't understand why people think V5 is more like V1. It ain't. V1 was going places. There are so many V5 choices that are completely antithetical to what V1 was all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T14:07:07-07:00","id":1450070,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I hadn't even heard of VTM until the Sabbat book was already out. By this amount of time...wasn't Dark Ages almost out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T14:08:37-07:00","id":1450071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450067#post1450067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really don't understand why people think V5 is more like V1. It ain't. V1 was going places. There are so many V5 choices that are completely antithetical to what V1 was all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, VtM 1st was a hot mess that needed an edition cleanup from the jump. V5 is a hot mess already in need of a big revision pass, due to the ambition of changes it makes.<br /> <br /> If anything this makes V5 the most faithful edition of VtM we've seen yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Changed to be a little less harsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 05-28-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T14:16:31-07:00","id":1450073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450067#post1450067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First edition released July 1991, PGtS released February 1993. That's 17 months, a year and a half, not a big leap, especially as with the first edition things were still getting worked out: the Cam was a global monopoly and the next biggest thing was the inconnu. Has V5 mentioned the Inconnu? V5 released in August 2018 and the book is scheduled for august 2021. That's three years, more than twice the time. When vampire was new and people weren't entirely sure what they were doing, now they should know better, yet they seem to be doing worse.<br /> <br /> Really don't understand why people think V5 is more like V1. It ain't. V1 was going places. There are so many V5 choices that are completely antithetical to what V1 was all about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V5 is not like V1 obviously. It's a reactionary knee-jerk reaction to Vampire. It's the product of people who idealize the good old days and wanted to set the record straight from all the new stuff non-sense. (New as in 1993 new...)<br /> <br /> V5 is closer to Requiem in that respect in coming back to the true and pure form of what VTM <u><i>should</i></u> be. Instead of what it is, or what it was.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't find that kind of thinking particularly attractive. Requiem grew out of it thankfully, but I don't see how V5 will escape this narrow vision. Bar from from a total make over... ala Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-28-2021, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T14:55:19-07:00","id":1450076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450073#post1450073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 is not like V1 obviously. It's a reactionary knee-jerk reaction to Vampire. It's the product of people who idealize the good old days and wanted to set the record straight from all the new stuff non-sense. (New as in 1993 new...)</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">What possibly made you think this was cool or appropriate for these forums?<br /> <br /> A reminder of who produces V5 products and are very proud of them: the people who own these forums. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450071#post1450071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, VtM 1st was a hot mess that needed an edition cleanup from the jump. V5 is a hot mess already in need of a big revision pass. If anything that makes V5 the most faithful edition of VtM we've seen yet. All they need to do is start pumping out supplements with poorly researched and tasteless takes on real-world tragedies and they'll hit the early White Wolf hat trick.<br /> <br /> Er...wait a second...</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Insulting editions and fans of said editions is a bannable offense. Just to remind people. Edition Wars have no place here.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450067#post1450067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really don't understand why people think V5 is more like V1. It ain't. V1 was going places. There are so many V5 choices that are completely antithetical to what V1 was all about.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">A pattern is forming here. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-28-2021, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T15:08:20-07:00","id":1450083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450076#post1450076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">What possibly made you think this was cool or appropriate for these forums?<br /> <br /> A reminder of who produces V5 products and are very proud of them: the people who own these forums. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise if my words were too harsh. Perhaps I shouldn't have said a knee-jerk reaction. For the rest, I have read multiple people that did claim that V5 came back to V1 roots which was good because subsequent editions strayed from the original vision.<br /> <br /> Or is that a wrong assessment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T15:13:25-07:00","id":1450085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450083#post1450083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I apologise if my words were too harsh. Perhaps I shouldn't have said a knee-jerk reaction. For the rest, I have read multiple people that did claim that V5 came back to V1 roots which was good because subsequent editions strayed from the original vision.<br /> <br /> Or is that a wrong assessment?</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify for everyone, no one is asking anyone to like or dislike V5. It's just important not to bash it. If you have an issue, please explain what it is. This is a forum meant to be welcoming V5, V20 and everything before fans.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness too, albeit not in this particular forum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T15:20:18-07:00","id":1450086,"title":"","content":"Oh I meant that in the spirit of affectionate banter, not an insult. VtM 1st was a groundbreaking, glorious mess of a game, and V5 is laudably ambitious in how it tries to blaze a new trail for Vampire, but I doubt anyone will disagree it's been a bit of a rough road so far. I'm not hostile to any particular edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 05-28-2021, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T15:24:05-07:00","id":1450087,"title":"","content":"Honestly at this point, I don't feel blaming V5 per se. Disliking systems or lore choices is one thing, but I just cannot comprehend why the devs refuse to make the Sabbat playable in V5. I just don't.<br /> <br /> Again that's like deleting core classes like the Sorcerer or the Bard from D&amp;D. It's just... wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-28-2021, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T16:22:46-07:00","id":1450094,"title":"","content":"The truth appears to be that they regret ever coming up with alternatives to humanity in the first place. That's probably been true since Requiem, we just didn't notice because we were leaving anyway. They want you on humanity, period. The only choice you have is where in the Hallmark movie to &quot;Sin City&quot; range you pick your tenets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T16:23:58-07:00","id":1450095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450058#post1450058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope not. Honestly, the &quot;clicking thing&quot; sounds more like how a WIGHT would ask. Sabbat have no use for Wights.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could if those wights are intelligent. And that's how they've been described in V5 already:<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you met someone about to be swallowed by the Beast? Looked into the dead eyes of a wight in the making. If you have, you have surely felt it. The revulsion rising from the realisation that this inhuman thing could be you if you just gave in to the hunger. We recoil from the edge and cling to memories of hot life to keep it at bay.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are frightening because they look back at us with these same inhuman eyes, but they do so with <b>full cognition</b>. Here are the dead drones of the Beast, yet they are gifted with a collective intelligence disguised as faith and purpose.&quot; - Victoria Ash, <i>Camarilla</i><br /> <br /> It's not that unlike a Toreador stereotype of Tzimisce in Revised:<br /> &quot;They want to be machines. Blood goes in, thought comes out. That\u2019s their ideal, their aesthetic. Pretty dry, huh? What's surprising is how many of them can create beauty, almost by accident. There is a certain thrilling something that can arise from perfect functionality, isn\u2019t there?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T16:43:05-07:00","id":1450096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450094#post1450094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth appears to be that they regret ever coming up with alternatives to humanity in the first place. That's probably been true since Requiem, we just didn't notice because we were leaving anyway. They want you on humanity, period. The only choice you have is where in the Hallmark movie to &quot;Sin City&quot; range you pick your tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core theme of the game and almost all of its inspirational material does really hinge on there being a personal horror and tragedy inherent to the vampire condition, yeah. People have been pointing this out since the Paths of Enlightenment were introduced. There's a reason Requiem never offered any escape hatches from Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 05-28-2021, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T16:51:04-07:00","id":1450098,"title":"","content":"But yes, this is just my completely unsubstantiated opinion but I believe the Sabbat are officially NPCs because they're scared of the controversy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T17:30:07-07:00","id":1450105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450096#post1450096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The core theme of the game and almost all of its inspirational material does really hinge on there being a personal horror and tragedy inherent to the vampire condition, yeah. People have been pointing this out since the Paths of Enlightenment were introduced. There's a reason Requiem never offered any escape hatches from Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'm glad I didn't discover the game until the Sabbat and, shortly thereafter, the Dark Ages books came out, because I was never interested in playing Louis or Nick Knight, and I never will be. That's not to say I want my characters angst-free. There's plenty of tragedy in a Sabbat or Dark Ages game. But humanity? No. Zero interest, to put it in more far more polite terms that what I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T17:43:00-07:00","id":1450106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450105#post1450105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I'm glad I didn't discover the game until the Sabbat and, shortly thereafter, the Dark Ages books came out, because I was never interested in playing Louis or Nick Knight, and I never will be. That's not to say I want my characters angst-free. There's plenty of tragedy in a Sabbat or Dark Ages game. But humanity? No. Zero interest, to put it in more far more polite terms that what I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think V:TM is very well suited to playing either to be honest. V5 especially emphasizes that Nick Knight would still be a monster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T17:46:53-07:00","id":1450107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450106#post1450106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think V:TM is very well suited to playing either to be honest. V5 especially emphasizes that Nick Knight would still be a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care. At all. Whatsoever. I want the richness of roleplaying a path, not simply to be a monster trying to be human and failing at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:04:05-07:00","id":1450108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450107#post1450107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't care. At all. Whatsoever. I want the richness of roleplaying a path, not simply to be a monster trying to be human and failing at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the problem was, a lot of the Sabbat stuff and related paths of enlightenment in-practice acted as nothing more than a pretext for sadistic rampage fantasies, at least back when I played (a long, long time ago).<br /> <br /> Thankfully as Revised hit they tuned up Paths considerably to make them less &quot;The Path of What I Was Going To Do Anyway&quot; but still, they were always a spicy variation, never a staple focus of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:18:46-07:00","id":1450111,"title":"","content":"They were the heart and soul of the game for those of us who played/ran Sabbat games and Dark Ages. And our money is just as green as anyone else's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:41:58-07:00","id":1450114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450107#post1450107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't care. At all. Whatsoever. I want the richness of roleplaying a path, not simply to be a monster trying to be human and failing at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which thankfully is just a religion in V5.<br /> <br /> You can follow any Morality in the current books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450111#post1450111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were the heart and soul of the game for those of us who played/ran Sabbat games and Dark Ages. And our money is just as green as anyone else's.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Roads were designed as deliberate &quot;take thats&quot; at the Paths. The writers pretty much said upfront they considered the Paths to be perversions of what they felt Roads embodied.<br /> <br /> There was a lot of disdain in their write-ups where a lot of the Roads were made around the idea of being completely the opposite of the Path that shared their name.<br /> <br /> See the Road of Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:50:06-07:00","id":1450115,"title":"","content":"As someone that got started with the WoD games with Vampire the Dark Ages, finding out how the core modern game line treated Paths for most of its run was always extremely disappointing.<br /> <br /> The DA Roads never came off as &quot;Path of What I Was Going to Do Anyway,&quot; despite effectively being the same mechanics, because they were a fully integrated part of normal vampire society. <br /> <br /> To me, one of the reasons to enjoy the Sabbat is that the Paths make sense in VtM and all the talk about the thematic importance of Humanity rings hollow when you've experienced the game where Humanity is just one of many common approaches to being a vampire. If the only place you can really explore that is the Sabbat, either you need to change it so it's not so dominated by the Sabbat, or give people the Sabbat as a playable faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:54:49-07:00","id":1450116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450115#post1450115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, one of the reasons to enjoy the Sabbat is that the Paths make sense in VtM and all the talk about the thematic importance of Humanity rings hollow when you've experienced the game where Humanity is just one of many common approaches to being a vampire. If the only place you can really explore that is the Sabbat, either you need to change it so it's not so dominated by the Sabbat, or give people the Sabbat as a playable faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of that is what I mentioned above that Roads are not Paths, they are REBUTTALS to Paths. Paths are designed explicitly with the fact they will not contradict with your ultimate loyalty to your pack mates, the Sword of Caine, or the fact that you are expected to commit extreme atrocities against both humans as well as Camarilla vampires. Part of what Revised was correct about was the fact the Path of Harmony that simply put, &quot;I will do not do evil beyond what is needed to survive&quot; was enough to get them all slaughtered.<br /> <br /> Roads by contrast require the contradictory belief structures of Devil, Heaven, and so on to be things that do not work together and that if you must choose between sect and Road then you choose Road. Roads are also based strongly on real life mortal belief structures so we don't need to know how they would work in real life because Roads are things people have effectively followed in RL and show how they do it.<br /> <br /> Not so Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:55:06-07:00","id":1450117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450114#post1450114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which thankfully is just a religion in V5.<br /> <br /> You can follow any Morality in the current books.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can not. You can only fail at Humanity due to being deluded by some other belief system. That is not the same thing as Paths of Enlightenment being viable.<br /> <br /> As for the contrast between Roads and Paths: I found both fun to roleplay, regardless of writer intent. If I had to pick, I'd say I enjoyed Paths more.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T18:56:29-07:00","id":1450118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450117#post1450117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you can not. You can only fail at Humanity due to being deluded by some other belief system. That is not the same thing as Paths of Enlightenment being viable.<br /> <br /> As for the contrast between Roads and Paths: I found both fun to roleplay, regardless of writer intent. If I had to pick, I'd say I enjoyed Paths more.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you think Humanity works on being humane, you are incorrect. Like I mentioned before, you can be a professional baby murderer in V5 if your Chronicle Tenet matches it.<br /> <br /> And yes, Human Touchstones for Baby Murder are stupid. They do not prohibit it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T19:01:35-07:00","id":1450120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450116#post1450116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of that is what I mentioned above that Roads are not Paths, they are REBUTTALS to Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is completely irrelevant to the experience of being exposed to Roads first, and how V5 could be handling things now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T19:10:46-07:00","id":1450122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450118#post1450118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you think Humanity works on being humane, you are incorrect. Like I mentioned before, you can be a professional baby murderer in V5 if your Chronicle Tenet matches it.<br /> <br /> And yes, Human Touchstones for Baby Murder are stupid. They do not prohibit it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god, again with the baby murder thing. How many times do I have to say I want the full richness of playing a Path before you quit with the baby murder strawman? I'll say this yet again: does roleplaying a Path Paragon of this: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_the_Feral_Heart\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pa...he_Feral_Heart</a> sound like I want to go on a baby murder rampage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T19:13:17-07:00","id":1450123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450122#post1450122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh my god, again with the baby murder thing. How many times do I have to say I want the full richness of playing a Path before you quit with the baby murder strawman? I'll say this yet again: does roleplaying a Path Paragon of this: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_the_Feral_Heart\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pa...he_Feral_Heart</a> sound like I want to go on a baby murder rampage?</div> </div> </div> </div>The richness of Paths are provided by the Cults of the Blood Gods, one of the biggest releases so far. What else could you be upset about than the rules?<br /> <br /> Serious confusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450120#post1450120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is completely irrelevant to the experience of being exposed to Roads first, and how V5 could be handling things now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Cults of the Blood Gods goes a long way to introducing the Road experience to V5.<br /> <br /> I wish they'd gone with another name for Humanity, though.<br /> <br /> Morality perhaps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T20:50:22-07:00","id":1450130,"title":"","content":"Hmm, as they are doing large scale changes anyhow I think I would take another spin on Antitribus and make them an actual Sabbat project. I mean the Sabbat see themselves as the enemies of the old Antideluvians, monsters that will rise and eat all the vampires and a big problem with that is that the antis seem to have a unique power to control and perhaps even kill the descendants of their blood directly in a way that is not a specific discipline but rather a unique third generation power. So how to solve this? Replace the old, evil antideluvians! Make new ones! Develop a ritual similar to Marduks throat to turn a group of fourth gen into second gens, each an equivalent of one of the antideluvians. Then use something similar to the Baali re-embrace to then change the clans of various vampires in the Sabbati into these new, alternate anti clans and break the old Antideluvians power over their blood (Or would it?). It would be wonderfully contradictory and hypocritical and fit the Sabbat well. Make an Antitribu an actual direct metaphysical thing rather then a vague concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","name":"Palp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T21:49:38-07:00","id":1450133,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat serves the Antediluvians the same way the Camarilla and Anarchs do. After all, you can't beat the House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T22:55:41-07:00","id":1450137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450061#post1450061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People like to compare V5 to DND4 but frankly it's far more divisive than 4e ever was. Imagine if wizards deleted the Sorcerer or Bard class because &quot;it was not in the first edition.&quot; Or &quot;it was a mistake.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Bard's existed in 1st ed AD&amp;D. They were tucked into the back of The Players Handbook on page 117 of the 6th printing 1980.<br /> <br /> I kind of figured Justin's vision of VtM would be along these lines, so I am not surprised that the Sabbat guide gives me no reason to reconsider my position on Paradox products.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T23:04:20-07:00","id":1450138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450137#post1450137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bard's existed in 1st ed AD&amp;D. They were tucked into the back of The Players Handbook on page 117 of the 6th printing 1980.<br /> <br /> I kind of figured Justin's vision of VtM would be along these lines, so I am not surprised that the Sabbat guide gives me no reason to reconsider my position on Paradox products.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt this is Justin Achilli's decision given he wrote copious amounts about the Sabbat for Revised and helped make them make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T00:35:16-07:00","id":1450144,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think Cults of the Blood Gods is a suitable replacement for Paths. Personally, I'd have beefed up the Paths to integrate more elements from DA Roads. Then you have several axes of alignment in the game that might conflict and present drama: Clan/Sect/Road.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450063#post1450063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is just that the creative vision is rooted in a dispute over this particular setting element that goes way, way back. Part of the reason Vampire: The Requiem even came into existence was creative dissatisfaction with some of the path-dependency built up in Masquerade over time; the setting kind of became stagnant, difficult to shake up, revise.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, they doubled down on Paths for Dark Ages, and that worked really well. You just have to make Paths nuanced and not 'easy'. If you allow murder, then there has to be a counterbalance to make things harder elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I think VTR was borne of more than a rejection of the Paths, TBH. It was an attempt to start from scratch because the metaplot and setting had become so big it might be intimidating to new players and it was becoming harder to write new things for. Paths were only a tiny part of that puzzle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want my personal opinion on what &amp;quot;way&amp;quot; they should have gone, I think attempting to put the Sabbat back in the mystery box is...well, I wouldn't call it a mistake, per se, since it's their vision to implement, so much as a lost opportunity. As pointed out, the vast majority of VtM's lifespan, the Sabbat has been the detailed organization we know and love. I would prefer V5 add a new antagonist group, one that they deliberately keep vague and/or toolkit in design approach, thereby creating a mysterious &amp;quot;off the map&amp;quot; antagonist.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, on the other hand, I'd like to see go through the Gehenna War and the V5 metaplot changes and all that fun stuff. Evolve it over time. Take some of the dated and juvenile elements that survived to VtM revised and dial them back, work the Paths to be more playable and interesting, and so on. One of the things I like about V5 is the Camarilla's regression into neo-feudalism as a defense mechanism against the Second Inquisition, it would be interesting to see how the Sabbat evolved to survive it as well in a playable sense.<br /> <br /> They've been on the map so long I think it'll be difficult to slap a &amp;quot;Here be Dragons&amp;quot; sign on the Sabbat and have it stick for old-timers, and newcomers won't notice either way.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But then again, I'd take a hatchet to every single WoD game, mechanics and setting, so I'm probably not the right person to ask. </div> </div> </div>These are very interesting ideas. And I think introducing a new mysterious faction is the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450067#post1450067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition released July 1991, PGtS released February 1993. That's 17 months, a year and a half, not a big leap, especially as with the first edition things were still getting worked out: the Cam was a global monopoly and the next biggest thing was the inconnu. Has V5 mentioned the Inconnu?</div> </div> </div> </div>And this would be the mysterious group I'd work on. The Inconnu has several factions, such as the Monitors and the Golconda-chasers of Hunedora Castle. There's room to make a group that is actively antagonistic. <br /> <br /> Maybe the Monitors, who've been waiting for aeons, have now been 'activated' by the arrival of the SI, and take strong action to 'correct' Masquerade breaches. Or perhaps they seek Golconda, but realise that they have to atone for the sins of their brethren to achieve it. Or maybe they see the fingers of the True Black Hand, even where the TMR doesn't have any influence, and are waging a shadow war against an imaginary foe they believe is working directly for the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> You could give them several mysterious motivations that remain theories, and that would increase the mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T00:48:22-07:00","id":1450146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450076#post1450076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">A pattern is forming here. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? I don't see what I'm doing wrong here. V5 isn't a V1 throwback, at least going by core rulebooks. There are several issues: Disciplines being bloated in V5, while simple in v1. The Cam being big in V1 while small in V5, The differences in power between ancient and young were very stressed in v1, while greatly diminished in v5. V1 presents the possibility to become human again and move up and down the humanity scale, whilst V5 only lets you wallow in your lost humanity and buying humanity back is extremely cost prohibitive. The beast is a completely different animal, and the morality attitude has virtually reversed. The Corebook of V1 also didn't really care too much about cultural lines; everyone's cam, no matter where they're from, whilst V5 does it's absolute best to stress that it has so many cultural lines. V1 presented clans as self-selecting social archetypes, whilst V5 presents clans as bloodlines with diverse internal divisions. This idea that they're cutting back on the Sabbat to be &quot;more like V1&quot; is terribly wrong. If we weren't talking about a fantasy roleplaying game, but politics or something real, that kind of willfull misunderstanding could be dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T00:53:14-07:00","id":1450147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450123#post1450123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The richness of Paths are provided by the Cults of the Blood Gods, one of the biggest releases so far. What else could you be upset about than the rules?<br /> <br /> Serious confusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Cults of the Blood Gods goes a long way to introducing the Road experience to V5.<br /> <br /> I wish they'd gone with another name for Humanity, though.<br /> <br /> Morality perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>no they aren't. Seriously, Cults offers nothing in that vain, . It has zero in common with paths, plays nothing like them and has none of the same themes... Like I cannot even comprehend how you can think it does, it's like comparing apples to whales... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450138#post1450138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt this is Justin Achilli's decision given he wrote copious amounts about the Sabbat for Revised and helped make them make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ymmv on that, and his dislike for the Sabbat and people who played them was obvious at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-29-2021, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T03:53:44-07:00","id":1450154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450114#post1450114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Roads were designed as deliberate &quot;take thats&quot; at the Paths. The writers pretty much said upfront they considered the Paths to be perversions of what they felt Roads embodied.<br /> <br /> There was a lot of disdain in their write-ups where a lot of the Roads were made around the idea of being completely the opposite of the Path that shared their name.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the 1996 <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> core book and the rest of the original line, Roads are literally just Paths of Enlightenment with different names but effectively the same mechanics, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> says. Here we have the likes of the Road of Paradox where the greatest sin you can commit is &quot;Actively inducing boredom&quot;, and the Road of Typhon whose level 1 sin is &quot;Not attempting to awaken Set at the earliest opportunity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Such amazing depth to these Roads when compared to Paths.<br /> <br /> Your claim that Roads are a reaction to Paths only starts in the Revised era with the 2002 release of <i>Dark Ages: Vampire.</i> It doesn't surprise me at all if this is the case, given how the Revised era is characterized in my mind as the <i>reactionary</i> edition, chiefly concerned with ridiculing the efforts of earlier writers, cleaning up &quot;problematic&quot; content, and pruning off playstyles that the then-current crop of developers did not approve of. Characterizing the Roads as the real deal and the Paths as debased versions of their former glory only starts here. Like many other Revised era efforts, I find it condescending and not at all interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T04:31:13-07:00","id":1450158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450154#post1450154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the 1996 <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> core book and the rest of the original line, Roads are literally just Paths of Enlightenment with different names but effectively the same mechanics, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> says. Here we have the likes of the Road of Paradox where the greatest sin you can commit is &quot;Actively inducing boredom&quot;, and the Road of Typhon whose level 1 sin is &quot;Not attempting to awaken Set at the earliest opportunity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Such amazing depth to these Roads when compared to Paths.<br /> <br /> Your claim that Roads are a reaction to Paths only starts in the Revised era with the 2002 release of <i>Dark Ages: Vampire.</i> It doesn't surprise me at all if this is the case, given how the Revised era is characterized in my mind as the <i>reactionary</i> edition, chiefly concerned with ridiculing the efforts of earlier writers, cleaning up &quot;problematic&quot; content, and pruning off playstyles that the then-current crop of developers did not approve of. Characterizing the Roads as the real deal and the Paths as debased versions of their former glory only starts here. Like many other Revised era efforts, I find it condescending and not at all interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And with V5 they did what they wanted to do in Revised, is my guess, i.e. finish the purge of the badwrongfun.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also that Road of Typhon one is kind of thorny, I can see why and how it can be used to bind the adherent to the hierarchy of the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-29-2021, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T06:13:08-07:00","id":1450164,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but while Revised surely started the trend against the bad wrong fun, it never took any real steps against it.<br /> Achilli despised a certain kind of games, but those games were stille heavily supported at the time of Revised. Sure, Achilli wrote that Paths were badwrongfun and so on, but still Revised is the era where an entire supplement full of paths was published (Sins of the Blood).<br /> Achilli despised the trench-coat-katana plays, but Revised gave us Midnight Siege and Caine's Chosen, which were the apotheosis of the trench-coat-katana games.<br /> At the time of Revised the authors made clear that according to them the game should have been played in a certain way, but still they gave you tools to do your thing.<br /> That's the big difference with V5. V5 doesn't give you any tools and smash the existing ones. There is not a &quot;suggested way of playing&quot;, there is only one, forced upon every player. Fuck the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the bad approach of V5 is true even if we decide to make the comparison with Requiem: while the game started with a very clear interpretation of how a vampire game should be, later supplements gave you tools to expand what was suggested at first.<br /> The entire supplement of Belial's Brood was developed under this notion, and it was also explicitly said by the developers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> A NOTE FROM THE DEVELOPER<br /> <br /> <b>I didn\u2019t want to do this book. Not at first.</b> I didn\u2019t want to add depth to Belial\u2019s Brood, because I was afraid it would humanize them. To me, what makes<br /> Belial\u2019s Brood scary is their fearlessness. They\u2019re not afraid of ruining the world they used to inhabit as living people. They\u2019re not afraid of exposing their<br /> loved ones to the truths of the World of Darkness. They\u2019re not afraid of losing their grip on immortality or humanity. They\u2019d rather charge through the gates<br /> of Hell than dwell in fear of the inevitable.<br /> Put another way, they\u2019re fodder for vampirehuntingtales in which the hunters are themselves vampires. Belial\u2019s Brood are the utter dark against which any <b>Storyteller can cast her troupe\u2019s characters as protagonists. They\u2019re a rare breath of guiltless action in an otherwise morally complicated game.<br /> Not everybody wants what I want, though. Colin and Ari changed my mind. They convinced me that some Vampire players want to see the vampires<br /> of Belial\u2019s Brood explain themselves. Some players want to see them get the philosophical depth that a chronicle can be built on. Some players want to<br /> see these monsters as people. Fair enough</b>. Unlike the approach we took in the book VII, which offered three distinct possible truths to the mystery<br /> of that fringe group, this book takes a closer look at a multifaceted possible truth for the would-be covenant.<br /> But that truth is tangled up with lies, errors, folklore, assumptions and disinformation that have been collecting over centuries like layers of blood<br /> drying on a slaughterhouse floor. You have lots of optional truths in here, but the edges of each are not so defined.<br /> <br /> This book can be used whether you choose to humanize Belial\u2019s Brood in your World of Darkness or not, because everything in here is potentially<br /> hellish propaganda. Throughout this book, you\u2019ll see Belial\u2019s Brood meditate on its own existence, read thoughts of the Forsworn put down with a kind of<br /> clarity that seems impossible for these barbarians to muster, and maybe come to see them as something other than beasts and murderers. If you do, you\u2019r buying into the lie. (Look behind you.)<br /> Some parts of this book will change the emotional tone or power level of your chronicle (Investments aren\u2019t quite like any other kind of vampiric<br /> mysticism) if you choose to let them in. Know what you\u2019re getting into. Once you\u2019ve pulled back the curtain on Belial\u2019s Brood and let your players dabble<br /> with their powers, the shine starts to come off their crisp black finish.<br /> <br /> Remember, though, that Belial\u2019s Brood has left so much of its past in darkness. Its self-destructive nature has left it without elders to anchor its culture<br /> or pass down stories from its past. Even what you see here may just be an attempt by some of the Forsworn to back away from the Hell just as they get<br /> close enough to blister and peel. Behind the Belial\u2019s Brood of this book, the truer, older and more alien insanity of the utter dark may yet be sleeping.<br /> <br /> \u2014Will Hindmarch, Developer, Vampire:The Requiem </div> </div> </div><br /> This is why V5 approach is not just a shame compared to previous editions of Masquerade, but it is a shame even when we take in account Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-29-2021, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T06:29:05-07:00","id":1450165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450158#post1450158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also that Road of Typhon one is kind of thorny, I can see why and how it can be used to bind the adherent to the hierarchy of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with it (and some of the other early Path and Road writeups) is: How do you actually use that in a game? How often are attempts to awaken Set &quot;at the earliest opportunity&quot; going to come in a typical chronicle? Or <i>any</i> chronicle, for that matter? It's a pretty ridiculous level 1 sin.<br /> <br /> Same thing with the Path/Road of Paradox writeup. How do you &quot;actively induce boredom&quot; in a chronicle? (Apart from having discussions like this, I suppose...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T06:59:32-07:00","id":1450168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450165#post1450165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with it (and some of the other early Path and Road writeups) is: How do you actually use that in a game? How often are attempts to awaken Set &quot;at the earliest opportunity&quot; going to come in a typical chronicle? Or <i>any</i> chronicle, for that matter? It's a pretty ridiculous level 1 sin.<br /> <br /> Same thing with the Path/Road of Paradox writeup. How do you &quot;actively induce boredom&quot; in a chronicle? (Apart from having discussions like this, I suppose...)</div> </div> </div> </div>'Failing to Awaken Set at the earliest opportunity' well the earliest opportunity is obviously what ever scheme to further the cause of the glorious return the local priest/elder has cooked up, how dare you refuse to aid in this glorious work! Oh and if their are two rival elders ? well now better pick one and face the consequences, remaining neutral isn't furthering the great awakening...<br /> <br /> Paradox: 'Actively induce boredom' that is helping to stabilize local politics, not trying to cause havoc and war between domains etc (I think, Paradox didn't really interest me that much, so never thought about it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-29-2021, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T08:10:57-07:00","id":1450173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450164#post1450164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but while Revised surely started the trend against the bad wrong fun, it never took any real steps against it.<br /> Achilli despised a certain kind of games, but those games were stille heavily supported at the time of Revised. Sure, Achilli wrote that Paths were badwrongfun and so on, but still Revised is the era where an entire supplement full of paths was published (Sins of the Blood).<br /> Achilli despised the trench-coat-katana plays, but Revised gave us Midnight Siege and Caine's Chosen, which were the apotheosis of the trench-coat-katana games.<br /> At the time of Revised the authors made clear that according to them the game should have been played in a certain way, but still they gave you tools to do your thing.<br /> That's the big difference with V5. V5 doesn't give you any tools and smash the existing ones. There is not a &quot;suggested way of playing&quot;, there is only one, forced upon every player. Fuck the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the bad approach of V5 is true even if we decide to make the comparison with Requiem: while the game started with a very clear interpretation of how a vampire game should be, later supplements gave you tools to expand what was suggested at first.<br /> The entire supplement of Belial's Brood was developed under this notion, and it was also explicitly said by the developers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is why V5 approach is not just a shame compared to previous editions of Masquerade, but it is a shame even when we take in account Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ulch. So they want everyone who isn't human to be the same sort of one-note villains Superman would fight in old timey comicbooks? That's very simplistic, reactionary thinking disguised as enlightenment. &quot;Everyone who doesn't think like me is a subhuman caricature&quot; thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T09:34:50-07:00","id":1450179,"title":"","content":"The core tension of the game is between the horrific personal cost of vampirism on a human being and the temptations of inhuman power. Being able to say, &quot;Nah, I'd rather not pay the cost, but I'll keep the power&quot; kind of defeats that theme. <br /> <br /> They clearly don't want to make that game. Honestly can't begrudge them. Creative integrity matters, you know? <br /> <br /> Call of Cthulhu never did a playable Cthulhu cultist book for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 05-29-2021, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T09:50:08-07:00","id":1450180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450179#post1450179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core tension of the game is between the horrific personal cost of vampirism on a human being and the temptations of inhuman power. Being able to say, &quot;Nah, I'd rather not pay the cost, but I'll keep the power&quot; kind of defeats that theme. Vampire without personal tragedy is just an antisocial power fantasy.<br /> <br /> They clearly don't want to make that game. Honestly can't begrudge them.<br /> <br /> Call of Cthulhu never did a playable Cthulhu cultist book for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The last 25 years of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> were a mistake, and anyone who disagrees is not welcome in the new edition&quot; is certainly an interesting marketing angle to take. I don't think it convinced anyone the first time, though, and repeating the same point with minor variations is probably not going to change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T09:56:38-07:00","id":1450181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450180#post1450180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The last 25 years of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> were a mistake, and anyone who disagrees is not welcome in the new edition&quot; is certainly an interesting marketing angle to take. I don't think it convinced anyone the first time, though, and repeating the same point with minor variations is probably not going to change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is something very meta about the Sabbat being wiped out by the Second Inquisition, a group of dogmatists who think everyone who doesn't think like them is a subhuman caricature with no place in their world except as enemies to be slaughtered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T10:00:09-07:00","id":1450182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450180#post1450180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The last 25 years of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> were a mistake, and anyone who disagrees is not welcome in the new edition&quot; is certainly an interesting marketing angle to take. I don't think it convinced anyone the first time, though, and repeating the same point with minor variations is probably not going to change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest, I do think it was a strange decision to lace the print copies of the new book with a poison that only kills people who are looking to play Sabbat characters. I mean, how do you even tailor a poison to be selective based on intent? <br /> <br /> It really is not about you. They have creative vision X. Variation Y does not fit within X. Therefore, they aren't doing Y. It isn't a personal affront to people who liked Variation Y. You're literally just as welcome to play the game as you are welcome to play any edition of any game. The only difference between this and a new game is there is a body of previous work that sets expectations. Not having your expectations met is not the same thing as being rejected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T10:25:10-07:00","id":1450184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450179#post1450179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core tension of the game is between the horrific personal cost of vampirism on a human being and the temptations of inhuman power. Being able to say, &quot;Nah, I'd rather not pay the cost, but I'll keep the power&quot; kind of defeats that theme.<br /> <br /> They clearly don't want to make that game. Honestly can't begrudge them. Creative integrity matters, you know?<br /> <br /> Call of Cthulhu never did a playable Cthulhu cultist book for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is missing a good chunk of the points Vampire was originally out to make. The World of Darkness was always satirical, it's our world but the bad shit is exaggerated so you'd think about it a little more. Rich and powerful parasites? Let's make them vampires and players can have fun working out how they're going to screw the little guy in order to make their leech a little more comfortable. The part where players fully buy in to their own monsters? That's wonderful. The Horror of Vampire isn't about wailing at a mirror &quot;I failed a roll, Oh the Humanity&quot; but rather a complete, political horror in which every aspect of society is geared towards shitting downhill, which becomes funny when you're playing lets pretend in your friend's basement. Ergo it's completely appropriate to play Patrick Bateman from American psycho rather than, say, a perpetual teenager who's overly optimistic about the quality of their own poetry. V20 lets you play both, V5 only the latter.<br /> <br /> As for creative integrity, art should shed light on a truth, not raise a lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T10:46:53-07:00","id":1450185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450182#post1450182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really is not about you. They have creative vision X. Variation Y does not fit within X. Therefore, they aren't doing Y. It isn't a personal affront to people who liked Variation Y. You're literally just as welcome to play the game as you are welcome to play any edition of any game. The only difference between this and a new game is there is a body of previous work that sets expectations. Not having your expectations met is not the same thing as being rejected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not taking it personally, though. I rarely comment on V5, as a general thing, because even though the edition is not my cup of tea, a lot of sensible people seem to get a kick out of it. I'm simply looking at the reactions of people on this forum and other online spaces, and it certainly does not seem like they feel welcome in the new edition. The argument that the artistic vision of a particular development team trumps all other considerations <i>does not work</i> on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T10:53:58-07:00","id":1450186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450185#post1450185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not taking it personally, though. I rarely comment on V5, as a general thing, because even though the edition is not my cup of tea, a lot of sensible people seem to get a kick out of it. I'm simply looking at the reactions of people on this forum and other online spaces, and it certainly does not seem like they feel welcome in the new edition. The argument that the artistic vision of a particular development team trumps all other considerations <i>does not work</i> on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I genuinely do not know what you mean by &quot;feel welcome.&quot; They make a game they want to make, you like it or you don't.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I suppose if the Sabbat book has an introduction that explicitly declares a personal animus on the part of the designers to anyone interested in playing casually violent monster-fascists, that would make one feel unwelcome. So I guess we'll see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:06:58-07:00","id":1450189,"title":"","content":"Guys, I think I should interject something: <b><i>Justin Achilli being against playing monsters is nonsense</i></b><br /> <br /> This is the man who wrote the Giovanni books.<br /> <br /> He's the reason they're a bunch of incestuous vile inhuman monsters versus the tame depiction of 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Justin LOVES playing degenerate vile monsters. It's WHY he wrote the Sabbat books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-29-2021, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:22:43-07:00","id":1450193,"title":"","content":"I think it would be more accurate to say that he is against moral relativism. You can play a monster, but the mechanics will clearly frame you as evil and punish you for it. The idea that different species would have different ideas about right and wrong and that there would not be an objective answer that the universe punishes you for violating is repellent to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:36:15-07:00","id":1450195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450189#post1450189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the man who wrote the Giovanni books.<br /> <br /> He's the reason they're a bunch of incestuous vile inhuman monsters versus the tame depiction of 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Achilli's Giovanni clanbook <i>is</i> a 2nd Edition product? If you mean just the two-page spread in <i>The Vampire Players Guide,</i> here's the opening sentence of the writeup: &quot;No other clan is more intent on maintaining a front of respectability than the Giovanni, and <i>none is more repulsive at heart.</i>&quot; (Emphasis mine.) That... doesn't sound all too different from the eventual clanbook depiction. Of course a 70 page book is going to go into more detail than a 2-page spread about what being the most repulsive clan at heart really means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:44:45-07:00","id":1450196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450186#post1450186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I genuinely do not know what you mean by &quot;feel welcome.&quot; They make a game they want to make, you like it or you don't.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's really not hard. &quot;Feel welcome&quot; amounts to, &quot;feel like they want me to like their product.&quot; It's fine for a company to make a game that's unwelcoming to some people, that's their choice, and there's lots of reasons it could be a good choice. There's also plenty of cases were products feel unwelcoming for reasons that really don't stand up to reason.<br /> <br /> They don't just make games, they sell games. Selling games means convincing people to buy them. If people say, &quot;I don't feel welcome by this game,&quot; it means the game is not being sold to them; perhaps purposefully, perhaps not. But the &quot;you like it or you don't&quot; thing doesn't hold water when talking about a for-profit company's products.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:55:30-07:00","id":1450198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450196#post1450196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really not hard. &quot;Feel welcome&quot; amounts to, &quot;feel like they want me to like their product.&quot; It's fine for a company to make a game that's unwelcoming to some people, that's their choice, and there's lots of reasons it could be a good choice. There's also plenty of cases were products feel unwelcoming for reasons that really don't stand up to reason.<br /> <br /> They don't just make games, they sell games. Selling games means convincing people to buy them. If people say, &quot;I don't feel welcome by this game,&quot; it means the game is not being sold to them; perhaps purposefully, perhaps not. But the &quot;you like it or you don't&quot; thing doesn't hold water when talking about a for-profit company's products.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but this feels like more hurt feelings than mere disinterest. My understanding of the interview is that the primary focus of the book is supporting Sabbat-as-antagonists, with secondary consideration for player-facing material. That seems logical given most campaigns will feature Camarilla vampires where the Sabbat actually are relegated to a role as antagonists. It seems like a misplaced expectation to assume the game was going to expand on what was always a B-side campaign frame rather than focus on the A-side. I agree it's a lost opportunity, product-value-wise given it's always nice to have B-sides available, but if the writers are genuinely uninterested in the subject, I'd rather they work on what they feel passionate on first and foremost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:01:34-07:00","id":1450199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450189#post1450189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, I think I should interject something: <b><i>Justin Achilli being against playing monsters is nonsense</i></b><br /> <br /> This is the man who wrote the Giovanni books.<br /> <br /> He's the reason they're a bunch of incestuous vile inhuman monsters versus the tame depiction of 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Justin LOVES playing degenerate vile monsters. It's WHY he wrote the Sabbat books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except the monsters he plays and writes are on humanity, nearly always, and thus uninteresting and dull. Eating babies because low humanity is *yawn* eating babies because *weird philosophy says it's of no more concern than stubbing a cigarette* is interesting or can be, and humanity, the blood cults, the tenets and convictions system all totally fail to allow exploration of that idea beyond the lightest of skims. But then v5 Humanity is shallow and ignorable to a level I can't recall in previous editions, utterly unsatisfying and again, dull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-29-2021, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:03:03-07:00","id":1450200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450198#post1450198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but this feels like more hurt feelings than mere disinterest. My understanding of the interview is that the primary focus of the book is supporting Sabbat-as-antagonists, with secondary consideration for player-facing material. That seems logical given most campaigns will feature Camarilla vampires where the Sabbat actually are relegated to a role as antagonists. It seems like a misplaced expectation to assume the game was going to expand on what was always a B-side campaign frame rather than focus on the A-side. I agree it's a lost opportunity, product-value-wise given it's always nice to have B-sides available, but if the writers are genuinely uninterested in the subject, I'd rather they work on what they feel passionate on first and foremost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No the interview made it clear, they do not want people to play Sabbat, they understand it will happen, but it is not welcome or wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:17:01-07:00","id":1450202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450195#post1450195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Achilli's Giovanni clanbook <i>is</i> a 2nd Edition product? If you mean just the two-page spread in <i>The Vampire Players Guide,</i> here's the opening sentence of the writeup: &quot;No other clan is more intent on maintaining a front of respectability than the Giovanni, and <i>none is more repulsive at heart.</i>&quot; (Emphasis mine.) That... doesn't sound all too different from the eventual clanbook depiction. Of course a 70 page book is going to go into more detail than a 2-page spread about what being the most repulsive clan at heart really means.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point that he created the change of Revised to a darker, nastier, and more adult depiction of Revised due to his work there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:23:40-07:00","id":1450203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450199#post1450199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the monsters he plays and writes are on humanity, nearly always, and thus uninteresting and dull. Eating babies because low humanity is *yawn* eating babies because *weird philosophy says it's of no more concern than stubbing a cigarette* is interesting or can be, and humanity, the blood cults, the tenets and convictions system all totally fail to allow exploration of that idea beyond the lightest of skims. But then v5 Humanity is shallow and ignorable to a level I can't recall in previous editions, utterly unsatisfying and again, dull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bluntly, I think you've completely misread not only his intention but also the benefits that Justin Achilli made to those of us who like playing both the Sabbat as well as Paths. Justin Achilli made Paths BETTER and the entire system of it more enriched with his revisions. He also introduced an additional layer of conflict to the Sabbat that made the games more interesting as well as sustainable for Sabbat games.<br /> <br /> Before, there was the idea that Paths of Enlightenment were followed by 100% of the Sabbat, which is hard to take seriously. The idea that you could remove a lifetime of indoctrination and moral values by plopping someone in a gravesite and letting them out. Instead, Justin created a long and fascinating journey where a Sabbat vampire would be required to lower their Humanity and then build themselves back up.<br /> <br /> He made paths for the ELITE of the Sabbat. The intelligent, the strong-willed, and those sincerely committed to changing themselves to being superior beings.<br /> <br /> It's like climbing Mount Everest, it's rewarding because it's HARD and the idea that every Tom, Dick, and Harry can pull it off made the idea of eldritch occultism laughable. Places like Montreal with their churches, mysteries, and ritae became important because of the fact that maybe 10% at most Sabbat got to be Path followers and even then only a few would become masters of it. Or to put it another way.<br /> <br /> &quot;If everyone knows martial arts, it's not exactly cool is it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:33:54-07:00","id":1450204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450198#post1450198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but this feels like more hurt feelings than mere disinterest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is?<br /> <br /> V5 is supposed to be the 5th edition of a long running RPG called Vampire: the Masquerade, not just a new RPG about playing vampires. When a company decides to take on the task of making a new entry into a long running series of products, they have account for expected continuity of product experience.<br /> <br /> When you say you're making the 5th edition of something, a significant portion of your customer base are going to see that as a statement that you intend to make something that continues the previous four editions of the game in a meaningful way. If you make major changes, you will hurt some feelings. That's unavoidable, but there's strong reason to minimize it if you can (esp. if you're not having the greatest PR time as it is). You set expectations, and if you break those expectations, it hurts feelings; even if to an extent people made assumptions to base those expectations on that you didn't actively state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That seems logical given most campaigns will feature Camarilla vampires where the Sabbat actually are relegated to a role as antagonists. It seems like a misplaced expectation to assume the game was going to expand on what was always a B-side campaign frame rather than focus on the A-side. </div> </div> </div>This logic doesn't hold up to the context of being a 5th edition with the history of the brand. As has been noted, repeatedly, the Sabbat have been a playable faction of VtM since 1992, when the game has published in 1991. Calling the Sabbat a &quot;B-side&quot; doesn't really work when it's more the second single of an album with the Cam being the first single. The Sabbat are an A-side track, even if not the biggest hit on the record.<br /> <br /> As for placing expectations between (1) the history of the Sabbat being playable and (2) the actual B-side faction that is the Anarchs getting a player-facing book, the expectation that V5 would follow V2-V20 and keep the Sabbat a player facing option seems a perfectly justifiable assumption for fans to make. The Sabbat not being playable in the core book is one thing, but in the book dedicated to them? That's a different thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree it's a lost opportunity, product-value-wise given it's always nice to have B-sides available, but if the writers are genuinely uninterested in the subject, I'd rather they work on what they feel passionate on first and foremost. </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of people in the wider WoD freelance writer community that would have written a player-facing Sabbat V5 source book if given the chance. That's sort of the whole point of Paradox having so many partners: if Renegade doesn't have an interested party, see if Onyx Path does. Etc. It's not a one-person RPG shop where if one person isn't interested in writing it, nobody is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:36:00-07:00","id":1450205,"title":"","content":"CT... maybe you should stop trying to talk for Justin... he has plenty of platforms to talk for himself, and if he chooses to reconcile the different things he's written at different times.<br /> <br /> As well, maybe remember that he didn't do any of that himself. He was the Revised VtM developer, not the solo operator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:43:25-07:00","id":1450207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450203#post1450203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)Bluntly, I think you've completely misread not only his intention but also the benefits that Justin Achilli made to those of us who like playing both the Sabbat as well as Paths. Justin Achilli made Paths BETTER and the entire system of it more enriched with his revisions. He also introduced an additional layer of conflict to the Sabbat that made the games more interesting as well as sustainable for Sabbat games.<br /> <br /> 2)Before, there was the idea that Paths of Enlightenment were followed by 100% of the Sabbat, which is hard to take seriously. The idea that you could remove a lifetime of indoctrination and moral values by plopping someone in a gravesite and letting them out. Instead, Justin created a long and fascinating journey where a Sabbat vampire would be required to lower their Humanity and then build themselves back up.<br /> <br /> 3)He made paths for the ELITE of the Sabbat. The intelligent, the strong-willed, and those sincerely committed to changing themselves to being superior beings.<br /> <br /> It's like climbing Mount Everest, it's rewarding because it's HARD and the idea that every Tom, Dick, and Harry can pull it off made the idea of eldritch occultism laughable. Places like Montreal with their churches, mysteries, and ritae became important because of the fact that maybe 10% at most Sabbat got to be Path followers and even then only a few would become masters of it. Or to put it another way.<br /> <br /> &quot;If everyone knows martial arts, it's not exactly cool is it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Hard disagree and his statements, then and now, lean more into him not liking Paths, and certainly not liking the Sabbat as anything but a morality play. Putting Humanity in for anything but shovelheads, did what can now be seen as great harm to the Sabbat, and sent them off down the road of being off screened with an idiot ball (and no, the upcoming book will not change how stupid going from a serious rival to the cam to weird clicking unplayable crettins is)<br /> <br /> 2) all it needed was being on a path to be a requirement of being True Sabbat, and culling the shovelheads who couldn't get with the program inside a reasonable time frame.<br /> <br /> 3) he made them something you had to beg to play, even in a sabbat game. Since I find no interest in either games with humanity, or anarch games at all, that left slim pickings. (tho still more than the local Cam games, at the time, cam seemed to basically be ignored, outside of the LARP)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-29-2021, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:48:51-07:00","id":1450208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450205#post1450205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CT... maybe you should stop trying to talk for Justin... he has plenty of platforms to talk for himself, and if he chooses to reconcile the different things he's written at different times.<br /> <br /> As well, maybe remember that he didn't do any of that himself. He was the Revised VtM developer, not the solo operator.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that my opinion of Justin's design intentions comes from a unique and powerful insight.<br /> <br /> I read his blog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://justinachilli.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://justinachilli.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/cropped-49656341_10156964839413659_3201134611421724672_n.jpg?w=200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://justinachilli.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Justin Achilli </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://justinachilli.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://justinachilli.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Creative Direction | Games Direction | Narrative Direction </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:53:26-07:00","id":1450210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450208#post1450208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should note that my opinion of Justin's design intentions comes from a unique and powerful insight.<br /> <br /> I read his blog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://justinachilli.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://justinachilli.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/cropped-49656341_10156964839413659_3201134611421724672_n.jpg?w=200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://justinachilli.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Justin Achilli </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://justinachilli.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://justinachilli.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Creative Direction | Games Direction | Narrative Direction </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The last entry is from 2018...or is the site being weird? And if their is an entry where he expresses his love of the Sabbat and desire for people to play on paths, please supply it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-29-2021, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:56:40-07:00","id":1450211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450210#post1450210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The last entry is from 2018...or is the site being weird?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it's correct. Achilli's last entry was in 2018<br /> And it's worth noting that in his blog Achilli never talked about the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So...I'm not sure what CTPhipps is talking about...<br /> Because I read the blog too, you know, it's not that difficult, it's just 4 pages and...no idea what he is talking about.<br /> <br /> So, instead of throwing the blog's name in the fray, could you point where Achilli says what you are saying he said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-29-2021, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:05:27-07:00","id":1450214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450210#post1450210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last entry is from 2018...or is the site being weird? And if their is an entry where he expresses his love of the Sabbat and desire for people to play on paths, please supply it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so we're clear, you actually believe that Justin achilli hates the Sabbat and Paths despite spending thousands of hours writing on them? This isn't you being sarcastic.<br /> <br /> The guy who wrote SINS OF THE BLOOD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:09:10-07:00","id":1450215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450203#post1450203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before, there was the idea that Paths of Enlightenment were followed by 100% of the Sabbat, which is hard to take seriously. The idea that you could remove a lifetime of indoctrination and moral values by plopping someone in a gravesite and letting them out. Instead, Justin created a long and fascinating journey where a Sabbat vampire would be required to lower their Humanity and then build themselves back up.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this take is that in order to hype up Achilli's supposed contributions, you have to build up a complete caricature of <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat</i> that most people who have read the book will, I assume, recognize as a caricature. Nowhere in the book does it state that 100% of the Sabbat are Path followers. It explicitly states otherwise, saying that a minority of vampires survive the Creation Rites with their Humanity intact. The book only forbids characters with Humanity from starting the game with a rating higher than 5 (before freebie points), to reflect the trauma of their creation and the fact that simply running with the Sabbat takes its toll on the character's previous values (pages 59-60).<br /> <br /> More importantly, the Sabbat of 2nd Edition are supposed to be a much smaller sect than the Camarilla. They <i>are</i> the elites, the products of not just the Creation Rites but of continual indoctrination through years of brutality and atrocity. It's not the sect for every Tom, Dick, and Harry, because those people fell by the wayside long before they could ever become Path followers. To me it seems that everything you say Revised Edition did to improve the Sabbat is already there in the original 2nd Edition depiction, and all Revised managed to do was bloat the numbers of the sect with additional low-Humanity goons. How is that supposed to make the Sabbat more interesting and compelling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:12:53-07:00","id":1450217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450214#post1450214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so we're clear, you actually believe that Justin achilli hates the Sabbat and Paths despite spending thousands of hours writing on them? This isn't you being sarcastic.<br /> <br /> The guy who wrote SINS OF THE BLOOD?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> HE was the developer, not the Author. and yes I do, his comments on v5 Sabbat made that perfectly clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:17:08-07:00","id":1450219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450215#post1450215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with this take is that in order to hype up Achilli's supposed contributions, you have to build up a complete caricature of <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat</i> that most people who have read the book will, I assume, recognize as a caricature. Nowhere in the book does it state that 100% of the Sabbat are Path followers. It explicitly states otherwise, saying that a minority of vampires survive the Creation Rites with their Humanity intact. The book only forbids characters with Humanity from starting the game with a rating higher than 5 (before freebie points), to reflect the trauma of their creation and the fact that simply running with the Sabbat takes its toll on the character's previous values (pages 59-60).<br /> <br /> More importantly, the Sabbat of 2nd Edition are supposed to be a much smaller sect than the Camarilla. They <i>are</i> the elites, the products of not just the Creation Rites but of continual indoctrination through years of brutality and atrocity. It's not the sect for every Tom, Dick, and Harry, because those people fell by the wayside long before they could ever become Path followers. To me it seems that everything you say Revised Edition did to improve the Sabbat is already there in the original 2nd Edition depiction, and all Revised managed to do was bloat the numbers of the sect with additional low-Humanity goons. How is that supposed to make the Sabbat more interesting and compelling?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the discussion here is the assumption the PLAYERS GUIDE TO THE SABBAT is better than the GUIDE TO THE SABBAT. I feel like the Sabbat benefited from being a &quot;Core&quot; part of the experience versus a supplemental one and that Revised was designed with the idea that the Sabbat were one of the pillars of the setting alongside Anarchs and Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I certainly prefer the Revised Sabbat and think part of the issue may be here that I'm a fan of the Sabbat that is very different from the one you're promoting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:18:09-07:00","id":1450220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450214#post1450214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so we're clear, you actually believe that Justin achilli hates the Sabbat and Paths despite spending thousands of hours writing on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a more fair reading is that Justin doesn't like what the Sabbat became in the hands of people playing the game. He likes his vision of the Sabbat just fine. That doesn't mean he likes what the Sabbat is to everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:20:19-07:00","id":1450221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450219#post1450219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the discussion here is the assumption the PLAYERS GUIDE TO THE SABBAT is better than the GUIDE TO THE SABBAT. I feel like the Sabbat benefited from being a &quot;Core&quot; part of the experience versus a supplemental one and that Revised was designed with the idea that the Sabbat were one of the pillars of the setting alongside Anarchs and Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I certainly prefer the Revised Sabbat and think part of the issue may be here that I'm a fan of the Sabbat that is very different from the one you're promoting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup. That would be a fair assumption. They could have been made core without throwing away large parts of what made them interesting and fun, but that didn't happen. (The Players and Storytellers guide aren't perfect, nothing is, but they are more interesting and fun that the revised sabbat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T14:34:55-07:00","id":1450229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450182#post1450182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really is not about you. They have creative vision X. Variation Y does not fit within X. Therefore, they aren't doing Y. It isn't a personal affront to people who liked Variation Y. You're literally just as welcome to play the game as you are welcome to play any edition of any game. The only difference between this and a new game is there is a body of previous work that sets expectations. Not having your expectations met is not the same thing as being rejected.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is totally not the context here. That is how it works if you are an author writing a book for your own pleasure or some IP you own.<br /> <br /> This is not an artistic process or intended to produce art. It is a commercial product, aimed at selling books. The authors are not working on some IP they own themselves. They are being paid a wage to write stuff that will sell. I am sure no one objects if it has artistic value, and might even see it as a bonus, but I can't imagine that is in their contract, or will result in a Christmas bonus. Their &quot;creative vision&quot; is not relevant except possibly as something that got confused with the word &quot;quality&quot; in their TQM standards.<br /> <br /> That is what makes this so baffling. It is like management has abdicated all control and things have spun into some death spiral of &quot;our way or the highway&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T15:01:19-07:00","id":1450233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450229#post1450229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what makes this so baffling. It is like management has abdicated all control and things have spun into some death spiral of &quot;our way or the highway&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's baffling that they hired a well known Vampire writer to write a Vampire book, and he is doing it the way he thinks best, and then some fans who have a different take on what is best are unhappy?<br /> <br /> That ain't baffling, that's inevitable. I'm reminded of that meme from the Ballad of Buster Scruggs: &quot;First time?&quot; Controversial edition shifts are practically the White Wolf family brand. I can't think of a single one that didn't piss somebody off.<br /> <br /> Your argument kind of depends on it being <i>obviously </i>and <i>incontrovertibly </i>wrong not to support player Sabbat, but while I agree it's probably the wrong call, I don't think it's that obviously wrong given the design intent of V5. I can see the logic to it. Certainly it's not so obvious that I'd interpret it as a deliberate snub to a particular subset of the existing fanbase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 05-29-2021, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T17:48:54-07:00","id":1450241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450196#post1450196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's really not hard. &quot;Feel welcome&quot; amounts to, &quot;feel like they want me to like their product.&quot; It's fine for a company to make a game that's unwelcoming to some people, that's their choice, and there's lots of reasons it could be a good choice. There's also plenty of cases were products feel unwelcoming for reasons that really don't stand up to reason.<br /> <br /> They don't just make games, they sell games. Selling games means convincing people to buy them. If people say, &quot;I don't feel welcome by this game,&quot; it means the game is not being sold to them; perhaps purposefully, perhaps not. But the &quot;you like it or you don't&quot; thing doesn't hold water when talking about a for-profit company's products.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest. I think that the boardames, the new computer games and if theymanage to make a movie/series as well as the comics. They wil get more fans. And even though you do not buy their product - others will.<br /> <br /> Mayne of those who complian here about the Sabbat book, has complained about V5 from start. So they have already lost you long before the Sabbat and therefore - why make a book that caters to you? When they can make a book that will entice other old fans and lots of new fans? It seems to me that many of those that has complained has refused to buy the books and are just vocal in their displeasure.<br /> <br /> Though i might be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T18:24:13-07:00","id":1450246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450220#post1450220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a more fair reading is that Justin doesn't like what the Sabbat became in the hands of people playing the game. He likes his vision of the Sabbat just fine. That doesn't mean he likes what the Sabbat is to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember being on the old White Wolf mailing list back in the late 90's and very early 2000's, and Justin would occasionally post. He liked a lot of aspects of the World of Darkness but didn't like what players did with them. Especially in regards to the Sabbat, he was always unhappy with the way those games nearly always turned into &quot;trenchcoats and katanas&quot; and personal horror was totally absent.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think Justin would have personally wanted to wall off the Sabbat as PCs, because he always made it clear that even if people were having fun with things in ways he didn't care about, if they were having fun that was the most important thing. So I have to imagine that the, &quot;No Sabbat player characters&quot; decision came down from higher up at Paradox, and Justin's response was to include a bunch of extensive rules so that players could still play the Sabbat regardless, fulfilling the &quot;no Sabbat player characters&quot; mandate while still providing enough material for people who really wanted to play them.<br /> <br /> But who knows. Vt1 came out almost 30 years ago, and things change. Maybe Justin does look back and think that, in retrospect, playable Sabbat were a major mistake, but if that was the case he probably wouldn't have included extensive rules for people who really wanted to play Sabbat. Ultimately having a book with systems and rules for Sabbat PCs along with a note that says, &quot;No Sabbat PCs&quot; seems more like his way to comply with a mandate to not allow Sabbat PCs than something he chose to write because he doesn't want to see Sabbat PCs in any way whatsoever. If that was the case it would have been easier to have no rules or anything that people could use as PC options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-29-2021, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T18:31:21-07:00","id":1450248,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I haven't played Vampire since before the oceans drank Atlantis, but in my experience about half the time there was a Certain Kind of Player, who was creepily fixated on Sabbat characters and Sabbat campaigns, for which all the material supporting those characters with depth was just a pretext to justify acting-out antisocial power fantasies at the table. The other half of the time it was just Trenchcoat Katana Action Hour, but that was true of every game back then, it was high school, I'm so old, when did that happen, why do I see the creeping shadow of my own mortality everywhere I look....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T18:34:02-07:00","id":1450250,"title":"","content":"I'm just glad the Sabbat isn't a simple power fantasy for angsty and edgy players to go killing and torturing like D&amp;D murder hobos describing how they use the goblin chiefs head as hat. And well, I agree with Achilli, V5 as product does not sit well thematically with a playable Sabbat, it would seem like a Vampire spinoff, not a supplement, and from all i've seen they are pretty playable in all actuality, just as elders are, the focus is simply not on them. It would be either Vampire the Death Cult or Vampire the Power Play, and no Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> And for the first time ever, the interview with Justin made want to use and even play with (and as) Sabbat in V5, and I'm really excited for this book. In the interview at least they stripped it from all that convoluted hierarchies, subfactions, True Black Hand, Inquisitor, Knights, Templars, Regents and etc. to talk and conceive the Sabbat for what it truly is, and I'm eager to see it exposed in the coming book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T20:08:30-07:00","id":1450258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450233#post1450233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That ain't baffling, that's inevitable. I'm reminded of that meme from the Ballad of Buster Scruggs: &quot;First time?&quot; Controversial edition shifts are practically the White Wolf family brand. I can't think of a single one that didn't piss somebody off.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness this could be applied to every edition change of every RPG. Ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T21:23:37-07:00","id":1450273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450250#post1450250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm just glad the Sabbat isn't a simple power fantasy for angsty and edgy players to go killing and torturing like D&amp;D murder hobos describing how they use the goblin chiefs head as hat. And well, I agree with Achilli, V5 as product does not sit well thematically with a playable Sabbat, it would seem like a Vampire spinoff, not a supplement, and from all i've seen they are pretty playable in all actuality, just as elders are, the focus is simply not on them. It would be either Vampire the Death Cult or Vampire the Power Play, and no Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> And for the first time ever, the interview with Justin made want to use and even play with (and as) Sabbat in V5, and I'm really excited for this book. In the interview at least they stripped it from all that convoluted hierarchies, subfactions, True Black Hand, Inquisitor, Knights, Templars, Regents and etc. to talk and conceive the Sabbat for what it truly is, and I'm eager to see it exposed in the coming book.</div> </div> </div> </div>. Edit: NVM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-30-2021, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T00:19:44-07:00","id":1450287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450241#post1450241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest. I think that the boardames, the new computer games and if theymanage to make a movie/series as well as the comics. They wil get more fans. And even though you do not buy their product - others will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will they get fans or customers is the real question though. Yes, they'll sell products. But are they going to be things people are playing a year later? Five years later?<br /> <br /> It's really not that hard (esp. in the video game and TV/movie arenas) to make something that can turn a profit on some level; at least if you have the starting capital. It's a lot hard to actually make something people go back and play/watch/read again. To make things that people tell their friends about and try to get them into as well. To make things people will pay full price for because of how much they enjoyed the previous game and not wait until it's on sale on Steam for 75% off. <br /> <br /> Getting fans isn't the same thing as making sales. The point of cultivating fans, is because they drive sales. It's a tight line to walk, because companies don't want to cede full control to the fans, but balancing keeping old fans with attracting new ones is important. Just betting on new fans has a very bad track record. Of course so does just focusing on old ones. Hence the need to make sure you're working to satisfy both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mayne of those who complian here about the Sabbat book, has complained about V5 from start. </div> </div> </div>1) Complaining &quot;from the start&quot; doesn't invalidate an opinion. And nobody actually complained from the start. Even I was actually cautiously optimistic about V5 at one point. They lost me at the second playtest because it was clear that all the great things I heard from the initial announcements weren't something the team knew how to deliver after seeing the playtests, and responses.<br /> <br /> 2) There's also plenty of people that have said the V5 Sabbat announcement was a deal breaker for them. Complainers or not, people that were buying V5 stuff, have said they're not buying this V5 thing, or done with V5 completely over this. That's not just old school complainers like me finding something knew to point out is bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> why make a book that caters to you? When they can make a book that will entice other old fans and lots of new fans? </div> </div> </div>They should make books that cater to me because they should want my money. I'm not a hard sell on new editions. V5 is the first new edition for the entire WW catalog (not just WoD) where I haven't converted to the most recent edition (sometimes more enthusiastically than others, but still, first time I haven't). I own V1 through V20, with the majority of the supplements, both editions of DA, and Victorian. Vampire is one of my least favorite WoD games and I have more books for it than I have for dozens of RPGs I like better. I have both VtM video games and I've played them within the last year. I once owned the DVD set of the old TV show.<br /> <br /> I might be biased... but if I was selling a new edition, and saw a fan that threw that much money at all the older stuff, but refuses to spend a penny on the new stuff? I'd want to know why. Maybe it's just some sort of grognard idiocy, but maybe there's something worth hearing to make the new stuff better. And it's not just my money. I can think of at least two dozen people that know I'm a big WoD fan, and asked me about V5 because they heard about it, and my negativity towards it convinced them to skip it too. Are 25 sales going to kill Paradox's bottom line. No. But do you think I'm alone? Is banking on all those potential fans a good idea if you're pissing off the hardcore ones that already exist? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450248#post1450248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit I haven't played Vampire since before the oceans drank Atlantis, but in my experience about half the time there was a Certain Kind of Player, who was creepily fixated on Sabbat characters and Sabbat campaigns, for which all the material supporting those characters with depth was just a pretext to justify acting-out antisocial power fantasies at the table. The other half of the time it was just Trenchcoat Katana Action Hour, but that was true of every game back then, it was high school, I'm so old, when did that happen, why do I see the creeping shadow of my own mortality everywhere I look....</div> </div> </div> </div>Those players exist with or without the Sabbat. D&amp;D has the players that always want to be evil or chaotic neutral.<br /> <br /> If a game leaves playing the baddies as a possibility, there are people out there that want to play it as power fantasy rather than deep character study.<br /> <br /> Not having playable Sabbat doesn't make them not exist; either they pester to be Sabbat anyway, or they just pick the Clan that best suites their power fantasies in whatever faction they can ick from. I've seen more than enough cartoonishly evil corporate overlord style Cam Ventrue to ever buy that cutting out playable Sabbat is actually going to deter these sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T01:07:50-07:00","id":1450290,"title":"","content":"Just as a personal note I purchased the 5th edition core book and ended up buying Chicago by Night, but with what happened with the Sabbat book, I won't be purchasing any future V5 books. Again, there was material I liked, and material I didn't like, but the decision to make the Sabbat an NPC only sect sent a message to me that I'm not the person they're publishing these books for. Which is fine, they can write whatever they want, but like with Heavy Arms, this will be the first edition I'm skipping and don't purchase any further books for (and this is coming from a guy with a dozen boxes of WoD books for every gameline sitting in my garage).<br /> <br /> Plus, past just Vampire, it's also making me extremely leery about the upcoming Werewolf 5th edition and other possible editions of other games beyond those as well. I may end up finding myself just writing off the World of Darkness as a whole, which would make me pretty sad considering I've been following this setting since I was in high school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T02:25:25-07:00","id":1450293,"title":"","content":"Ok, a thought occurs, from the interview: The hierarchy and priesthood is gone, Packs have been turned into monopath drone squads so interpack/path rivalries are gone, territory and goals are gone...what exactly is left to call Sabbat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-30-2021, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T03:32:09-07:00","id":1450297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450290#post1450290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a personal note I purchased the 5th edition core book and ended up buying Chicago by Night, but with what happened with the Sabbat book, I won't be purchasing any future V5 books. Again, there was material I liked, and material I didn't like, but the decision to make the Sabbat an NPC only sect sent a message to me that I'm not the person they're publishing these books for. Which is fine, they can write whatever they want, but like with Heavy Arms, this will be the first edition I'm skipping and don't purchase any further books for (and this is coming from a guy with a dozen boxes of WoD books for every gameline sitting in my garage).<br /> <br /> Plus, past just Vampire, it's also making me extremely leery about the upcoming Werewolf 5th edition and other possible editions of other games beyond those as well. I may end up finding myself just writing off the World of Darkness as a whole, which would make me pretty sad considering I've been following this setting since I was in high school.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean I bought V5 Core book after all despite them ignoring every single fix and improvement suggested in our playtesting submissions but pretty much gave up after a few months as the mechanics of the rule set kept draining the fun out of every session. That said I'm not too fussed as I've read all the V5 books that have come out and can see I'm not missing anything and its freed up the cash to spend a hell of lot on V20 products from Storytellers Vault that, for myself at least, seem to be much better in terms of writing quality than any of the non-OPP V5 products and up to and in cases exceeding the quality of those.<br /> <br /> So I'm fine, personally. <br /> <br /> But I do feel for those fans who have stuck with V5 hoping that it would do something, anything to allow them to play the games they loved to play with VtM through the decades. So I can understand there would be feelings of being cast aside and ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T03:53:46-07:00","id":1450303,"title":"","content":"Outstar has said you can use the book for creating a sabbat pc it's just not the focus of the book.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/JOSEPHRAYMONDM6/status/1397498302132891650/photo/1\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/JOSEPHRAYMONDM6/...891650/photo/1</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","name":"Syren1987","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T08:24:13-07:00","id":1450312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450293#post1450293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, a thought occurs, from the interview: The hierarchy and priesthood is gone, Packs have been turned into monopath drone squads so interpack/path rivalries are gone, territory and goals are gone...what exactly is left to call Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. They probably just exist to caricature the flaws of the Camarilla players. The Honorable Accord packs are there to caricature how ruthless your Cammy players are getting in their attempts to create order and justice.<br /> <br /> Your players are debating killing that guy who is technically violating the masquerade by keeping a family and them knowing his secret? Throw an Honorable Accord pack at them who murder their own families to protect Sabbat secrets, emphasize how horrific and bestial they are as part of a &quot;there but for the grace of God go I!&quot; message to wag your finger at the players with.<br /> <br /> Your Gangrel player has been becoming a feral hermit, spending most of their time in the woods avoiding human contact? Throw a Feral Heart pack at them who are so animalistic they've forgotten human language. Emphasize how horrific and bestial they are as part of a &quot;there but for the grace of God go I!&quot; message to wag your finger at the players with.<br /> <br /> They exist now to be dark reflections, telling the player there is no solution to the Beast. Focus on justice and the Beast will make you a merciless rule machine. Avoid humans entirely because you don't want to hurt them, and the Beast will devolve you into a literal animal.<br /> <br /> They are wights, but wights that tell more sophisticated lessons than the old wights did. But still just there to teach lessons to others rather than being characters themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T08:52:21-07:00","id":1450315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Syren1987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450303#post1450303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outstar has said you can use the book for creating a sabbat pc it's just not the focus of the book.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/JOSEPHRAYMONDM6/status/1397498302132891650/photo/1\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/JOSEPHRAYMONDM6/...891650/photo/1</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, you can homebrew it to play as Sabbat, but we knew that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T12:10:08-07:00","id":1450335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450315#post1450315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yea, you can homebrew it to play as Sabbat, but we knew that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it homebrew? I mean, if the rules provide everything to make a Sabbat PC its not homebrew.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T12:14:28-07:00","id":1450337,"title":"","content":"Does it count as homebrew if you really don't have to do anything to the mechanics or setting?<br /> <br /> Each person uses the phrase with varying degrees of meaning. I bring it up so everyone is on the same page.<br /> <br /> Ex. For me making an adventure in an established world isn't homebrew. Making my own setting is.<br /> <br /> And now homebrew is tarting to sound weird to me. Sigh...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T12:16:34-07:00","id":1450338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450335#post1450335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it homebrew? I mean, if the rules provide everything to make a Sabbat PC its not homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it isn't RAW (and thus going to be rarer on Roll20 et al.) Then yes, it's homebrew, and also almost certainly going to be unsupported. Maybe you could argue house rule, but it's the same level of Homebrew as (for instance) good Drow cities used to be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-30-2021, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T12:25:24-07:00","id":1450339,"title":"","content":"While convictions in some ways make more sense than paths, as I do think they're more &quot;organic&quot; to real human morality, they're also more dependent on what the storyteller will allow. If I want a character to have some complicated crazy religion (say I'm playing a setite) it's basically impossible to ask a storyteller for enough convictions to actually get that to work, at least in a game where there are two or three other players and they all want convictions that, while not oppositional to my convictions, aren't the same. You've also got to consider how many fucking touchstones does the Settite need to pull off all the convictions his religion needs, maybe it's his entire cult, but then again touchstones are really antithetical to the whole settite belief system since reality's a prison and you need to break chains and....<br /> <br /> Yeah<br /> That's why we need paths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also will Sabbat even viniculum anymore since Lasombra can apparently laugh that off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T12:36:02-07:00","id":1450342,"title":"","content":"We get the problem that Tenets 'force' you to care about actions that your personal morality doesn't, convictions only mitigate that, you still eventually wassail if you disobey the outside force imposing tenets, morals don't work that way it doesn't matter how much the local society tries to force religious/political ideas, dissent isn't madness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T13:26:10-07:00","id":1450346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450342#post1450342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We get the problem that Tenets 'force' you to care about actions that your personal morality doesn't, convictions only mitigate that, you still eventually wassail if you disobey the outside force imposing tenets, morals don't work that way it doesn't matter how much the local society tries to force religious/political ideas, dissent isn't madness</div> </div> </div> </div>The change of Humanity is that it is acting against YOUR beliefs.<br /> <br /> And yes, people have been driven to quivering broken messes by mental disassociation from their actions, guilt, and trauma.<br /> <br /> RL is full of people who are destroyed by their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T13:41:07-07:00","id":1450347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450346#post1450346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The change of Humanity is that it is acting against YOUR beliefs.<br /> <br /> And yes, people have been driven to quivering broken messes by mental disassociation from their actions, guilt, and trauma.<br /> <br /> RL is full of people who are destroyed by their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not tho, Tenets are not your beliefs. They are a forced common morality, supposedly from society, society can tell me a billion times something or someone is evil, doesn't deserve to live etc not agreeing won't make me go insane. You are never going to convince me that Biblical commandments are moral (3 of them are: no murder, no theft, no false witness) breaking the other 7 won't eventually drive me mad, breaking Tenets will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-30-2021, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T13:42:44-07:00","id":1450348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450347#post1450347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not tho, Tenets are not your beliefs. They are a forced common morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tenets are there for the benefit of the Storyteller so that the players and they are on the same page in what sort of game they want to play. Surely you don't object to that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T13:49:59-07:00","id":1450350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450348#post1450348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tenets are there for the benefit of the Storyteller so that the players and they are on the same page in what sort of game they want to play. Surely you don't object to that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I do. Do a session zero, set limits and run the story, in game penalties have no place in that. Tenets get in the way. (Consequences of NPCs reacting to PC actions is a whole different thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-30-2021, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:06:28-07:00","id":1450352,"title":"","content":"Morality isn't as simple as &quot;beliefs go in, behavior comes out.&quot; People have empathy, intuitions, and social instincts that are not produced by specific social pressures or by philosophical convictions.<br /> <br /> That was the problem with the Paths of Enlightenment, they weren't actually paths you had to follow to progressively dismantle your humanity, they were a button you pressed in character creation to turn off the game's most fundamental conflict. It'd be like having an option in Call of Cthulhu to be cool with the Mythos and be immune to SAN loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 05-30-2021, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:11:12-07:00","id":1450353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450352#post1450352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morality isn't as simple as &quot;beliefs go in, behavior comes out.&quot; People have empathy, intuitions, and social instincts that are not produced by specific social pressures or by philosophical convictions.<br /> <br /> That was the problem with the Paths of Enlightenment, they weren't actually paths you had to follow, they were a button you pressed in character creation to turn off the game's most fundamental conflict. It'd be like having an option in Call of Cthulhu to be cool with the Mythos and be immune to SAN loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you didn't think about the implications of the Sins. Some of them are real nasty buggers that look like a license to do anything, but can bite real hard. They could be far more tricky that. Humanity ever was, you could just hit humanity 4 and forget about it mostly, Paths not so much, some would still get you, all the way to 1.<br /> Prime example:. Typhon 1 'Fail to aid in Sets resurrection' sounds like it would never come up right? Except it should, what ever scheme your Elders are running is working towards Sets Resurrection (honest), not aiding them is not aiding the great awakening, and ofc they each have competing schemes, and you are bound, on pain of wassail, to help....<br /> <br /> Example 2: Power and the Inner Voice 1: Never turn down an opportunity for power. Well hello unwise bargains, and becoming the fall guy or the bullseye on the throne... Not commiting mass murder is way simpler than either of those..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-30-2021, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:21:21-07:00","id":1450355,"title":"","content":"And of course, VtM has a lot of &quot;central conflicts&quot; but the most important one is frequently whatever is best for someone trying to score points in an argument rather than any real attempt to justify that by the books (since the books talk about a lot of conflicts to explore and do not generally settle on one that rules them all even if certain developers and writers do).<br /> <br /> Paths aren't about eroding your Humanity, they're about rebuilding your resistance to the Beast after your Humanity has been eroded in a fashion other than rebuilding Humanity. Taking a Path at char-gen is, yes, skipping past the &quot;lose a bunch of Humanity and then gain a Path,&quot; part, but that's because playing through that just to play through it is not actually that interesting. If I make a character that starts with an odd Discipline selection for their Clan instead of earning it in-game, I've &quot;skipped&quot; stuff, but that doesn't mean I've tossed away something vital to the game. It means I've skipped forward to the part that's vital to the game I'm trying to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:27:48-07:00","id":1450356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450355#post1450355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, VtM has a lot of &quot;central conflicts&quot; but the most important one is frequently whatever is best for someone trying to score points in an argument rather than any real attempt to justify that by the books (since the books talk about a lot of conflicts to explore and do not generally settle on one that rules them all even if certain developers and writers do).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, there are points? How many did I get? Can I turn them in for prizes? <br /> <br /> I had no interest in provoking a hostile response or convincing you to like something you dislike, so I'll bow out now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T15:10:39-07:00","id":1450361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450352#post1450352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morality isn't as simple as &quot;beliefs go in, behavior comes out.&quot; People have empathy, intuitions, and social instincts that are not produced by specific social pressures or by philosophical convictions.<br /> <br /> That was the problem with the Paths of Enlightenment, they weren't actually paths you had to follow to progressively dismantle your humanity, they were a button you pressed in character creation to turn off the game's most fundamental conflict. It'd be like having an option in Call of Cthulhu to be cool with the Mythos and be immune to SAN loss.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Paths didn't turn off the game's fundamental conflict, they just altered it. If you're on Humanity and you act against your beliefs you risk falling into wassail. If you're on a Path of Enlightenment and you act against your beliefs, you risk falling into wassail. It's the same conflict, it's just that someone on a Path and someone on Humanity have different beliefs. The risk and conflict and all of that are still fundamentally there though.<br /> <br /> So I don't think your Cal of Cthulhu comparison is terribly fair. To make the Call of Cthulhu comparison more accurate, rather than making the character <i>immune</i> to SAN lose, it would be like changing out the list of events that can cause a character to suffer SAN loss. So as you play the game your character is still at risk of losing SAN, and the results of losing SAN are the same, it's just that the things that cause the character to lose SAN are different than the default base list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T15:42:58-07:00","id":1450369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450352#post1450352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morality isn't as simple as &quot;beliefs go in, behavior comes out.&quot; People have empathy, intuitions, and social instincts that are not produced by specific social pressures or by philosophical convictions.<br /> <br /> That was the problem with the Paths of Enlightenment, they weren't actually paths you had to follow to progressively dismantle your humanity, they were a button you pressed in character creation to turn off the game's most fundamental conflict. It'd be like having an option in Call of Cthulhu to be cool with the Mythos and be immune to SAN loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how you play them, I like exploring the process of coverting to a path.<br /> <br /> Paths of Enlightenment are not too far from the concept of KotE's Dharmas. Messing up the conversion process results in either frenzying or wassailing, which implies to me that the vampire actually wassails and then comes out the other end still sane, clinging to the shreds of alien understanding beyond their reach at the beginning of a long and incredibly dangerous spiritual journey. Path followers have thrown away their humanity forever, they need to understand and cultivate their understanding of their spirituality and actively pursue it because they're closer to their beasts than any vampire with intact humanity could be. I don't remember there being rules for switching paths, and as ST I wouldn't allow it. This is your creed for eternity, become disilusioned with it and you're fucked.<br /> <br /> Roleplayed, this isn't just &quot;I do what I want&quot;, a vampire on a path must genuinely believe in and actively seek deeper understanding of it to even start on one.<br /> <br /> The conflict of the paths is the opposite of humanity. Humanity typically starts high-ish and you fight to keep it there, Enlightenment starts with you being one or two steps away from a mindless killing machine as you start clawing your way up from the bottom.<br /> <br /> Or that's how I interpret them, anyway.<br /> <br /> Besides, you don't <i>have</i> to focus on the human-beast conflict, even if it is &quot;the point&quot; or the artists' vision, it's a game we play for fun. There are other ways to have fun with the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-30-2021, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T16:45:49-07:00","id":1450373,"title":"","content":"I've never used the old mechanics for switching from humanity to a path in my game, mostly because I find the idea of the player randomly becoming a wight very dull. Instead, I've made it a pure roleplay thing. For example, a player wants to transition to Honorable Accord, and so has to hold to a series of sworn oaths to his teacher even when physically or emotionally painful. Being ordered to just stand there stoically while having his hand chopped off. Killing a friend from his human days. Everything designed to instill a sense of icy cold stoicism in the face of difficulties keeping your word.<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord is easily the easiest to do this with. The lessons are basically military discipline training combined with fraternity hazing, taken up a notch or three.<br /> <br /> Feral Heart is the next easiest. Half of it is instilling rank tribalism, a tribalism so extreme that it creates indifference to anything not immediately advantageous to the pack. The other half is about letting go of material concerns beyond immediate survival, rather like Diogenes.<br /> <br /> Path of Caine is basically just acting like an Honorable Accord mentor half the time, and a fundamentalist preacher the other half.<br /> <br /> Death and the Soul is fairly easy as well, since it is mostly about purging emotions. I can basically have mentors pontificate like a Vulcan while performing vivisections. Metamorphosis is similar, just with a few details changed.<br /> <br /> Past that it gets more difficult. I am aware that Power/Inner Voice is based off of Ayn Rand thinking, and I've slogged through 'The Fountainhead&quot;, but I confess that STing someone transitioning to this Path is something I've been mediocre at best at accomplishing. Cathari is a stuggle for me as well. Fortunately it doesn't often come up, as I usually start my games with characters already on their Paths, and it is up to them to bring it to life. Still, would love some advice on roleplaying mentors of characters seeking to switch to Power/Inner Voice or Cathari. I'm honestly at a loss when trying to roleplay an NPC mentoring someone in these two paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T21:46:24-07:00","id":1450393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450193#post1450193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be more accurate to say that he is against moral relativism. You can play a monster, but the mechanics will clearly frame you as evil and punish you for it. The idea that different species would have different ideas about right and wrong and that there would not be an objective answer that the universe punishes you for violating is repellent to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get much of a sense of moral absolutism from Justin Achilli. Part of the issue is that the central conflict of Vampire: The Masquerade isn't good vs. evil. It's Man versus Animal. The Beast is not evil. It is a creature that will eventually destroy your rational mind. It's a far more primal and elemental conflict of Civilization vs. Savage.<br /> <br /> And the Savage always wins.<br /> <br /> The Beast is a monster to be feared by all, including the Sabbat, because its a fate worse than death to become a wight. Not because you are evil but because you are simply NOT A PERSON anymore.<br /> <br /> You are just a creature that has no goals, thoughts, or aspirations. You kill, sleep, repeat.<br /> <br /> To quote Blade, &quot;The thirst always wins.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-31-2021, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T23:23:34-07:00","id":1450401,"title":"","content":"Eh, used to be that Diablerie was just murder and you'd roll for murder if you did it. Then in Revised you're sucking away a soul and not really knowing what you're doing with it and you automatically lose a dot of Humanity and most paths, roll for an additional humanity loss if the storyteller thinks you were particularly nasty during this act of canibalism, then maybe roll for addiction, which paradoxically doesn't work so well since the auto-humanity loss makes players extremely unwilling to commit too many diableries while their humanity is low.<br /> <br /> The &quot;it's just a murder&quot; stance seemed infinitly closer to the original intention for vampires; people who kill for power, not people who anguish over their lost humanity more than what is necessary for keeping their humane facade. <br /> <br /> The morality stance definetly changed for Revised. You can also see it in things like only humanity having a 'goldonda/enlightnment' stage or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-31-2021, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T00:00:23-07:00","id":1450406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450393#post1450393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't get much of a sense of moral absolutism from Justin Achilli. Part of the issue is that the central conflict of Vampire: The Masquerade isn't good vs. evil. It's Man versus Animal. The Beast is not evil. It is a creature that will eventually destroy your rational mind. It's a far more primal and elemental conflict of Civilization vs. Savage.<br /> <br /> And the Savage always wins.<br /> <br /> The Beast is a monster to be feared by all, including the Sabbat, because its a fate worse than death to become a wight. Not because you are evil but because you are simply NOT A PERSON anymore.<br /> <br /> You are just a creature that has no goals, thoughts, or aspirations. You kill, sleep, repeat.<br /> <br /> To quote Blade, &quot;The thirst always wins.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of the conflicts, one that has now overwhelmed and removed everything else. I mean now the central conflict is avoiding dice rolls at all costs, but hey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T00:03:21-07:00","id":1450407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450406#post1450406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the conflicts, one that has now overwhelmed and removed everything else. I mean now the central conflict is avoiding dice rolls at all costs, but hey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend watching a WIP to see how V5 should be played and you'll find it decidedly non-threatening.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T00:11:28-07:00","id":1450408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450407#post1450407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recommend watching a WIP to see how V5 should be played and you'll find it decidedly non-threatening.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have, LA By Night, it was...so insanely, stupifyingly boring it made me want to play less, and they did so much to avoid rolls, that at least was comedy, basically it looked like even the ST didn't want to make people roll for actions. Oh and they completely ignored what the Touchstones Rules actually say ofc. Oh and interactions relyed on player charisma and ability much more than character ofc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-31-2021, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T00:20:10-07:00","id":1450409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450408#post1450408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have, LA By Night, it was...so insanely, stupifyingly boring it made me want to play less, and they did so much to avoid rolls, that at least was comedy, basically it looked like even the ST didn't want to make people roll for actions. Oh and they completely ignored what the Touchstones Rules actually say ofc.</div> </div> </div> </div>They roll pretty much a normal amount of times for a game, IMHO. I think one thing this is illustrating is that V5 was meant to leave rolling for critical actions versus roleplay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T00:35:47-07:00","id":1450410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450409#post1450409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They roll pretty much a normal amount of times for a game, IMHO. I think one thing this is illustrating is that V5 was meant to leave rolling for critical actions versus roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> which hugely favours people who are good at social interactions, which replaces character skill with player skill, no thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T02:17:04-07:00","id":1450416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450409#post1450409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They roll pretty much a normal amount of times for a game, IMHO. I think one thing this is illustrating is that V5 was meant to leave rolling for critical actions versus roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is a 'right' amount of rolling. Some tables are all roleplay and narrative, and hence a form of storytelling; others are more game-like, and rolling dice is a big part of the tension there. Most games are somewhere in between.<br /> <br /> Some people don't like social interaction in-character for various reasons. They find it socially painful. Those players might rely on dice rolling more frequently.<br /> <br /> The only way I could get one neurodiverse player to join us was to allow him not to have to say anything IC and roll for all his social interactions instead.<br /> <br /> Such a player is not catered for if your system is 'try not to roll wherever possible'. He also really enjoys rolling dice, so there's that, too. <br /> <br /> Gamers can also be superstitious about their dice (putting them in the freezer, blowing on them, etc) and it's a big part of the gaming experience.<br /> <br /> Unless you actively design a diceless roleplaying game, you should accept that the right number of rolls is highly subjective, so your rules should work if you have lots of rolls as well as if you have fewer rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T09:00:22-07:00","id":1450456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450373#post1450373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never used the old mechanics for switching from humanity to a path in my game, mostly because I find the idea of the player randomly becoming a wight very dull. Instead, I've made it a pure roleplay thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I privately grade the player on their roleplay while they're still being mentored during their humanity days, then decide whether they survived the process based on that. A bad roll can spoil a lot of effort, so I'd say the roll determines how smoothly the process went. Do it perfectly and transition cleanly into your path, mess it up and spend time in control of the beast before your new sanity slowly puts itself into place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I confess that STing someone transitioning to this Path is something I've been mediocre at best at accomplishing. Cathari is a stuggle for me as well. Fortunately it doesn't often come up, as I usually start my games with characters already on their Paths, and it is up to them to bring it to life. Still, would love some advice on roleplaying mentors of characters seeking to switch to Power/Inner Voice or Cathari. I'm honestly at a loss when trying to roleplay an NPC mentoring someone in these two paths. </div> </div> </div>The way I would interpret these paths and the learning (hopefully this is coherent, because my thought processes tend to ramble):<br /> <br /> <u>Power and the Inner Voice</u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The student is here to learn absolute mastery of their own self and then how to exert this control over the world around them. And pursuit of power begins with power over oneself.<br /> Expect punishment, a lot.<br /> <br /> Make a point of illustrating every single tiny failure and flaw, and make sure that all of these are punished. From your student, from your lessers, from your superiors, from yourself. The message must be diven home: Fuck ups are never tolerated. <i>Ever.</i> Only when one is perfect can one acheive enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Wealthy victorians used to test the maids by putting coins under the rug. If the maid found the coins and didn't return them to the house owners, she was a thief and was fired. If she didn't find them she was incompetent, and was fired. Students can look forward to things like this, because the mentor will make mistakes on purpose to test that the student can spot them and will hold them responsible. Find a situation to illustrate how those who are not fit to lead can always be replaced.<br /> <br /> Give your students projects and responsibilities. Maybe grade them, or something. Reprimand them for missing an oportunity to advance. Point out where they went wrong. Point out and explain their mistakes, but do not give them advice on how to fix it, they must improve through their own understanding.<br /> <br /> Your student is to develop a keen insight into human behaviour and how to manipulate it. They'll learn how to use every emotion under the sun, and then they'll learn which ones matter. Fear, hate, desire.<br /> Illustrate through your lessons how love fades, how mere loyalty is bought and sold. And when the student finds their underlings have screwed up because of these things, punish them. If the underlings fail, it means that the superior has failed to control them adequately.<br /> <br /> Test that they understand they subtleties of what they are currently manipulating. Review their conduct. Question them, have them write essays or talk you through it or something. They will learn that to know how to manipulate you must know how the pieces fit together. The more you understand, the more you can manipulate, the more you can manipulate, the deeper your knowledge of creation runs and the closer you get to Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Stamp out weakness. Provide opportunities for them to discover their weaknesses, and make the punishment memorable so that it sticks out to them. Gaslight them. Smoke cigarettes in front of them and then put them out on their eye if they flinch from the flame. Break bones at random times, punish them again if they cry out. Teach them not to unintentionally make expressions or display body language. This will continue until the student has perfect control of their reactions at all times.<br /> The student is expected to start punishing themselves for mistakes too. If you can't recognise your flaws for what they are and demand better of yourself, you should not be here.<br /> <br /> But despite all this talk of punishment, do not punish if there's nothing to punish. Reward success adequately, but not to the degree that the student expects reward as a given. Unifiers are to seek power and enlightenment, not to indulge in meaningless sadism. This is your student, and you are responsible for them. If you cannot control their tutelage well enough to lead them to success, then that is <i>your</i> failure.</div></div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Path of Cathari</u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(Not one I typically allow except for NPCs.)<br /> All reasoning that leads you away from indulgence in vulgar material needs comes from the higher soul, which, as a servant of the demiurge and jailer of souls, you should not have. It deters vampires from their divinely ordained role, ergo they must learn to destroy that voice of higher reason in their head. Kill off sympathy, trust, adherance to expectations and laws of society.<br /> <br /> Learn your student's hangups and desires. Invade their privacy, gain their trust, then use what you've learned to errode their soul.<br /> <br /> The mentor will do what they want, take what they want, say what they want, all the second a whim pops into their head because there's nothing in there to tell them not to. They'll do anything to anything and anyone, ranging from the helpful to the innocuous to the mildly creepy and cruel to the utterly violating and monstrous, and then they'll probably move on and forget about it, because to them it's all no different than making a passing remark about the weather. Desire is desire. The Cathar experiences all their wants and whims as the same, with no distinction (they understand that others distinguish in degrees however, and know how to use it to their advantage, and in the education of their students)<br /> It's supposed to be degrading, it's supposed to be shaming. Your student must grow numb to these instincts of restraint through the acts of kindness and abuse you inflict on them (gnosis is a futile goal made for humans to seek, you are damned and don't need these things), and later learn how to inflict these lessons on others to fufill their duty.<br /> <br /> A student will learn betrayal. Test them often, betray them often in unexpected ways. Reward them for passing their tests with gifts that later turn out to be poisonous. Actually reward them sometimes, so they know not to trust in your predictability. Reward them for nothing at all. Expose them to the betrayals that others commit in the world, from the little things to the largest.<br /> <br /> Killing is the only thing the Cathar is forbidden from. I'd expect tests where the student is meant to kill somebody without remorse and is (without prior explanation) brutally punished. Then the mentor explains the fruitlessness of killing and how it unravels all the work put into their duty of corrupting them.<br /> <br /> The student will be abused until they are incapable of feeling shame, compassion and trust. They must learn not to give a damn about any reasons not to do what they want except for a direct threat to their existence (reincarnating will reset all they've learnt).<br /> On the plus side, a Cathar mentor will probably offer every luxury and indulgence you could dream of when they're not busy abusing you out of your mind. Or during.<br /> <br /> I'd also expect some conflict with the Setites, considering they're sort of heretical to each other.</div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-31-2021, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T10:03:22-07:00","id":1450462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450456#post1450456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I privately grade the player on their roleplay while they're still being mentored during their humanity days, then decide whether they survived t