ent, from your lessers, from your superiors, from yourself. The message must be diven home: Fuck ups are never tolerated. <i>Ever.</i> Only when one is perfect can one acheive enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Wealthy victorians used to test the maids by putting coins under the rug. If the maid found the coins and didn't return them to the house owners, she was a thief and was fired. If she didn't find them she was incompetent, and was fired. Students can look forward to things like this, because the mentor will make mistakes on purpose to test that the student can spot them and will hold them responsible. Find a situation to illustrate how those who are not fit to lead can always be replaced.<br /> <br /> Give your students projects and responsibilities. Maybe grade them, or something. Reprimand them for missing an oportunity to advance. Point out where they went wrong. Point out and explain their mistakes, but do not give them advice on how to fix it, they must improve through their own understanding.<br /> <br /> Your student is to develop a keen insight into human behaviour and how to manipulate it. They'll learn how to use every emotion under the sun, and then they'll learn which ones matter. Fear, hate, desire.<br /> Illustrate through your lessons how love fades, how mere loyalty is bought and sold. And when the student finds their underlings have screwed up because of these things, punish them. If the underlings fail, it means that the superior has failed to control them adequately.<br /> <br /> Test that they understand they subtleties of what they are currently manipulating. Review their conduct. Question them, have them write essays or talk you through it or something. They will learn that to know how to manipulate you must know how the pieces fit together. The more you understand, the more you can manipulate, the more you can manipulate, the deeper your knowledge of creation runs and the closer you get to Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Stamp out weakness. Provide opportunities for them to discover their weaknesses, and make the punishment memorable so that it sticks out to them. Gaslight them. Smoke cigarettes in front of them and then put them out on their eye if they flinch from the flame. Break bones at random times, punish them again if they cry out. Teach them not to unintentionally make expressions or display body language. This will continue until the student has perfect control of their reactions at all times.<br /> The student is expected to start punishing themselves for mistakes too. If you can't recognise your flaws for what they are and demand better of yourself, you should not be here.<br /> <br /> But despite all this talk of punishment, do not punish if there's nothing to punish. Reward success adequately, but not to the degree that the student expects reward as a given. Unifiers are to seek power and enlightenment, not to indulge in meaningless sadism. This is your student, and you are responsible for them. If you cannot control their tutelage well enough to lead them to success, then that is <i>your</i> failure.</div></div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Path of Cathari</u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(Not one I typically allow except for NPCs.)<br /> All reasoning that leads you away from indulgence in vulgar material needs comes from the higher soul, which, as a servant of the demiurge and jailer of souls, you should not have. It deters vampires from their divinely ordained role, ergo they must learn to destroy that voice of higher reason in their head. Kill off sympathy, trust, adherance to expectations and laws of society.<br /> <br /> Learn your student's hangups and desires. Invade their privacy, gain their trust, then use what you've learned to errode their soul.<br /> <br /> The mentor will do what they want, take what they want, say what they want, all the second a whim pops into their head because there's nothing in there to tell them not to. They'll do anything to anything and anyone, ranging from the helpful to the innocuous to the mildly creepy and cruel to the utterly violating and monstrous, and then they'll probably move on and forget about it, because to them it's all no different than making a passing remark about the weather. Desire is desire. The Cathar experiences all their wants and whims as the same, with no distinction (they understand that others distinguish in degrees however, and know how to use it to their advantage, and in the education of their students)<br /> It's supposed to be degrading, it's supposed to be shaming. Your student must grow numb to these instincts of restraint through the acts of kindness and abuse you inflict on them (gnosis is a futile goal made for humans to seek, you are damned and don't need these things), and later learn how to inflict these lessons on others to fufill their duty.<br /> <br /> A student will learn betrayal. Test them often, betray them often in unexpected ways. Reward them for passing their tests with gifts that later turn out to be poisonous. Actually reward them sometimes, so they know not to trust in your predictability. Reward them for nothing at all. Expose them to the betrayals that others commit in the world, from the little things to the largest.<br /> <br /> Killing is the only thing the Cathar is forbidden from. I'd expect tests where the student is meant to kill somebody without remorse and is (without prior explanation) brutally punished. Then the mentor explains the fruitlessness of killing and how it unravels all the work put into their duty of corrupting them.<br /> <br /> The student will be abused until they are incapable of feeling shame, compassion and trust. They must learn not to give a damn about any reasons not to do what they want except for a direct threat to their existence (reincarnating will reset all they've learnt).<br /> On the plus side, a Cathar mentor will probably offer every luxury and indulgence you could dream of when they're not busy abusing you out of your mind. Or during.<br /> <br /> I'd also expect some conflict with the Setites, considering they're sort of heretical to each other.</div></div> </div> </div></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons I love Paths so much! So much story potential right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T10:34:46-07:00","id":1450467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450462#post1450462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of the reasons I love Paths so much! So much story potential right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there really is! :-D And all of it erased by relegating the Sabbat to NPC status. :-(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T11:16:00-07:00","id":1450472,"title":"","content":"Just as a quick stab regarding the &quot;Sabbat players = vapid murderhoboes and edgelords&quot; angle:<br /> It's pretty funny to see Vampire players looking down on other Vampire players for their choice of sect or clan, considering Vampire players in general are considered &quot;edgelords&quot; by other RPG players...<br /> <br /> I started playing tabletop roleplaying games through a D&amp;D group. The D&amp;D players thought I was terribly &quot;edgy&quot;, what with the whole &quot;playing vampires&quot; thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:44:53-07:00","id":1450488,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just under half of my DnD characters were LE. I blame Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T06:31:47-07:00","id":1450583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450472#post1450472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a quick stab regarding the &quot;Sabbat players = vapid murderhoboes and edgelords&quot; angle:<br /> It's pretty funny to see Vampire players looking down on other Vampire players for their choice of sect or clan, considering Vampire players in general are considered &quot;edgelords&quot; by other RPG players...<br /> <br /> I started playing tabletop roleplaying games through a D&amp;D group. The D&amp;D players thought I was terribly &quot;edgy&quot;, what with the whole &quot;playing vampires&quot; thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>This, too. It's like, 'Play a monster, but not too monstrous.' And: 'Grapple with evil, but only in a very narrow, predefined way.'<br /> <br /> And then the books feature crass examples of how vampires do things like torture people for months to get minor bonuses on some rolls (Dyscrasias), how mortals can be used as crucibles for Thin Blood Alchemy (literally putting inorganic objects inside their bodies and causing all kinds of suffering) and how Brujah characters might include neo-Nazis who pretend to be alt-right, and that's all permissable subject matter, apparently. <br /> <br /> But not the Sabbat, because...Paths?<br /> <br /> Similarly, several people here have said that people who like playing Sabbat characters basically enjoy playing fascism or eating babies. The above-mentioned evil is apparently all fine, though, because it's done by the Camarilla and Anarchs, I guess.<br /> <br /> 'Yeah, maybe we're bad, but look at those *other* vampires over there! See how much worse they are? And you think we're edgelords? Check out this other group.'<br /> <br /> That sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T10:11:31-07:00","id":1450602,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there's any overlap between people who play vampire and people who like playing underdark races and similar. Maybe it's just me. I love them though and not just for the sake of being evil for evil's sake, but exploring exactly why they and their society work the way they do, and how they have their own vicious alien morality that formed from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-01-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T10:47:43-07:00","id":1450605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450583#post1450583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, too. It's like, 'Play a monster, but not too monstrous.' And: 'Grapple with evil, but only in a very narrow, predefined way.'<br /> <br /> And then the books feature crass examples of how vampires do things like torture people for months to get minor bonuses on some rolls (Dyscrasias), how mortals can be used as crucibles for Thin Blood Alchemy (literally putting inorganic objects inside their bodies and causing all kinds of suffering) and how Brujah characters might include neo-Nazis who pretend to be alt-right, and that's all permissable subject matter, apparently.<br /> <br /> But not the Sabbat, because...Paths?<br /> <br /> Similarly, several people here have said that people who like playing Sabbat characters basically enjoy playing fascism or eating babies. The above-mentioned evil is apparently all fine, though, because it's done by the Camarilla and Anarchs, I guess.<br /> <br /> 'Yeah, maybe we're bad, but look at those *other* vampires over there! See how much worse they are? And you think we're edgelords? Check out this other group.'<br /> <br /> That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the game's mechanics really assume you will take tenets in the Hallmark movie to Sin City range. Tenets can be anything, but creating ghouls always gives you stains. Tenets can be anything, but being a Farmer Pred gets you Humanity 8 and Allycat Pred gets you Humanity 6. Tenets can be anything, but your Touchstones have to be human. It all assumes very conventional tenets. You can do things to like the Dyscrasia stuff you mentioned, but the game will consider you wrong, and punish you karmically for it. A lot of their mechanics actually break if you don't pick conventional tenets.<br /> <br /> It was something I noticed immediately when trying to adapt the current system to Sabbat. It wasn't enough simply to use the Long Road Out Of Hell Sabbat faction tenets and Beast Marks system, though that was a tremendous, tremendous help. I had to drop the Predator types and replace it with simply giving everyone one more dot in their Clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I also dropped things like getting stains for creating ghouls and progeny, which I'm pleased to say hasn't created any of the problems you might expect. Players want to solve problems themselves. They don't want to watch a bunch of NPCs solve their problems for them, so giving them stains for creating ghouls and childer is a solution in search of a non-existent problem. Plus, creating a bunch of ghouls and childer has plenty of complications that don't require humanity, such as feeding them all, keeping them all from killing each other out of jealousy, problems the players are always keenly aware of, in addition to just not wanting to stand around waiting for the horde of NPCs they created to solve the problem for them.<br /> <br /> I'm digressing: the creators only want you to do stuff outside of conventional morality if they can punish you for it with humanity loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-01-2021, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T11:11:07-07:00","id":1450612,"title":"","content":"Fascism is fun when it's pure fantasy, that's where 90% of its appeal lies; fantasy. <br /> <br /> anyhow, I like my anarchs to be just as bad as the Cam. But V5 seems to go for team anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T11:22:07-07:00","id":1450615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450602#post1450602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there's any overlap between people who play vampire and people who like playing underdark races and similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's certainly some, but there's lots of other reactions.<br /> <br /> I know a lot of people that I mentally think of as &quot;setting extreme&quot; style players. Rather than necessarily being super into dark characters, they want to play exemplars of what the setting is about. If the setting is about daring heroes doing quests for the good of the fantasy-world? They're going to play the most morally upstanding, righteous, and just dealer of adventuring action there is. If they're playing in a setting about brooding monsters struggling with their nature, they want to dial their angst up to 11. If they're playing a character study in evil character, they're going to dive right at the most vile thing allowed.<br /> <br /> While a bit of an over-the-top explanation, it explains players I know that seem to always play things like Paladins in D&amp;D, but Sabbat in VtM. So the motivations here can sometimes lead to overlap, and sometimes to divergence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T12:01:11-07:00","id":1450620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450615#post1450615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's certainly some, but there's lots of other reactions.<br /> <br /> I know a lot of people that I mentally think of as &amp;quot;setting extreme&amp;quot; style players. Rather than necessarily being super into dark characters, they want to play exemplars of what the setting is about. If the setting is about daring heroes doing quests for the good of the fantasy-world? They're going to play the most morally upstanding, righteous, and just dealer of adventuring action there is. If they're playing in a setting about brooding monsters struggling with their nature, they want to dial their angst up to 11. If they're playing a character study in evil character, they're going to dive right at the most vile thing allowed.<br /> <br /> While a bit of an over-the-top explanation, it explains players I know that seem to always play things like Paladins in D&amp;D, but Sabbat in VtM. So the motivations here can sometimes lead to overlap, and sometimes to divergence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do Holy Warriors be that Paladin, War Priest or Inquisitor in Pathfinder, or Sabbat Honourable Accord or Caine in VtM","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T12:31:50-07:00","id":1450626,"title":"","content":"A paladin and a sabbat have a lot of similarities; Zealous adherence to dogma. Infact the Sabbat have their own Paladins... Ultra-lawful types are fun. <br /> <br /> A few stray thoughts in my head: <br /> There are probably a bunch of Vampire -Actual Nazis- that seem very much amused by the Neo-Nazi movements that've popped up in countries that fought the Nazis. <br /> <br /> If you were a Nazi (neo or otherwise) I think the embrace would really freshen up your perspective. Few Cainites remain athiests, and few are going to hold to the belief that communist-Jew-Lizards are responsible for the decadence of society when they've just been absorbed into the Actual-Fucking-Vampire conspiracy that's clearly the culprit, a few mage conspiracies nonwithstanding. You might still be really into hierarchies and boot-licking and all that, but you're definetly getting a new perspective on things. Especially as you move from angry-disaffected misfit into -the mastermind- territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T12:49:24-07:00","id":1450630,"title":"","content":"In any case, every version of vampire society is a variation on Feudalism. Camarilla are blatantly feudalistic. Anarchs are like the Barons who created the Magna Carta, or the those Aristocrats who wanted what they called &quot;democracy&quot; in ancient Greece and the &quot;Republic&quot; in ancient Rome, or the Aristocrats who created the pre-bill of rights version of American &quot;democracy&quot; and those who formed the Confederacy because they wanted a continuance of that early version of American &quot;democracy&quot;: they want rights for themselves, but still want to lord it over the peasants.<br /> <br /> Camarilla vs Anarch is a fight between a version of Feudalism with power mainly in the hands of the King and High Nobles versus a version of Feudalism where the Low Nobles have more collective power than the King and High Nobles. The Sabbat are the version of Feudalism where the Pope and those Crusader type nobles who serve the Pope have most of the power. But nobody in this is really in it for the peasants.<br /> <br /> Join the Confederacy feudalists, the Absolute Monarchy feudalists, the Papacy/Crusader feudalists, or just go it completely alone and be the enemy of all, those are your options as a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-01-2021, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T23:31:30-07:00","id":1450668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450605#post1450605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of the game's mechanics really assume you will take tenets in the Hallmark movie to Sin City range. Tenets can be anything, but creating ghouls always gives you stains. Tenets can be anything, but being a Farmer Pred gets you Humanity 8 and Allycat Pred gets you Humanity 6. Tenets can be anything, but your Touchstones have to be human. It all assumes very conventional tenets. You can do things to like the Dyscrasia stuff you mentioned, but the game will consider you wrong, and punish you karmically for it. A lot of their mechanics actually break if you don't pick conventional tenets.<br /> <br /> It was something I noticed immediately when trying to adapt the current system to Sabbat. It wasn't enough simply to use the Long Road Out Of Hell Sabbat faction tenets and Beast Marks system, though that was a tremendous, tremendous help. I had to drop the Predator types and replace it with simply giving everyone one more dot in their Clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I also dropped things like getting stains for creating ghouls and progeny, which I'm pleased to say hasn't created any of the problems you might expect. Players want to solve problems themselves. They don't want to watch a bunch of NPCs solve their problems for them, so giving them stains for creating ghouls and childer is a solution in search of a non-existent problem. Plus, creating a bunch of ghouls and childer has plenty of complications that don't require humanity, such as feeding them all, keeping them all from killing each other out of jealousy, problems the players are always keenly aware of, in addition to just not wanting to stand around waiting for the horde of NPCs they created to solve the problem for them.<br /> <br /> I'm digressing: the creators only want you to do stuff outside of conventional morality if they can punish you for it with humanity loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And as you point out, there's more than one way to skin a cat or introduce your players to consequences for their characters' actions. Humanity loss isn't the only consequence; there are Masquerade/Silence of the Blood breaches, reprisals from hunters and/or other supernaturals, punishments from one's elders or sect, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T08:19:30-07:00","id":1450823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450472#post1450472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a quick stab regarding the &quot;Sabbat players = vapid murderhoboes and edgelords&quot; angle:<br /> It's pretty funny to see Vampire players looking down on other Vampire players for their choice of sect or clan, considering Vampire players in general are considered &quot;edgelords&quot; by other RPG players...<br /> <br /> I started playing tabletop roleplaying games through a D&amp;D group. The D&amp;D players thought I was terribly &quot;edgy&quot;, what with the whole &quot;playing vampires&quot; thing...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it is pretty funny to see people who love V20 and hate v5 trah V5 on almost every chance they get in all threads. even those who has been just to ask a question about lore or getting a name for something. There is almost always one comment that tells people to play v20 instead. It could be made into a drinking game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not just on this forum, but all forums.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T08:36:05-07:00","id":1450824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450823#post1450823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it is pretty funny to see people who love V20 and hate v5 trah V5 on almost every chance they get in all threads. even those who has been just to ask a question about lore or getting a name for something. There is almost always one comment that tells people to play v20 instead. It could be made into a drinking game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not just on this forum, but all forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, what do you want? good advise is good advise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T09:09:30-07:00","id":1450830,"title":"","content":"V5 players be all like &quot;We can be at peace, we can co-exist, why you gotta be so hostile?&quot;<br /> And V20 players be all like &quot;you took everything from me, you threatened my family, you killed my father; prepare to die&quot; or some other mashup of what people say when attempting revenge.<br /> <br /> No really, A lot of people aren't just bitter because they don't like V5. they're bitter because V5 is going to influence future WoD products, and they desperately hope that by preaching their displeasure, they'll help course-correct the IP, so that more people can enjoy future products.<br /> <br /> Fact is V5 took away the Sabbat, something people liked, and what they're doing now might be some of the course correction they wanted, or it might be more of the problems they've feared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T09:34:47-07:00","id":1450834,"title":"","content":"Pretty much.<br /> And it doesn't matter that we can homerule, the fact that we need to homerule in the first place suggests that if one wants certain content in the future (such as the Sabbat) it will never be provided and the game in creation is never going to be something that really interests you. So why bother supporting it? There's a complete game that already offers that. I'm not a pure Sabbat player, I'd play anything, but between my already mixed feelings on the edition and the fact that the Sabbat are being taken out in the first place, it doesn't bode well to me. V5 has just diverged too far from my liking, I suppose. I'd still favour a blend of V20 with a less drastic V5 metaplot.<br /> <br /> That's probably where the &quot;just play V20&quot; comes from, more players that play V20 means a greater chance that the version of the setting others enjoy won't get cast aside into the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-03-2021, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T13:55:56-07:00","id":1450882,"title":"","content":"Not to mention... how many people learn roleplaying from buying a rulebook? Have you seen the size of those things? Non gamers blanch at a game with that many pages of just rules. I think you're mostly getting players of other rpgs doing that. Most people getting into roleplaying have it transmitted socally. They get it from people they are friendly with, like the clap.<br /> <br /> Other media is edition agnostic or neutral. If the majority of people keep playing V20, it out-reproduces V5, like a more virulent social disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T11:46:04-07:00","id":1450974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450612#post1450612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fascism is fun when it's pure fantasy, that's where 90% of its appeal lies; fantasy.<br /> <br /> anyhow, I like my anarchs to be just as bad as the Cam. But V5 seems to go for team anarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>No faction in vampire is fascist. Every faction is a variation on feudalism. For most of history, the big conflict was between the version of feudalism where the the low nobles had more collective power than the king and high nobles, and the version of feudalism where the king and high nobles had all the power. For a very long time, &quot;democracy&quot; and &quot;republic&quot; didn't mean what it means today.<br /> <br /> Both were really just words that meant that the low nobles had more collective power than the high nobles and king. Ancient Greece, the Roman Republic, Magna Carta era Britain, early America, and the Confederacy, were all forms of government where the low nobles had more collective power than the high nobles and the top guy. None of them were great places to live for peasants and slaves. All of them were inline with what the &quot;Anarchs&quot; actually represent. Hell, the Anarchs even name their leaders &quot;Barons&quot; as an homage to the Magna Carta Barons.<br /> <br /> Imperial Rome, the various Absolute Monarchies that sprung up in the late Middle Ages, and indeed most Empires with a famous leader, were the form of feudalism where the King(or equivalent) and a few high nobles had all the power, and the low nobles were, depending on the era, poor farmers with the ability to tax a few even poorer farmers, or moderately wealthy people with no real political power. Not a great place to be a peasant or slave. And this is the Camarilla's inspiration.<br /> <br /> Regardless, neither group was &quot;fascist&quot;, though the various low-nobles-have-more-collective-power-than-the-king versions has just as much claim to resembling fascism as the king-and-high-nobles-have-all-the-power versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-05-2021, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T13:04:01-07:00","id":1450976,"title":"","content":"Fascism isn't a system of goverment, it's a set of ideas that can accompany any kind of government. There's no fascist ideal for monetary policy or an idea of if Fascists should use a Prime Minister/President/Chancelor/King as the head of state. It's purely a social issue (which is often used to hide an economic one) <br /> <br /> Similarly, Fuedalism's a bit of a neologism and really describes a lot of types of goverment that seem similar from our modern perspective, but wouldn't be seen as the same from people living under &quot;fuedalism&quot; <br /> <br /> The Sabbat are fascist, or at least 3/5 of them are fascist; Uniting for the cause, Everyone not with us is against us, &quot;we're supreme and our enemies are weak but also they are a huge threat but if we just band together and rise up...&quot; Yeah. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla and Anarchs are almost the exact same thing; Both have the capacity to be very 'hands off' and both have the capacity to be extremely dogmatic. The Anarchs just have a younger flavour, and are the underdogs, and their defining seperation is that they don't hold traditions sacred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T17:12:01-07:00","id":1450996,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about what they mean when they say that Paths have to be followed more fanatically to work, and I think they mean that Sabbat will not have any Touchstones at all, of any sort. If you violate one of the Chronicle Tenets, Tenets which will be mono-path-centric, you just eat the stains. Which makes a kind of sense, I'll admit, but is also rather a bland solution.<br /> <br /> Like a Feral Heart chronicle Tenets might be: &quot;Always be loyal to your Packmates. Do not engage in politics. Do not kill for reasons other than food or survival.&quot; and if you violate any of those, you just eat the full stains, since you can never have a human touchstone rooted conviction to mitigate it.<br /> <br /> It makes sense for characters who avoid the beast purely via fanatical purity to a set of beliefs, but it's rather bland. The price for being on a Path will likely be a throwback to the old version, where you look like you have a Humanity of 3 even if you have a Path rating of 10.<br /> <br /> It also explains WHY they insist on mono-path packs: because the Tenets are meant to be followed by all players, and the Tenets need to be tailored to a particular Path. The only way you could really create a multi-path tenet is by referencing older editions, like, &quot;avoid all 10 sins of your chosen Path&quot;, which would require someone knowing all ten sins from older editions.<br /> <br /> I actually do have several Paths memorized, and behave as if my characters had &quot;avoid all 10 sins of your chosen Path&quot; as one of my convictions even when it's officially not, but I can see why they would want to avoid making players memorize older editions. You have to REALLY love Paths to my degree to do this.<br /> <br /> I get it, I really do, but I find it all rather bland. I think I'll keep using Long Road Out Of Hell if I'm right about this. I like my nonhuman touchstones, and I like my Beast Marks, and having it replaced with just &quot;here are three Tenets rooted in one path, you have no touchstones of any sort, and you always look like you've got Humanity 3 even if you have Path rating 10&quot;, is sooooo much blander than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T04:23:12-07:00","id":1451038,"title":"","content":"That would give the packs flavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T05:02:34-07:00","id":1451042,"title":"","content":"The thing is, people all want to play different paths in every Sabbat game I've ever run. I'll get, like, one Power/Inner person, a couple of Cathari, a Feral Hearter, a Metamorphisist, even had one secret Lilith follower recently. Trying to tell people they all have to play one path would go over about as well as that time I tried to run a D&amp;D game where everyone was a Pugilist. I had an idea for a wandering boxing show campaign. Did not go over well. Never got enough people for even one game. People wanna play what they wanna play. I doubt I could get a group together if I insisted on everyone being on one path, and I don't really want to try. I like people being on different paths, and all the drama this creates. A monopath pack is one of those ideas clearly intended for NPCs only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T05:23:28-07:00","id":1451043,"title":"","content":"If you wanted a monopath pack, you could already do that. You just didn't <i>have</i> to, because you could also have the potential conflict of multiple ideologies in a pack for a change of pace.<br /> <br /> I feel like tenets just can't do the paths of enlightenment justice, the hierarchy is important in illustrating your growing understanding of the path itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-05-2021, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T12:17:26-07:00","id":1451071,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I get where they are likely coming from with the absence of touchstones/convictions. Convictions are supposed to represent past humanity and that's been stomped out of Sabbat crusaders. They've gained the ability to use Path tenets, tenets that are somewhat more forgiving than humanity tenets, but they've lost any ability to mitigate stains via Convictions. They need to hold to their Path Tenets like iron, because they eat stains full in the face when they don't.<br /> <br /> To go back to my earlier example about a Feral Heart pack. Let's say you had a pack whose tenets were &quot;Always be loyal to your Packmates. Do not engage in politics. Do not kill for reasons other than food or survival.&quot;<br /> <br /> Members of that pack can suck humans dry so long as they have at least one point of hunger when they do so. Humans are food, you need to kill them to fully sate your hunger, so drink away. Sounds much easier than Humanity, right? On the other hand, let's say you have ambitions to rise to leadership in the Sabbat. So you engage in a bit of political scheming to do so. On Humanity, you might be able to have a Gorden Gekko type as your Touchstone for the conviction, &quot;power is worth any price&quot; and reduce the stains from engaging in politics. Not for Sabbat. You just eat full stains.<br /> <br /> Of course, all this is me doing an awful lot of reading between the lines of what they've been saying. But it does fit with their general design philosophy that rather than do something sophisticated, they do something extremely simple. And &quot;they get Tenets that are a little more forgiving, but completely lose access to the Conviction mechanic&quot; is as simple as it gets.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T18:49:28-07:00","id":1451092,"title":"","content":"What I don't get with all this is the whole premise that Sabbat is = evil.<br /> <br /> I mean, in Revised edition and V20, it was stated over and over <i>that most Sabbat vampires are not on a Path of Enlightenment. </i><br /> <br /> As I player who began in Revised edition, I loved the Sabbat because it was <i>a more interesting ideological and political structure than the Camarilla. </i>It was like a bizarre fundamentalist warlord army about to turn on itself, a dysfunctional death cult with pseudo-democratic trappings run on a social darwinist platform, with an old testament:y jihadist doomsday sect hidden within. It was so insanely f*ing compelling. Even at pack level, the Sabbat had a much more interesting structure and internal culture than the Camarilla, with their vaulderies, ductuses and pack priests - the Sabbat packs had a clear reason for existing, whereas Camarilla coteries always felt kinda pointless and forced. <i>The Sabbat was designed so that its core structure was a tight-knit yet conflict-ridden </i><i>group of bizarre and motley player characters. </i>Can we just dwell for a moment on how genius an idea that was?<br /> <br /> To just add to the giant sm\u00f6rg\u00e5sbord of awesomeness that was the Guide to the Sabbat, it was complemented by Mexico City by Night. The Sabbat's capital was what is basically the best city for Vampire chronicles in the entire contemporary world - Mexico City is both gargantuan, shock full of history and local culture, downtrodden yet vibrant, shabby yet sophisticated, corrupt, crime-ridden, extremely violent, a literally drug war going on in the streets...what an amazing place for Vampire play.<br /> <br /> I always imagined that Camarilla elders could be just as monstrous as Sabbat ones, and in a way, were even more monstrous, because they ran the Camarilla, a giant pyramid scheme meant to forever deceive its lower ranking members and rob them of all influence. The Sabbat at least had some elders who truly believed that what they were doing were for the good of all of Vampirekind.<br /> <br /> I really like a lot about V5. I love the rules, and several of the changes to the world were brave and clever. But the Revised edition Sabbat was a friggin' masterpiece of worldbuilding. The Sabbat was <i>so</i> dynamic, complex and compelling. I just can't understand why you would ruin something so great, but it increasingly seems to be what V5 has done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 06-05-2021, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T19:35:28-07:00","id":1451097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451092#post1451092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't get with all this is the whole premise that Sabbat is = evil.<br /> <br /> I mean, in Revised edition and V20, it was stated over and over <i>that most Sabbat vampires are not on a Path of Enlightenment. </i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Most of what you talked about I have no answer for. But I can give you a pretty good guess as to this one: they are seeking to strip each sect down to its defining features.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla have always been the royal elites, but previously tried to be a big tent that included everyone. Now they are shameless about being a small, exclusive club of royals and those who seek royal favor.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat were always controlled by fanatical path-followers, but pretended to be a big tent where you could have humanity so long as you weren't preachy about it and followed orders no matter how brutal. Now they are packs of fanatics each following quasi-religious paths with with utter devotion, accept other packs only as loose allies, and don't accept humanity at all past a brief indoctrination period where you had best learn fast and get with the program or be destroyed.<br /> <br /> I think they also want the game to be about small scale survival horror, so big institutions in general were destroyed. You're not part of some big organization. You're a tiny creature with lots of weaknesses who struggles just to survive night to night. You're most likely an Anarch, which now seems to be the default, and you barely know what you are. You have to live extremely quietly, lest the smug, paranoid royals kill you because they deem you a threat to their only slightly less fragile existences, or vampire hunters discover you and kill you very, very casually.<br /> <br /> You're discouraged from being Camarilla, but if you insist on playing one, you are still tiny, tiny, tiny. The little bit of wealth and comfort you've managed to accumulate could be wiped out in a moment if the surveillance state peering over everyone's shoulder discovers who you are. You are constantly endangered not only by your own mistakes, but by the mistakes of anarchs who bring surveillance down on your territory with their clumsiness and ignorance. And if you beg them to be quiet and cautious, they act like you are the second coming of Hitler and attack you for it, forcing you to attack them in return.<br /> <br /> You're VERY discouraged from playing Sabbat, but if you insist on playing one, you are still tiny, tiny, tiny. You are not allowed to have any human friends, and must adopt a Path of Enlightenment quickly or be executed by your own Sect. The Paths are hard to follow, and since you aren't allowed human touchstones, you eat full stains for the slightest transgression, making the threat of becoming a wight constant and oppressive.<br /> <br /> The result is an extremely low-power survival horror game regardless of Sect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T01:45:09-07:00","id":1451121,"title":"","content":"The Cam's pretty dumb this edition.<br /> <br /> The main issue is that vampires, even the Anarchs, are still pretty elite as far as humans are concerned. You're 1 in 100,000, you can easily acquire a decent business or a harem of fanatical slaves if you're so inclined. V5 changes the dynamics of fringe-types VS the establishment to poor liberal vs wealthy republican, which is horrifically half-baked given that we're talking about low grade millionaires VS high grade millionaires. The cam giving up on so many is a confusing issue because how the fuck do they give up on someone? Is this the inner circle deciding to abandon cities or princes deciding some people aren't members and thus forcing them into becoming his opposition, meaning the prince is certainly using the SI to kill them... <br /> <br /> Not a viable plan. You don't need to be a hundred year old ancilae to work out that it's actually a terrible plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T11:27:33-07:00","id":1451153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451121#post1451121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cam's pretty dumb this edition.<br /> <br /> The main issue is that vampires, even the Anarchs, are still pretty elite as far as humans are concerned. You're 1 in 100,000, you can easily acquire a decent business or a harem of fanatical slaves if you're so inclined. V5 changes the dynamics of fringe-types VS the establishment to poor liberal vs wealthy republican, which is horrifically half-baked given that we're talking about low grade millionaires VS high grade millionaires. The cam giving up on so many is a confusing issue because how the fuck do they give up on someone? Is this the inner circle deciding to abandon cities or princes deciding some people aren't members and thus forcing them into becoming his opposition, meaning the prince is certainly using the SI to kill them...<br /> <br /> Not a viable plan. You don't need to be a hundred year old ancilae to work out that it's actually a terrible plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it effectively makes the Cam a secret conspiracy of the rich who assassinate any outsider they consider even a slight risk to the masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T12:53:31-07:00","id":1451160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451153#post1451153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it effectively makes the Cam a secret conspiracy of the rich who assassinate any outsider they consider even a slight risk to the masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they aren't secret, The Sabbat and Anarchs must have been force fed the idiot ball to not jump into the power vacuum the Camarilla opened up by withdrawal, and starting to stack heads, plus why did all those abandoned ex Cam not invited suddenly become Anarchs? Like that is a semi cohesive Sect now, with titles and obligations, why not peace out, take the reins that have been dropped and do your own thing? The Sabbat have run away to degenerate into 2d cartoons of themselves, the Anarchs didn't seem interested in moving in force, and the Independents don't exist anymore....They either schismed into powerlessness, joined a sect, or are so fundamentally changed as to not be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T13:11:57-07:00","id":1451162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451042#post1451042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, people all want to play different paths in every Sabbat game I've ever run. I'll get, like, one Power/Inner person, a couple of Cathari, a Feral Hearter, a Metamorphisist, even had one secret Lilith follower recently. Trying to tell people they all have to play one path would go over about as well as that time I tried to run a D&amp;D game where everyone was a Pugilist. I had an idea for a wandering boxing show campaign. Did not go over well. Never got enough people for even one game. People wanna play what they wanna play. I doubt I could get a group together if I insisted on everyone being on one path, and I don't really want to try. I like people being on different paths, and all the drama this creates. A monopath pack is one of those ideas clearly intended for NPCs only.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my previous Sabbat campaign, and the one before that, the players sat down on session zero to design the pack and their characters. I only described the city they were in and what type of campaign i wanted to run they said their wishes and when creating character they decided both times upon packs that followed 1 pack only. It wa all player decided i only supplied rules and lore so that they could mae ther characters.<br /> <br /> I have nothing gainst momopack. i actually find that really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T13:15:28-07:00","id":1451163,"title":"","content":"The Cam Prince: You guys are out, Oh there's some hunters out there that're only going to hunt you but surely they have nothing to do with me. <br /> The New Anarchs: Oh he wants us all to die. He also gave us all the Brujah for some reason. Well I guess the prince might win if we spend a lot of time fighting over who gets to diablerise him, oh wait Diablerie is shit now, GRIGORI, BUILD THE GUILOTINE. <br /> <br /> -Why there's no cam in V6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T14:27:01-07:00","id":1451169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451163#post1451163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cam Prince: You guys are out, Oh there's some hunters out there that're only going to hunt you but surely they have nothing to do with me.<br /> The New Anarchs: Oh he wants us all to die. He also gave us all the Brujah for some reason. Well I guess the prince might win if we spend a lot of time fighting over who gets to diablerise him, oh wait Diablerie is shit now, GRIGORI, BUILD THE GUILOTINE.<br /> <br /> -Why there's no cam in V6.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is that your life is too tiny and fragile for things to go down like that. If you're part of a tiny group of vampires who scramble to get blood and avoid hunters every night, the idea of getting a huge group together and waging war on someone in a skyscrapper with multiple well-armed ghouls isn't really a thing for you. If you ARE the guy in the skyscrapper, things are a little better for you, but you need to protect the masquerade even harder lest you find your bank-accounts frozen by the government. So if you hear about some lowbies threatening the masquerade, you're going to want to eliminate them as quickly and quietly as possible, because your existence is so fragile. The result is that there are no &quot;Sects&quot; as previously understood. There are some rich guys quietly conspiring to eliminate threats to their fragile existence, and some poor people too weak and fragile to do any more than deal with the problem of the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T00:45:30-07:00","id":1451189,"title":"","content":"As weak as V5 vampires are that's a hilarious underestimation of their strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T08:24:55-07:00","id":1451214,"title":"","content":"How weak are the Vampires in V5 ? I'm mostly a Requiem player (even if my first contact with WoD was a PBF of Sabbats vs Camarilla and I picked up the latter). I always had the impression that vampires were a lot stronger (too much for me) in Mascarade, compared to Requiem with Disciplines really over-powered. Have they equalized the powerscale ? Because Kindred in Requiem feel powerful enough to be almost untouchable if they want to and have pursued said goal, at least to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T09:09:15-07:00","id":1451218,"title":"","content":"I'd say your average non-elder is half as powerful as they would be in V20. This is confounded by the &quot;difficulties&quot; of rolls in V5, where having 4 dice means you're going to need to spend willpower to reliably complete normal tasks. Elders are monumentally weaker in V5, barely functional with blood potency working the way it does.<br /> <br /> Some reasoning.<br /> 3 dots of V20 Auspex gives you what would be 6 dots of V5 Auspex.<br /> 3 dots of V20 Dominate gives you more than you can get with 5 dots of V5 Dominate<br /> 3 dots of V20 Obfuscate gives you more than what you can get with 5 dots of V5 obfuscate.<br /> V20 Potence and Celerity are just way, way, way stronger. V20 Potence would break V5 combat, nevermind celerity, which breaks v20 combat. V5 equivalents of these powers are hyper-specific things, more like werewolf gifts than vampire disciplines.<br /> <br /> Elders cannot gain more than 5 dots of a discipline in V5, while they can in V20, and blood potency is a terrible boost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Still, there's no reason why the Anarchs wouldn't be able to also hire a bunch of humans or use bombs or whatever to take out the Camarilla aggressors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T09:38:15-07:00","id":1451225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451214#post1451214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How weak are the Vampires in V5 ? I'm mostly a Requiem player (even if my first contact with WoD was a PBF of Sabbats vs Camarilla and I picked up the latter). I always had the impression that vampires were a lot stronger (too much for me) in Mascarade, compared to Requiem with Disciplines really over-powered. Have they equalized the powerscale ? Because Kindred in Requiem feel powerful enough to be almost untouchable if they want to and have pursued said goal, at least to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re not weak. However, Requiem 2e frontloads more power onto them, particularly in the disciplines. V5 also levels the playing field somewhat between young and old vampires, to finally make the eternal struggle and the mutual fear between young and old make sense, whereas previous editions tried to tell us the old feared the young while also portraying them all as untouchable blood gods the young would never be able to challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:24:31-07:00","id":1451232,"title":"","content":"Nah, you could totally challenge the &quot;blood gods&quot; in prior editions<br /> 1-You outnumber them a hundred to one.<br /> 2- Good planning<br /> 3- Good equipment. Modern technology is amazing technology. You've got more Dakka and Ka-Boom-Boom than the elders ever had.<br /> <br /> V5 actually makes the struggle between young and old kinda pointless. You've got to wonder why the SABBAT even try. Diablerizing your way down to Caine is a really, really, really terrible idea, because the power gain is minimal and the eternal hunger you'll gain is just not worth it. If we use rules, The Antideluvians are just going to be slightly nastier elders, so all these fears of Gehenna are comical. With the young unwilling to diablerise for a leg-up, the elders have no reason to fear them trying to rise up for their blood, and there's no good reason to oppress the neonates with stick rather than offer plentiful carrot; the Jyhad is a joke.<br /> But really, this discussion belongs in another thread. Still, it has some relevancy; the Sabbat really don't fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:26:14-07:00","id":1451234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451214#post1451214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How weak are the Vampires in V5 ? I'm mostly a Requiem player (even if my first contact with WoD was a PBF of Sabbats vs Camarilla and I picked up the latter). I always had the impression that vampires were a lot stronger (too much for me) in Mascarade, compared to Requiem with Disciplines really over-powered. Have they equalized the powerscale ? Because Kindred in Requiem feel powerful enough to be almost untouchable if they want to and have pursued said goal, at least to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fair to say that VTR2e vampires appear stronger at the start than V20 or V5 ones, due to their Disciplines and innate advantages. V20 ones clearly win out at elder levels, however. V5 ones are the weakest of the three, comparatively speaking.<br /> <br /> Compare, for example, Protean 1 between VTR2e and V20, and you'll notice right away that its first dot is equivalent to Protean 3 in V20. So that makes Requiem look more powerful off the bat.<br /> <br /> Requiem also has Kindred Senses and Lashing Out as default abilities, which add a boost. <br /> <br /> However, strictly speaking, the slightly lower dice pools and (usually) higher target number (always 8 in VTR2e; usually 6 in V20) also skews things somewhat.<br /> <br /> V20's blood buffs last for a scene and can go really high if you don't mind spending blood over multiple turns, where the bonus in VTR2e is fleeting and much smaller. V20 powers also cost less blood on the whole, since many are free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T12:13:22-07:00","id":1451241,"title":"","content":"Some clarification, as I think about it in more detail:<br /> <br /> As of 2e, Requiem vampires can lash out and have keen senses by default. The latter is a small thing, but it\u2019s cool and I wouldn\u2019t have minded V5 swiping it. Their disciplines are also designed differently, in that you tend to get the main power upfront and add to and refine it with subsequent dots. The first dot of any discipline in Requiem is a much bigger deal than the equivalent in Masquerade, where you might have to get to the 2nd or 3rd dot to do something similar (as mentioned above). <br /> <br /> As of V5, Masquerade vampires are physically a little bit harder to kill, with very little that causes them aggravated damage (V5 doesn\u2019t distinguish between bashing and lethal) and no chance of instantly killing them without it. They also are not subject to fear frenzy from small fires, which is a nice change. Their ability to rouse the beast to add to attributes is somewhat more generous, as it applies to *any* attribute, not just physical ones. Their blush of life is also more generous, lasting the whole night instead of a scene. Discipline-wise, again, the design is significantly different, with V5\u2019s disciplines being collections of similarly-themed powers rather than refinements of a single core power. They\u2019re more versatile and variable but not as potent as the ones in Requiem, at least not upfront. <br /> <br /> Unlike Requiem, V5 limits all traits at 5 dots and doesn\u2019t allow bloodlines to have unique disciplines, though you can see in 2e Requiem is already moving away from the latter. This may make elders appear weaker in V5 if one\u2019s only understanding of elder strength is having disciplines over 5 dots, but in reality they have a wide and unpredictable range of powers, bonus dice to use and resist disciplines, faster healing, more bonus dice to attributes when rousing the beast, and a greater ability to do all those things without increasing hunger (which means they can do more of them at one time and/or keep it up for longer). In effect it\u2019s not that different from what you see in Requiem\u2019s elders, except with greater unpredictability because of how the dice and hunger system works, so that it\u2019s possible for a Masquerade elder to use disciplines and heal and add to attributes nonstop without ever running out of power during the scene). They\u2019re operating on the same scale as neonates but are generally much better at everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-07-2021, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T12:34:28-07:00","id":1451243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1450830#post1450830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 players be all like &amp;quot;We can be at peace, we can co-exist, why you gotta be so hostile?&amp;quot;<br /> No really, A lot of people aren't just bitter because they don't like V5. they're bitter because V5 is going to influence future WoD products, and they desperately hope that by preaching their displeasure, they'll help course-correct the IP, so that more people can enjoy future products.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is in fact the textbook rationale behind all edition-warring. The reality, though, is that internet trolls have never course-corrected jack shit. The only thing the constant harping and negativity accomplishes is making online spaces unpleasant to participate in and turning the fandom in general into a toxic cesspool that turns away people who might have otherwise wanted to be a part of it. The only reason anyone actually thinks it works is because certain online spaces become echo-chambers once those who don\u2019t agree with them have been driven away. And then they path themselves on the back and say they\u2019ve changed the world...<br /> <br /> As to your other statement above: It\u2019s true, the Sabbat are absolutely fascist. And there is some interesting narrative space there, though it\u2019s hard to do it from *within* the group in question, as fascism, for many of us, is never entirely fantastical. And I don\u2019t blame WW for not wanting to say, \u201cHey, come play this violent supremacist cult that bears a strong resemblance to various groups that might be making your real life a lot more scary right now.\u201d They should be part of the overall picture, but I get them not being the focus (unless players really want them to be, in which case nobody\u2019s stopping them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T13:11:45-07:00","id":1451247,"title":"","content":"Ya...I don't run my Sabbat games as facists...I run them as movie monsters. Ala Lost Boys or Near Dark. So maybe they should just stick to the fantasy part of this game and less trying to insert it into the real world...lol just my 2 cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T13:26:23-07:00","id":1451250,"title":"","content":"All vampire societies are feudalist. All of them have elements that echo fascism. The Anarchs are the same variation on feudalism that produced the Confederacy and John Wilkes Booth unironically shouting &quot;<b>Sic semper tyrannis</b>&quot; for chrissakes. The eternal struggle between High Nobles and Low Nobles is not a fight for freedom, no matter how much the Low Nobles try to pretend it is. Both groups of nobles are fine with lording it over the peasants and slaves, always have been.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are just the variation on feudalism that allows you to explore what it is to be a different species via Paths of Enlightenment. They are the variation on feudalism that mainly serves the Papacy, but unlike what inspired them they allow a great deal of freedom of choice on paths, just so long as the path has been modified to include loyalty to the Sabbat itself, which is the main difference between the Paths and the old Roads. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T13:48:35-07:00","id":1451252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451243#post1451243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing the constant harping and negativity accomplishes is making online spaces unpleasant to participate in and turning the fandom in general into a toxic cesspool that turns away people who might have otherwise wanted to be a part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>5th Edition D&amp;D says hello; it was an absolute course-correction/authorial saving throw back towards older styles of play after 4E and that certainly would not have happened without all the pushback (and Paizo providing an alternate outlet for fans of older style play via Pathfinder).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T13:53:07-07:00","id":1451255,"title":"","content":"Well we don't get to see Sales Figures. Its very possible that V5 is performing really well and in fact is out selling V20. We don't know. Anyone saying they do is just guessing really. If V5 was performing badly...you would probably see a course correction with a new edition. Since companies like money, and that's really the driving factor here. <br /> <br /> For me? I wish there was a pathfinder option they (Paradox) allowed. So all play styles and desires were welcome in the current era. Besides market confusion...I never understood why paradox simply didn't allow say Onyx Path to continue to produce &quot;V20&quot; material; as it would just be another source of revenue for them and thus more money. But maybe I'm wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T14:17:35-07:00","id":1451257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451255#post1451255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we don't get to see Sales Figures. Its very possible that V5 is performing really well and in fact is out selling V20. We don't know. Anyone saying they do is just guessing really. If V5 was performing badly...you would probably see a course correction with a new edition. Since companies like money, and that's really the driving factor here. <br /> <br /> For me? I wish there was a pathfinder option they (Paradox) allowed. So all play styles and desires were welcome in the current era. Besides market confusion...I never understood why paradox simply didn't allow say Onyx Path to continue to produce &quot;V20&quot; material; as it would just be another source of revenue for them and thus more money. But maybe I'm wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same reason previous editions are killed off, even loosing people in the transition is better than having to compete with the previous editions for new customers.<br /> <br /> If Pathfinder hadn't happened, 5e DnD never would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T14:22:03-07:00","id":1451258,"title":"","content":"Ya I mean I guess my point was..using this anology...Wizards could have made all that Pazio money. Difference here is Paradox could avoid that mistake and just also make that money as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T21:31:51-07:00","id":1451282,"title":"","content":"The WoD fanbase is already split between the World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness. I can understand Paradox not wanting to split the fanbase a second time into WoD, V20, and Chronicles. And as Frederick Wester (the CEO of Paradox) said on day one about the acquisition, \u201cWe\u2019re going to start licensing out the brand again from the beginning. We\u2019ll start with one World of Darkness. We\u2019ll start, basically, from day one to unite the community under one flag.\u201d Further splitting up the fanbase would go against their most basic goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451255#post1451255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we don't get to see Sales Figures. Its very possible that V5 is performing really well and in fact is out selling V20. We don't know. Anyone saying they do is just guessing really. If V5 was performing badly...you would probably see a course correction with a new edition. Since companies like money, and that's really the driving factor here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not. Sometimes a company decides to stick with something for awhile figuring people will start coming around, especially if it's early on. 4th edition D&amp;D lasted for 6 years (2008-2014), most of which it spend being outsold by Pathfinder (which was basically the old 3rd edition). Even if 5th edition is not doing great in comparison to older editions, it's probably doing 'well enough' since it's Paradox's first foray into the TTRPG field. And Paradox is no doubt hoping that upcoming content (like the Bloodlines game and others) will start pulling people into 5th edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-08-2021, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T00:32:39-07:00","id":1451287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451241#post1451241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of V5, Masquerade vampires are physically a little bit harder to kill, with very little that causes them aggravated damage (V5 doesn\u2019t distinguish between bashing and lethal) and no chance of instantly killing them without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true and goes back to VTM1e's approach, IIRC. I've basically pinched it for my V20 games: you can only die if your HLs are full of aggravated damage and you take one or more additional levels of aggravated damage. V20DA has some neat changes to make vampires a bit tougher too (e.g., if all your HLs are only full of bashing damage, you only count as Crippled).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They also are not subject to fear frenzy from small fires, which is a nice change. </div> </div> </div>RAW and RAI, you only test in V20 if the small fire poses a threat--e.g., if someone waves a cigarette near your face. Though this is a common assumption people make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their ability to rouse the beast to add to attributes is somewhat more generous, as it applies to *any* attribute, not just physical ones. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you get the bonus for one roll only--not even for the whole turn. In V20 you keep any buffs up to your Generational maximum +1 for a whole scene, and can bump stats up beyond that (max. 10) for three turns after you stop spending blood. (This is costly, yes, but more efficient than Blood Surge in most cases.)<br /> <br /> Yes, in V5 you can spend the blood to gain bonus dice on any Attribute, but as others have noted on other threads, for elders this is a poor substitute for traits over five to begin with. Compare and contrast pre-V5 Helena and V5 Helena for example. One is epic all the time; the other is epic for brief moments when she spends blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their blush of life is also more generous, lasting the whole night instead of a scene. </div> </div> </div>This is a good bonus for V5. Though, the stronger Disciplines and Bearing modifiers in V20 mean Blush of Health isn't as necessary.<br /> <br /> I like the flexibility of Bearings, though. E.g., you might get a bonus to Stealth if you follow the right Path, and that may be more fitting for your character concept than being a wolf in sheep's clothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Discipline-wise, again, the design is significantly different, with V5\u2019s disciplines being collections of similarly-themed powers rather than refinements of a single core power. They\u2019re more versatile and variable but not as potent as the ones in Requiem, at least not upfront. <br /> <br /> Unlike Requiem, V5 limits all traits at 5 dots and doesn\u2019t allow bloodlines to have unique disciplines, though you can see in 2e Requiem is already moving away from the latter. This may make elders appear weaker in V5 if one\u2019s only understanding of elder strength is having disciplines over 5 dots, but in reality they have a wide and unpredictable range of powers, bonus dice to use and resist disciplines, faster healing, more bonus dice to attributes when rousing the beast, and a greater ability to do all those things without increasing hunger (which means they can do more of them at one time and/or keep it up for longer). </div> </div> </div>I feel this is possibly misleading. Yes, elders, like neonates, have a more pick and mix platter of Discipline powers, but those powers are frequently weaker and they're still limited to only five powers per Discipline. <br /> <br /> Since XP awards are significantly lower in V5 (despite cheaper XP costs overall), it'll also take elders longer to acquire that suite of powers.<br /> <br /> Many V20 elders can get Disciplines at 6+, which gives them way more versatility in general, since most of these powers are broader than those in V5. <br /> <br /> True, some of these elder level powers were nerfed and are offered as lower level V5 powers, but they generally replace the more versatile V20 powers (e.g., Potence adding to every Strength dice pool instead of a collection of one-off feats of Strength). Having five broad powers is better than having five narrower ones, and if you have elders at 7th Generation or lower, those six, seven, eight or even nine powers begin to massively outweigh the five narrower powers.<br /> <br /> Everything else you describe is also offered by V20 in the form of increased blood pool and increased blood per turn spend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In effect it\u2019s not that different from what you see in Requiem\u2019s elders, except with greater unpredictability because of how the dice and hunger system works, so that it\u2019s possible for a Masquerade elder to use disciplines and heal and add to attributes nonstop without ever running out of power during the scene). They\u2019re operating on the same scale as neonates but are generally much better at everything. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is true. But conversely, that same randomisation means said elder could hit Hunger 5 much quicker than a V20 elder runs out of blood points. So it depends if you want more variability in outcomes on this particular element.<br /> <br /> The benefit here is that neonates do always have a chance to luck out, which is good. In V20 and earlier, you need to plan ahead a lot more if you want to take out an elder. You need numbers and every single advantage you can get, and even then, there's a serious risk you'll die.<br /> <br /> But you can win against an elder. We played through the Diablerie adventures for a laugh one year, and it is possible to slay and diablerise an elder (usually while they're sleeping, though). I also remember doing Nights of Prophecy and Baba Yaga being diablerised by the coterie when one of them frenzied (thereby ignoring wound penalties).<br /> <br /> Partially, this is due to the way VTM has always privileged those who attack rather than those who defend, so if you're lucky with your initiative roll, you can be deadly. When initiative became Dex+Wits+d10 it became more swingy than when it was a straight dice pool roll. V5's initiative may be better for avoiding that.<br /> <br /> So, all in all, there are different strengths and weaknesses, but I still think V20 elders eclipse V5 ones. When one side is rolling a maximum of 10-18 dice before blood buffing (for anything up to 4th Generation), and the other is rolling a maximum of 10 (regardless of Generation), it just seems obvious to me that this isn't an even fight (plus the V20 elders might then add on extra dice from the physical Disciplines too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-09-2021, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:08:11-07:00","id":1451316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451282#post1451282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes a company decides to stick with something for awhile figuring people will start coming around, especially if it's early on. 4th edition D&amp;D lasted for 6 years (2008-2014), most of which it spend being outsold by Pathfinder (which was basically the old 3rd edition).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it was worse than that. 4E attempted a relaunch closer to older editions with Essentials in 2010 and the last product for 4E was released in early 2012 and was a fluff only book (no mechanics at all). The rest of 2012-2014 was spent instead on the D&amp;DNext surveys and playtest documents as they pulled every trick in the book to get older players back by convincing them they were listening to the actual fans this time instead of to some \u201cvision\u201d or \u201ctheories.\u201d<br /> <br /> In the context of VtM, I think there is probably some middle ground between V20 and V5 where the vast majority of players (say 80% with about 10% outliers in either direction) would actually be happy with the result. But that would require the developers to bend on their vision because \u201cplayable Sabbat\u201d is definitely one of points you\u2019d need to hit that level of support for the overall fanbase.<br /> <br /> Also worth pointing out is that one of the key selling points of V20 is that it was largely \u201csetting agnostic\u201d in terms of presenting the base information and mechanics needed to play without tying itself to a specific point in the metaplot. By contrast, V5\u2019s rules, particularly limiting generation to double digits is really tied to the Beckoning/Gehenna War metaplot period (and the Withering metaplot if you wanted to say the express loss of elder disciplines and 6+ stats is a recent development instead of having always been the case).<br /> <br /> The reason I bring this up is that, as D&amp;D has always proven, its a lot easier to sell a more generic mechanical system that metaplot can be easily tacked onto (i.e. 5e\u2019s system isn\u2019t joined at the hip to the current Forgotten Realms metaplot), than to sell a metaplot specific system.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think you could probably even mechanically merge the Chronicles of Darkness into that 80% happy fans crowd by just offering different interpretations of shared mechanics (i.e. Blood Potency to Generation) for that setting and basically have VtR as essentially Dragonlance to VtM\u2019s Forgotten Realms. V5 is already halfway there with its switch to the CoD attributes, Blood Potency, Humanity as sole morality meter (which is also redefined relative to its previous VtM meaning) and fixed difficulty numbers.<br /> <br /> Pull back the surge mechanics to the Blood Points shared by V20 and Requiem and change Humanity to something that instead is essentially a \u201cResist the Beast\u201d stat (where so long as you have personal tenants that oppose the Beast\u2019s influence it doesn\u2019t particularly matter what they are; which enables Sabbat and Dark Ages roads to be easily applied to the core mechanic) and find a level of common ground between the disciplines shared by V20, V5 and Requiem (with version specific disciplines in various splats) and I think it\u2019s something that\u2019s eminently doable.<br /> <br /> A solid shared mechanical core, with mix and match splats for playing various aspects of Masquerade (i.e. here\u2019s how you interpret \u201cBlood Potency\u201d as Generation and the \u201cresist beast\u201d score for a Camarilla game as Humanity and a Sabbat game as Paths), Requiem or a GM\u2019s homebrew urban fantasy setting (ex. take the Sabbat material and create something like the VanHelsing series where a post-apocalyptic world is ruled by inhuman vampires).<br /> <br /> A mix-and-match approach would also work well in expanding out into the other supernatural critters as well. Maybe a GM likes Masquerade, but prefers the Lost Changelings over the Dreaming variety... and a shared mechanical base would allow you to plug VtM + CtL into that GM\u2019s setting easily.<br /> <br /> The degree to which the WoD/CoD has always relied on \u201cfluff\u201d to shape their settings as much or more than mechanics I think would be a major strength to such an approach and taking lessons from how D&amp;D lost and then regained and expanded its share of the fantasy tabletop market and trying to apply those to the World of Darkness seems like a worthwhile endeavor even if the divide between V20, V5 and CoD is not as vast as it was for D&amp;D c. 2012.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:32:13-07:00","id":1451351,"title":"","content":"I agree with you SOOO MUCH. Your core books should be metaplot neutral, and just release metaplot books and rule books. Keep them separate. It makes complete sense from a busniess point of view for a TTRPG Company. Which Wizards is. Paradox is not. They (in my opinion) care FAR more about video games and films. The TTRPOG is prolly at best an after thought to form the basis of those video games and films..and that's prolly about it. That's my guess though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:34:42-07:00","id":1451352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451282#post1451282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as Frederick Wester (the CEO of Paradox) said on day one about the acquisition, \u201cWe\u2019re going to start licensing out the brand again from the beginning. We\u2019ll start with one World of Darkness. We\u2019ll start, basically, from day one to unite the community under one flag.\u201d Further splitting up the fanbase would go against their most basic goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fair to say though, that their goal and their actions aren't lining up. The WoD fanbase (even ignoring the CofD for now) is probably as divided as its ever been; largely driven by decisions at Paradox like making the Sabbat a default antagonist group despite being a playable group for the vast majority of the game's lifespan that has a still present subfandom.<br /> <br /> You can't make a &quot;big tent&quot; edition of the game that's suppose to unify everyone under one flag, and then release a series of books that have fans rejecting the new edition for cutting out their play preferences. Regardless of if you like where V5 is going or not, it's an edition that has a strong vision for what it wants to be, and that vision is contrary to the goal of appealing to as broad a Vampire community as possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T00:59:22-07:00","id":1451420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451316#post1451316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the context of VtM, I think there is probably some middle ground between V20 and V5 where the vast majority of players (say 80% with about 10% outliers in either direction) would actually be happy with the result. But that would require the developers to bend on their vision because \u201cplayable Sabbat\u201d is definitely one of points you\u2019d need to hit that level of support for the overall fanbase.<br /> <br /> Also worth pointing out is that one of the key selling points of V20 is that it was largely \u201csetting agnostic\u201d in terms of presenting the base information and mechanics needed to play without tying itself to a specific point in the metaplot. By contrast, V5\u2019s rules, particularly limiting generation to double digits is really tied to the Beckoning/Gehenna War metaplot period (and the Withering metaplot if you wanted to say the express loss of elder disciplines and 6+ stats is a recent development instead of having always been the case).<br /> <br /> The reason I bring this up is that, as D&amp;D has always proven, its a lot easier to sell a more generic mechanical system that metaplot can be easily tacked onto (i.e. 5e\u2019s system isn\u2019t joined at the hip to the current Forgotten Realms metaplot), than to sell a metaplot specific system.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think you could probably even mechanically merge the Chronicles of Darkness into that 80% happy fans crowd by just offering different interpretations of shared mechanics (i.e. Blood Potency to Generation) for that setting and basically have VtR as essentially Dragonlance to VtM\u2019s Forgotten Realms. V5 is already halfway there with its switch to the CoD attributes, Blood Potency, Humanity as sole morality meter (which is also redefined relative to its previous VtM meaning) and fixed difficulty numbers.<br /> <br /> Pull back the surge mechanics to the Blood Points shared by V20 and Requiem and change Humanity to something that instead is essentially a \u201cResist the Beast\u201d stat (where so long as you have personal tenants that oppose the Beast\u2019s influence it doesn\u2019t particularly matter what they are; which enables Sabbat and Dark Ages roads to be easily applied to the core mechanic) and find a level of common ground between the disciplines shared by V20, V5 and Requiem (with version specific disciplines in various splats) and I think it\u2019s something that\u2019s eminently doable.<br /> <br /> A solid shared mechanical core, with mix and match splats for playing various aspects of Masquerade (i.e. here\u2019s how you interpret \u201cBlood Potency\u201d as Generation and the \u201cresist beast\u201d score for a Camarilla game as Humanity and a Sabbat game as Paths), Requiem or a GM\u2019s homebrew urban fantasy setting (ex. take the Sabbat material and create something like the VanHelsing series where a post-apocalyptic world is ruled by inhuman vampires).<br /> <br /> A mix-and-match approach would also work well in expanding out into the other supernatural critters as well. Maybe a GM likes Masquerade, but prefers the Lost Changelings over the Dreaming variety... and a shared mechanical base would allow you to plug VtM + CtL into that GM\u2019s setting easily.<br /> <br /> The degree to which the WoD/CoD has always relied on \u201cfluff\u201d to shape their settings as much or more than mechanics I think would be a major strength to such an approach and taking lessons from how D&amp;D lost and then regained and expanded its share of the fantasy tabletop market and trying to apply those to the World of Darkness seems like a worthwhile endeavor even if the divide between V20, V5 and CoD is not as vast as it was for D&amp;D c. 2012.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree wholeheartedly. D&amp;D doesn't suffer from having an Eberron setting, so I don't think VTM should suffer from having VTR either. There is definitely a way to bring everyone together. Personally, I'd use the CofD chassis as the basis, make it metaplot agnostic, and find a compromise somewhere between the V20 and V5 versions of the game to make the most people happy.<br /> <br /> For instance, I really love how Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay 4e cribs from all three previous editions of WFRP, and rolls back the setting to a point before 2e (which shook up the setting quite a bit). They've reintroduced things from 1e, when the setting was more fluid and less tied to the wargame, such as Gnomes, that people have really loved, while reconciling that with the world as presented in later editions of the wargame and the TTRPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451352#post1451352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to say though, that their goal and their actions aren't lining up. The WoD fanbase (even ignoring the CofD for now) is probably as divided as its ever been; largely driven by decisions at Paradox like making the Sabbat a default antagonist group despite being a playable group for the vast majority of the game's lifespan that has a still present subfandom.<br /> <br /> You can't make a &amp;quot;big tent&amp;quot; edition of the game that's suppose to unify everyone under one flag, and then release a series of books that have fans rejecting the new edition for cutting out their play preferences. Regardless of if you like where V5 is going or not, it's an edition that has a strong vision for what it wants to be, and that vision is contrary to the goal of appealing to as broad a Vampire community as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. You can't have One World of Darkness if everybody has split off into factions. Nevermind that the One World of Darkness only includes one supernatural type at present, so everyone playing mages, werewolves, fae and wraiths are using the *20 editions anyway.<br /> <br /> All it needs is for a retroclone of Vampire to pop up (let's call this hypothetical game Trenchcoats and Katanas) and you're exactly where D&amp;D4e was when Pathfinder came out. Things splinter further and you risk some players not coming back even if you undo it all in the next edition.<br /> <br /> Similar things have happened in other gamelines too. Using my above example, WFRP3e spawned Zweihander as a reaction to its huge changes to system and the like, and for a long time Zweihander was really popular among WFRP fans. Then WFRP4e came out with a return to what people loved before, and the fans mostly all play that now (though some have still kept with Zweihander).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T02:17:17-07:00","id":1451425,"title":"","content":"I think one thing that's saving Paradox from competition from an external source (like Pathfinder or Zweihander) is that they own their games biggest competitors in V20 and VtR 2e anyway. Even if fans see similarities between V20 vs. V5 and Pathfinder vs. D&amp;D 4e, Paradox might not feel the same pressures as their IP is being bought and played either way.<br /> <br /> And there have been attempts to do a retroclone of the WoD (like, one is literally called Katanas and Trenchcoats which very smartly leans into being 90s retro), but none of those efforts has displaced V20 as the default choice for fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T06:32:16-07:00","id":1451437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451425#post1451425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one thing that's saving Paradox from competition from an external source (like Pathfinder or Zweihander) is that they own their games biggest competitors in V20 and VtR 2e anyway. Even if fans see similarities between V20 vs. V5 and Pathfinder vs. D&amp;D 4e, Paradox might not feel the same pressures as their IP is being bought and played either way.<br /> <br /> And there have been attempts to do a retroclone of the WoD (like, one is literally called Katanas and Trenchcoats which very smartly leans into being 90s retro), but none of those efforts has displaced V20 as the default choice for fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I totally hadn't heard of Katanas and Trenchcoats. That's hilarious. I'm gonna check it out, actually. <br /> <br /> Zweihander had a big enough audience because it pretty much had open development on WFRP forums, so people already knew what it was and in some ways, they could shape it to be their ultimate version of WFRP.<br /> <br /> But yeah, V20 has remained in print (as have all the previous editions), which makes a retroclone less necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T07:01:05-07:00","id":1451438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451437#post1451437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, V20 has remained in print (as have all the previous editions), which makes a retroclone less necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for that time when oWW rounded up all the WoD books that the could get their hands on at the distribution centers and physically destroyed them all to shove CofD down our throats. The previous version weren't in print for along time after that. I may still have the security footage from Alliance for that somewhere.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T07:31:30-07:00","id":1451441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451438#post1451438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for that time when oWW rounded up all the WoD books that the could get their hands on at the distribution centers and physically destroyed them all to shove CofD down our throats. The previous version weren't in print for along time after that. I may still have the security footage from Alliance for that somewhere.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd never heard that. That's... very White Wolf. Remember 'graduate your game'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:51:03-07:00","id":1451475,"title":"","content":"That's... not really accurate.<br /> <br /> Stripping books is a very old practice in the publishing world. Sellers and distributors rip off the covers of books and send them back to the publisher for a refund (serving as proof the book wasn't sold, and saving on shipping by not sending the whole book back) to clear out inventory without taking more of a loss on unsold books. This was happening to WoD books long before the CofD was decided on. Refund rates tend to be higher when there's a new big thing the distributor wants to push (like a new edition, or a brand new line like the CofD), so stripping is worse around those events.<br /> <br /> During the heyday of brick &amp; mortar gaming stores, RPG books tended to be safer from stripping because in gamer culture &quot;old&quot; turns into &quot;collectable&quot; which means small sellers tended to not strip their books for refunds because it was better for them to maintain a back catalog. But the WoD was big enough to get sold in major retailers, which means WoD books were getting stripped all the time, because national chains do not keep old books on shelves that fresh stock could be on instead.<br /> <br /> There's nothing nefarious about this. Pushing for stripping was (and in many parts of the publishing world still is) standard practice to help get people to buy new books instead of old books taking up space. It was bad across the industry at the time because when the RPG bubble burst, small stores were desperate and had to do things they normally might not to try and stay afloat (and most didn't anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T13:23:45-07:00","id":1451481,"title":"","content":"That is really accurate. Were you at Alliance Distribution when this went down?<br /> <br /> This wasn't a return or a strip cover situation. The had us recall all products from stores and had a WW employee on hand to physically guard the books 24 hrs a day until they were satisfied that they had all that they were going to get. Then they burned the whole skid of them so nothing was allowed to survive because they were afraid (probably correctly) employees were going to take home the books instead of them being destroyed completely. The goal was clear force the old games out of existence. In all my years I have never seen another company do anything like this before or after.<br /> <br /> Also thanks for explaining how an industry that I worked in for a over decade works.<br /> <br /> Note this was oWW --not any of the current owners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:45:59-07:00","id":1451493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451481#post1451481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is really accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible to describe a real event without doing so in an accurate fashion in order to make it sound far worse than it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Were you at Alliance Distribution when this went down? </div> </div> </div>I've dealt with them enough to not consider them being involved in burning a skid of books at all shocking or unusual as long as it's good for their bottom line. I'm rather incredulous of any attempt to spin this as not standard practice even if one skid in one warehouse had a WW &quot;guard&quot; on it (and seriously, one skid of every cWoD book they could get recalled? If the point was to cleanse the cWoD from stores one skid means it was pointless).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This wasn't a return or a strip cover situation. </div> </div> </div>While the &quot;guard&quot; is strange... still sounds like a return motivated by new stock once you get to the details. I have zero reason to believe Alliance didn't get every cent from WW that they were entitled to for all those books; they're in business to make money, not burn it, even if they'll gladly burn stock if that helps their bottom line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then they burned the whole skid of them so nothing was allowed to survive because they were afraid (probably correctly) employees were going to take home the books instead of them being destroyed completely. </div> </div> </div>Um... yeah. Burning or pulping is what happens to returned books so people can't try to sell/keep them without giving the companies their cut. Employees walking off with stock marked for destruction is illegal (stupid, but is, because these laws are about protecting profits not books), and has contractual liabilities attached to it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The goal was clear force the old games out of existence. </div> </div> </div>The goal seems pretty clear... push out old stock to make room for new stock. Of course oWW wanted to get old books off the shelves and put shiny new books on the shelves... selling books was how they made money, old books sitting around waiting for a collector to come around doesn't benefit a publisher.<br /> <br /> The idea that one skid of Revised books was going to force the old game out of existence is laughable. The idea that it would help put more new stock on the shelves and get old stock off the shelves is... completely normal business thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In all my years I have never seen another company do anything like this before or after. </div> </div> </div>If you were working at Alliance... probably because you didn't see all the books distributors have had retailers destroy rather than bother to recall them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T13:59:48-07:00","id":1451573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've dealt with them enough to not consider them being involved in burning a skid of books at all shocking or unusual as long as it's good for their bottom line. I'm rather incredulous of any attempt to spin this as not standard practice even if one skid in one warehouse had a WW &quot;guard&quot; on it (and seriously, one skid of every cWoD book they could get recalled? If the point was to cleanse the cWoD from stores one skid means it was pointless). </div> </div> </div>If old White Wolf was around doing the skid burning, wouldn't that mean any recalled books were Revised or 2nd Edition Old World of Darkness books being destroyed in favor of New World of Darkness (ie, CoD 1st edition) games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T14:37:13-07:00","id":1451577,"title":"","content":"To an extent, of course, but it's no different than any 2e books destroyed for Revised books to get on shelves.<br /> <br /> The point I'm making, is that this is standard stuff in traditional publishing. Old books that don't get sold get destroyed to make room for new books. Ascribing more to it than that is hyperbolic. It isn't a sign of &quot;trying to shove things&quot; down people's throats,&quot; or &quot;cleanse the old games from the world.&quot; It's just how companies deal with excess stock, that always goes up a bit if there's a new big release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T21:40:28-07:00","id":1451613,"title":"","content":"It does seem common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://thelatestoutrage.blogspot.com/2009/12/pulping-is-publishing-industrys-dirty.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://thelatestoutrage.blogspot.com/2009/12/pulping-is-publishing-industrys-dirty.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://thelatestoutrage.blogspot.com/2009/12/pulping-is-publishing-industrys-dirty.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://thelatestoutrage.blogspot.com/2009/12/pulping-is-publishing-industrys-dirty.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;In time for the holiday season, while you're perusing best-of-lists to find that perfect book gift for a loved one, here's something the publishing industry doesn't want you to know. By shipping books to retailers on consignment terms, then requiring the return or destruction of unsold merchandise, the publishing industry operates unlike all other manufacturers. An estimated 30 TO 40 PERCENT of books are returned by bookstores annually. Between 65 and 95 percent of returned books are pulped - destroyed by publishers.&quot;<br /> <br /> This would have been around the RPG crash, as well, 2003, 2004. &quot;In 2003 Wizards of the Coast released version 3.5 of their Dungeons &amp; Dragons (and thus d20) system. It was a large enough change that many consumers panicked, figuring that their old 3.0 material was no longer good, and thus they stopped buying 3.0 d20 books, including books just published by licensees not ready for the change. This caused a cascade effect, and probably contributed to the downfall of companies like Wizard's Attic, who in turn took more gaming companies with them when they went down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T00:38:24-07:00","id":1451618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451613#post1451613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem common.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://thelatestoutrage.blogspot.com/2009/12/pulping-is-publishing-industrys-dirty.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://thelatestoutrage.blogspot.com...rys-dirty.html</a><br /> <br /> &quot;In time for the holiday season, while you're perusing best-of-lists to find that perfect book gift for a loved one, here's something the publishing industry doesn't want you to know. By shipping books to retailers on consignment terms, then requiring the return or destruction of unsold merchandise, the publishing industry operates unlike all other manufacturers. An estimated 30 TO 40 PERCENT of books are returned by bookstores annually. Between 65 and 95 percent of returned books are pulped - destroyed by publishers.&quot;<br /> <br /> This would have been around the RPG crash, as well, 2003, 2004. &quot;In 2003 Wizards of the Coast released version 3.5 of their Dungeons &amp; Dragons (and thus d20) system. It was a large enough change that many consumers panicked, figuring that their old 3.0 material was no longer good, and thus they stopped buying 3.0 d20 books, including books just published by licensees not ready for the change. This caused a cascade effect, and probably contributed to the downfall of companies like Wizard's Attic, who in turn took more gaming companies with them when they went down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's absolutely common to destroy unsold books. I work in publishing and can confirm this happens all the time with big publishers, since they often have print runs of at least 10-20,000 copies a pop to keep unit prices low. That leads to lots of waste.<br /> <br /> Most indie and small presses print much fewer copies (e.g., 100-1,000 at a time) so there's much less waste. But that means unit prices are higher. POD is even more expensive, as you can tell from DTRPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-12-2021, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T03:47:24-07:00","id":1451627,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">It goes without saying that comparing a poster to a Holocaust denier is beyond the pale on these forums. As such, a week long ban is being imposed on Gubenyochi.<br /> <br /> It is also something that will get your posts deleted.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:42:47-07:00","id":1451691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451481#post1451481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is really accurate. Were you at Alliance Distribution when this went down?<br /> <br /> This wasn't a return or a strip cover situation. The had us recall all products from stores and had a WW employee on hand to physically guard the books 24 hrs a day until they were satisfied that they had all that they were going to get. Then they burned the whole skid of them so nothing was allowed to survive because they were afraid (probably correctly) employees were going to take home the books instead of them being destroyed completely. The goal was clear force the old games out of existence. In all my years I have never seen another company do anything like this before or after.<br /> <br /> Also thanks for explaining how an industry that I worked in for a over decade works.<br /> <br /> Note this was oWW --not any of the current owners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you are actually referring to here. Neither myself, the two ex-CEOs of White Wolf, nor our chief sales guy who worked with Alliance have any memory of anything like this happening or being ordered to happen by our company. I just asked them. If you do have vids from Alliance security, like you mentioned earlier, I would love to see them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T06:08:15-07:00","id":1451983,"title":"","content":"A preview is available to download from the World of Darkness website. As with the V5 companion, you need an account to access it. It includes: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>An overview of the Sabbat's cause in the Gehenna War.</li> <li>A page about the Path of Caine.</li> <li>A paragraph about a necronomist who gather ghosts who have grudge against kindred in targeted cities, with abbreviated stats.</li> <li>A Protean amalgam that uses Blood Sorcery to absorb surrounding bodies and gore into one's own body, serving as a way to clean up after small massacres without ghouls or a lot of work and products.</li> <li>Credits (I don't know if those have been published elsewhere).</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T06:35:40-07:00","id":1451984,"title":"","content":"It appears more like a teaser than a preview, in my eyes. I hope that the paths are developped further than a one page spread. As of now, it doesn't give us much more than what was already known. The amalgam is more interesting, in many ways, because it speaks of a more covert action, which is, as we know, not generally the Sabbat way (apart from some top end units in the Manus Nigrum, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T07:07:44-07:00","id":1451990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darthpalpy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451984#post1451984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears more like a teaser than a preview, in my eyes. I hope that the paths are developped further than a one page spread. As of now, it doesn't give us much more than what was already known. The amalgam is more interesting, in many ways, because it speaks of a more covert action, which is, as we know, not generally the Sabbat way (apart from some top end units in the Manus Nigrum, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat do have the Silence of the Blood. They just don't have that other part of the Masquerade, which was pretending to be human or blending in. The way they deal with infractions is to kill or silence all witnesses, and the Grimaldi often have the job doing the dirty work for their masters.<br /> <br /> I like the new amalgam a lot. I'm less keen on the Path of Caine rewrite, since it focuses almost exclusively on Diablerie and power, rather than the scholastic elements of previous editions, and it does a lot of treading on the Path of Blood's toes (the two may have been merged now, I guess).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T10:39:31-07:00","id":1452011,"title":"","content":"What the hell have they done with the Path of Caine?! Where is the scholarship, the exploration, both of history, and the Cainite condition?! The restraint and self control? I mean...what, exactly is this new path of Caine supposed to be? It has no structure, nothing to hold onto, just mindless consumption and rage . Oh and they are still kneecapped by tenets, that horrific imposition of ST power to snuff out all that makes the game interesting, the internal conflict of mind Vs beast, debased by an external imposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-13-2021, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:01:17-07:00","id":1452013,"title":"","content":"So reading the new excerpt, it looks like paths are not lorrsheets but instead are structured sort of like clans. I actually like that. It's also not super clear to me how these are not playable. The revealed path of Caine looks like i could easily just out together a character and play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:02:37-07:00","id":1452014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452011#post1452011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell have they done with the Path of Caine?! Where is the scholarship, the exploration, both of history, and the Cainite condition?! The restraint and self control? I mean...what, exactly is this new path of Caine supposed to be? It has no structure, nothing to hold onto, just mindless consumption and rage .</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to be the way i read it. It literally hss blood sorcery as their main discipline. It's just relentless pursuit of their goals. That hardly needs to be mindless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:20:15-07:00","id":1452020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452014#post1452014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't seem to be the way i read it. It literally hss blood sorcery as their main discipline. It's just relentless pursuit of their goals. That hardly needs to be mindless.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have to drink all blood they can, that's completely new, and the other two are diablerie. Also the flavor text has them as near frenzied shock troopers 'often over extended' when not in direct battle...what the actual? Where is 'if possible leave the children of Seth alone'? Where is 'learn as much as you can about vampiric history?' or 'restrain yourself and never give into extremes'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-13-2021, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:30:45-07:00","id":1452024,"title":"","content":"For those of us that haven't bothered with an account over there, and we're talking about a free document, any hope for some quotations so we can weigh in a bit more here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T12:52:04-07:00","id":1452037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1451990#post1451990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat do have the Silence of the Blood. They just don't have that other part of the Masquerade, which was pretending to be human or blending in. The way they deal with infractions is to kill or silence all witnesses, and the Grimaldi often have the job doing the dirty work for their masters.<br /> <br /> I like the new amalgam a lot. I'm less keen on the Path of Caine rewrite, since it focuses almost exclusively on Diablerie and power, rather than the scholastic elements of previous editions, and it does a lot of treading on the Path of Blood's toes (the two may have been merged now, I guess).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Sabbat aren't idiots. Not believing in the Masquerade doesn't mean they don't believe in secrecy, it means they don't believe in lying TO THEMSELVES. The masquerade has always had a double meaning, where the vampires pretend to be human both to humans, and to themselves. The Sabbat accept that they are vampires, and attempt to follow a vampire-focused morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:09:37-07:00","id":1452041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452013#post1452013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reading the new excerpt, it looks like paths are not lorrsheets but instead are structured sort of like clans. I actually like that. It's also not super clear to me how these are not playable. The revealed path of Caine looks like i could easily just out together a character and play it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because people keep kind of missing the obvious intent of what they've said.<br /> <br /> Justin said in Twitch 'all the mechanics are there if you want to play PCs' but they've said 'the book is not written for PC play'. That's pretty obvious that 'the mechanics can be used , but(with tweaks I guess, as others have said on Twitter), but there won't be any And Here Is How You Run A Sabbat-focused Game' material in the book.<br /> <br /> The only thing that's unclear is how Paths work as a mechanic, since they said it's not a replacement for Humanity, but they also said it's basically a a 'get out of Stains free' card essentially. Which is weird and, for SPCs, pointless since you don't normally track stains like that for SPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 06-13-2021, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:15:28-07:00","id":1452043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452013#post1452013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reading the new excerpt, it looks like paths are not lorrsheets but instead are structured sort of like clans. I actually like that. It's also not super clear to me how these are not playable. The revealed path of Caine looks like i could easily just out together a character and play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't offer an alternative humanity set up. You could use the &quot;ethics&quot; as chronicle tenets or even convictions depending on how you use touchstones, but diablerie isn't just a matter of stain mitigation, it universally lowers humanity (unless you have &quot;The Joy of Transgression&quot; or a similar merit).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452024#post1452024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those of us that haven't bothered with an account over there, and we're talking about a free document, any hope for some quotations so we can weigh in a bit more here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything in particular? I expect the Noddists to be the contentious topic, so here are the aforementioned Ethics:<ul><li>&quot;Lower one\u2019s generation and concentrate the power of one\u2019s Blood to become closer to Caine and exult in the potency it yields.</li> <li>Partake of all blood, the better to understand the power contained in it and to build wisdom from its nuances.</li> <li>Brook no failure from one\u2019s leaders \u2013 be pre-pared to commit diablerie upon them if their shortcomings hold the pack back.&quot;</li> </ul><br /> A lot of it explains these rules, but the second paragraph says a little about their other ideals:<br /> <br /> &quot;A desired emulation of the First Vampire is what distinguishes this Path from other Sabbat ideology. In the parables of Caine, the Dark Father had mastered the Beast, not to deny it, but in an un-derstanding that his Curse was the eternal conflict between his lower and higher selves. The Beast is a servant, not to be feared, but to be respected and even nourished, for as the Beast grows in might, so grows the strength of the master required to direct it as desired.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:18:56-07:00","id":1452044,"title":"","content":"If there aren't clear rules on how Paths work as a mechanic, then Paths aren't really playable, and the book doesn't have all the mechanics if you want to play a Sabbat PC...<br /> <br /> There's only two mechanically important things that separate the Sabbat from other vampires: their rites and their plethora of Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:35:19-07:00","id":1452047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452043#post1452043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything in particular? I expect the Noddists to be the contentious topic, so here are the aforementioned Ethics:</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow... yeah... that's a giant change. The older write-up's ethics included scholarly matters (studying the history of Caine and the vampire condition), stressed rejecting humanity so you can master your Beast, and focused on diablerizing the unworthy (specifically later to focus on humane vampires).<br /> <br /> The old Noddists were always comfortable with diablerie but never stressed it as a major ethic of the Path to reduce Generation as much as possible.<br /> <br /> The &quot;partake of all blood&quot; thing makes sense in the V5 resonance mechanics, but it drops all the other stuff the Noddists are supposed to study (Blood Potency and V5's take on Disciplines would give them a lot to study beyond sampling different blood resonances).<br /> <br /> The Noddists were never focused on taking down their leaders like that.<br /> <br /> If feels like an ethic from Path of Blood, and an ethic from Path of Power and the Inner Voice replaced having three ethics about the Path of Caine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:58:26-07:00","id":1452055,"title":"","content":"Take the ethics of a path and use them as your humanity chronicle tenet. Convictions could be used to better hone in on the way your character interacts with their path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:25:34-07:00","id":1452066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452055#post1452055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the ethics of a path and use them as your humanity chronicle tenet. Convictions could be used to better hone in on the way your character interacts with their path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't really make sense as a Chronicle Tenet. Sabbat chronicle tenets would be more like, &quot;Do not bring destruction upon the Sabbat. Fight the Infernal wherever you find it. Be loyal to your Pack.&quot; Caine ethics work better as Convictions: for example you were disloyal to your pack, but your Caine conviction reduces your stains because the pack displayed signs of incompetence, so you were better off destroying them and forming a new pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-13-2021, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:26:04-07:00","id":1452067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452055#post1452055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the ethics of a path and use them as your humanity chronicle tenet. Convictions could be used to better hone in on the way your character interacts with their path.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only works if everyone is on the same path. (And even then it doesn't work well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:32:29-07:00","id":1452068,"title":"","content":"We also need an expanded Conviction system for any Path that rejects the trappings of Humanity. Pre-V5 Path of Caine followers can't really have Touchstones (even non-human ones are a stretch for them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:54:40-07:00","id":1452072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452068#post1452068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also need an expanded Conviction system for any Path that rejects the trappings of Humanity. Pre-V5 Path of Caine followers can't really have Touchstones (even non-human ones are a stretch for them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Really, that's the problem with Paths in this system: a character on a Path should really only have Tenets. They should be too obsessed with Path Tenets to have personal Convictions and Touchstones. Yet the Tenet/Conviction system itself breaks down if you do this, since Tenets are supposed to be general rules, and Convictions are supposed to be personal beliefs that allow you to reduce the stains from breaking the general rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T15:12:41-07:00","id":1452078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452066#post1452066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't really make sense as a Chronicle Tenet. Sabbat chronicle tenets would be more like, &quot;Do not bring destruction upon the Sabbat. Fight the Infernal wherever you find it. Be loyal to your Pack.&quot; Caine ethics work better as Convictions: for example you were disloyal to your pack, but your Caine conviction reduces your stains because the pack displayed signs of incompetence, so you were better off destroying them and forming a new pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be appropriate for a more generic Sabbat pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T15:20:18-07:00","id":1452079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452078#post1452078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be appropriate for a more generic Sabbat pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I had barely sent it before realizing the flaw in it: Sabbat should, by rights, only have Tenets, not personal Convictions. Your Path isn't the personal set of Convictions you have that allows you to mitigate the general rules of Humanity. It is something that replaces Humanity entirely. Ergo, Sabbat should have Tenets only, and completely lose access to the Conviction system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T18:12:27-07:00","id":1452098,"title":"","content":"Currently I'm mastering a Sabbat game where I have 2 players on the Path of the Inner Voice, 2 on the Path of the Honorable Accord, 1 on the Path of the Death and Souls and 1 on the Path of Cathari. I doubt I could conceive common tenents that would work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T03:37:19-07:00","id":1452141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452098#post1452098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently I'm mastering a Sabbat game where I have 2 players on the Path of the Inner Voice, 2 on the Path of the Honorable Accord, 1 on the Path of the Death and Souls and 1 on the Path of Cathari. I doubt I could conceive common tenents that would work</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> their isn't. You could do Personal Tenets and Convictions, that would be about the only thing that would approach a Path imho. EDIT: Yea ok, PATH Tenets, so pick the Path, here are your Tenets, then Personal Convictions based on the Characters interpretation of that Path, Touchstones would be observances, like the Power and the Inner Voice meditation rituals, or the Path of Caine Scholarship, Death and the Soul Experiments etc, you have to carry out those actions at a reasonable frequency, or you start to slip from the Path, represented by loosing convictions (Experiments say once or twice a week use most of a night, Meditate for an hour each night, Study for an hour or so, every night or lose a night every week, your choice) Pack and Sect Rites support a conviction each as well to make the 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-14-2021, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T04:55:16-07:00","id":1452146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452141#post1452141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> their isn't. You could do Personal Tenets and Convictions, that would be about the only thing that would approach a Path imho. EDIT: Yea ok, PATH Tenets, so pick the Path, here are your Tenets, then Personal Convictions based on the Characters interpretation of that Path, Touchstones would be observances, like the Power and the Inner Voice meditation rituals, or the Path of Caine Scholarship, Death and the Soul Experiments etc, you have to carry out those actions at a reasonable frequency, or you start to slip from the Path, represented by loosing convictions (Experiments say once or twice a week use most of a night, Meditate for an hour each night, Study for an hour or so, every night or lose a night every week, your choice) Pack and Sect Rites support a conviction each as well to make the 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be an interesting system. I may pinch these ideas for my own table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T10:27:05-07:00","id":1452179,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that V5 will be focusing on single path packs. Even without that though, yeah i think it's easy to just make generic sabbat convictions. I would probably replace touchstones with pack mates. Make it about the internal pack dynamics. It just seems to my that the adjustments to V5 to make sabbat playable seem very slight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T23:01:34-07:00","id":1452280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452179#post1452179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that V5 will be focusing on single path packs. Even without that though, yeah i think it's easy to just make generic sabbat convictions. I would probably replace touchstones with pack mates. Make it about the internal pack dynamics. It just seems to my that the adjustments to V5 to make sabbat playable seem very slight.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's possible, the preview so far makes Paths so much more archetypal and antagonistic than before that people may not want to play them after all. Perhaps that was the intent all along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T01:17:24-07:00","id":1452590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452280#post1452280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it's possible, the preview so far makes Paths so much more archetypal and antagonistic than before that people may not want to play them after all. Perhaps that was the intent all along.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think so, the design seems to be geared to one true way of playing, with no room for other styles, so it's Humanity, Anarchs or Cam, low powered games, rare rolls and that is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T01:42:05-07:00","id":1452594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452590#post1452590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would think so, the design seems to be geared to one true way of playing, with no room for other styles, so it's Humanity, Anarchs or Cam, low powered games, rare rolls and that is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another aspect to this OneTrueWayism: they want everyone to be failed superheroes. They've always said that this isn't a superhero game, and for the longest time I thought that meant you could explore all sorts of variant play. But putting everything they say together and reading between the lines, I've realized something: the one true way they want you to play is that you try incredibly hard to be conventionally heroic, and you fail. You try to be a superhero with fangs, and a combination of hunger and frenzies and the wearying complexities of vampire politics drag you down and make you fail.<br /> <br /> That's it. That's the only way the game is supposed to be played.<br /> <br /> You can't progress on an alien morality and become a Path Paragon. Golconda is a pipedream that even Saulot fell from. You're supposed to try to be a vampire superhero, every single time, and lose, every single time. That's it. That's all. That's the game. That's their completely suffocating vision for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-17-2021, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T03:41:42-07:00","id":1452605,"title":"","content":"I still find it funny that despite all this the combat system is geared for less- serious conflict and the physical disciplines are more... uh... rule of cool/gamified than a serious part of the setting. on one hand you are meant to mope about your frail humanity and in the other hand you're holding a submachinegun while trying to pull off the hallway scene from The Matrix","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-17-2021, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T09:13:05-07:00","id":1452641,"title":"","content":"I suppose there is a bit of one true way ism in the new edition, but that doesn't bother me for a couple of reasons. First, the one true way they picked happens to be the genre i play vampire in anyways, and two, I have trended towards story games in my philosophic bent towards RPGs lately where i want my RPGs to be very thematically tight and focused. I potentially see some space in this for a sabbat game though where you use the inhumane actions of the protagonists to highlight the need for humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T09:43:19-07:00","id":1452647,"title":"","content":"How would that highlight the need for humanity? If anything, It'll show you that you can just throw humanity aside. <br /> <br /> One-true wayism means less stories<br /> Less stories; Less games. <br /> Less games, less sales. <br /> Less sales means fewer people want to play with the IP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T07:47:28-07:00","id":1452895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452641#post1452641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose there is a bit of one true way ism in the new edition, but that doesn't bother me for a couple of reasons. First, the one true way they picked happens to be the genre i play vampire in anyways, and two, I have trended towards story games in my philosophic bent towards RPGs lately where i want my RPGs to be very thematically tight and focused. I potentially see some space in this for a sabbat game though where you use the inhumane actions of the protagonists to highlight the need for humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>What need for Humanity? It's not interesting and not fun, 25 ish years of games taught me that. If you like it, cool, have fun. I don't, it isn't what is interesting about the setting for me. The weird philosophy and esoterica of Paths and Roads have are fascinating, Humanity isn't, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-19-2021, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T08:41:45-07:00","id":1452899,"title":"","content":"I remember someone talking about the devs adding humanity into 1e with the intention to have most players laugh it off. It's something that'll tell you that you're inhumane, but won't actually do anything beyond give you a longer torpor time. Diablerie was only as punishing as murder in pre-revised, so you'd only degenerate into a wight if you were really indulging in sick stuff. It functioned to discourage disturbing evil, but not much more. You could have fun with the mechanic if you seriously wanted to be human again, but for most, you can happily hover at 3-6 and not be worried about it. <br /> <br /> Humanity post revised, well, Diablerie would drag you down, so you paradoxically stopped doing it when your humanity is low, the complete opposite of how the story said it should go. <br /> <br /> V5? All kinds of messed up. Being super humane is impossible, but it does give you an advantage in Diablerie, so say your prayers before you chow down on Mr Clark. I just don't think I can handle how... how do I say this diplomatically... Trying to Force you to care about something is how you get people to reject it. The humanity system is not robust enough to support the undue attention it is given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T10:44:03-07:00","id":1452904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452899#post1452899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember someone talking about the devs adding humanity into 1e with the intention to have most players laugh it off. It's something that'll tell you that you're inhumane, but won't actually do anything beyond give you a longer torpor time. Diablerie was only as punishing as murder in pre-revised, so you'd only degenerate into a wight if you were really indulging in sick stuff. It functioned to discourage disturbing evil, but not much more. You could have fun with the mechanic if you seriously wanted to be human again, but for most, you can happily hover at 3-6 and not be worried about it.<br /> <br /> Humanity post revised, well, Diablerie would drag you down, so you paradoxically stopped doing it when your humanity is low, the complete opposite of how the story said it should go.<br /> <br /> V5? All kinds of messed up. Being super humane is impossible, but it does give you an advantage in Diablerie, so say your prayers before you chow down on Mr Clark. I just don't think I can handle how... how do I say this diplomatically... Trying to Force you to care about something is how you get people to reject it. The humanity system is not robust enough to support the undue attention it is given.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That doesn't matter to me, it doesn't matter what you can 'get away with' on humanity, it's that humanity is what you are using to hold onto your will, and...I really don't care about that, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T07:33:11-07:00","id":1452954,"title":"","content":"Humanity is basically just a thematic rail guard for games. I don't mind it as such but i would much prefer to see it replaced with something similar to the corruption mechanic in urban shadows. Bad actions result in corruption which gives access to darker powered but moves your character closer to unplayability. That reinforces the mood of humanity versus the beast but also makes the spiral more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:29:39-07:00","id":1452966,"title":"","content":"Paragon/Renegade powers or whatever run contrary to the WoD's approach of -You can learn everything with enough XP/ You're not learning new things but unlocking potential. &quot;I want Power, So I'll do bad things to get it&quot; works well, but &quot;I want Power, so I'll kill some babies for fun&quot; is just... ehh. You can say some interesting things about society when you sell someone into slavery for personal gain, but you just look silly when you're selling people into slavery because once you sell enough you get +1 to charisma. It kinda works with infernalism, but infernalism also works because it's optional and in the corner, not thrown at you and made mandatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-20-2021, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T21:39:54-07:00","id":1453012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449578-pre-orders-open-for-the-sabbat-book?p=1452966#post1452966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paragon/Renegade powers or whatever run contrary to the WoD's approach of -You can learn everything with enough XP/ You're not learning new things but unlocking potential. &quot;I want Power, So I'll do bad things to get it&quot; works well, but &quot;I want Power, so I'll kill some babies for fun&quot; is just... ehh. You can say some interesting things about society when you sell someone into slavery for personal gain, but you just look silly when you're selling people into slavery because once you sell enough you get +1 to charisma. It kinda works with infernalism, but infernalism also works because it's optional and in the corner, not thrown at you and made mandatory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Congratulations! You have sold <b>500</b> people into slavery! You have unlocked the<b> Horrific Slaver</b> Title! You gain <b>+1</b> to your <b>Charisma</b> while you have this Title equipped!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}